nd they're attacking you for doing that. Talk about dark, that is truly demonic. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Stephen Miller, former senior adviser to President Trump, founder America First Legal. Also with me is Mollie Hemingway, The Federalist editor-in-chief and Fox News contributor.\par \par \uc2 Mollie, now what's worse? Pretending that the left hasn't been engaging in their own political violence, or for years of pretending that January 6 is really something that's defining the Republican Party at this moment?\par \par \uc2 MOLLIE HEMINGWAY, EDITOR-IN-CHIEF, THE FEDERALIST: I mean, to some extent, they're the same thing. We know the left has engaged in political violence for decades, and it has not been condemned, unfortunately, by Democrat politicians.\par \par \uc2 You remember, in the summer of 2020, that people all the way up to and including \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  were encouraging riots, where the people were attacking the White House, federal courthouses, people's businesses, police precincts. This was - and this was coordinated and this was nationwide, and you didn't hear much pushback.\par \par \uc2 I think conservatives and Republicans have been pretty consistent in condemning political violence. And the aberration, as you point out, of one day of rioting versus this ongoing campaign of threatening people and intimidating them. I mean, it's --there's not really a comparison here.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Stephen, this is serious. I mean, looking at these clinics, these are amazing women and some members - mostly women, it's mostly a volunteer effort just to help these young women who feel like they have no choice, either get an abortion or their life is over.\par \par \uc2 To do that to them, at this moment, I found that particularly chilling dark. I keep saying the word demonic, because that's the thing that, to me, captures at the most.\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER, "AMERICA FIRST LEGAL" FOUNDER: Well, the DOJ, unfortunately, is a deeply corrupt organization. They should be putting all their resources into protecting these crisis clinics, these pregnancy counseling clinics, to protect these women and to protect those that they're serving.\par \par \uc2 They should also be in our cities in Chicago, in Detroit, in New York, in Los Angeles, breaking up these criminal street gangs, that are dealing drugs, that are using illegal weapons, that are laundering money and putting them behind bars for decades.\par \par \uc2 But instead, all they want to do is drill Republicans. So you can all sleep safely at night, because they got leg irons on Peter Navarro or you have real criminals running amok spilling innocent blood all across this country.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Mollie, a DHS bulletin is warning of a heightened threat environment in the months ahead. The bulletin listed potential targets to include public gatherings, faith-based institutions, schools, racial and religious minorities, government facilities, personnel U.S. critical infrastructure, media. I mean, it seems like everything's on the list.\par \par \uc2 It almost seems like, they don't want anyone to leave their homes before the midterm elections. I'm sorry, but I mean, the list is pretty much everything.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: Or maybe they have a sense that the left will again do another campaign of violence, like we saw in 2020, leading up to the election. But I think it's so true that we - the biggest crisis facing this country is that we do not have a serious department of justice, or a serious department of homeland security that treats people the same regardless of their political positions.\par \par \uc2 These agencies have been going after their political opponents, while protecting their political allies. I mean, the - you list all these things are happening with pro-life pregnancy centers, pro-life groups, churches, dozens of attacks, including three fire bombings that we've heard about