rriving on campus with a rifle. Law enforcement have identified him as an 18-year-old male, a local named Salvador Ramos. We are told that he had a domestic dispute before going to the school, shot his grandmother, then drove to the school, abandoned his car and as you see in the video went inside and started shooting children and teachers indiscriminately.\par \par \uc2 You take a look at this video here of children evacuating the school. Robb Elementary School services second grade, third grade and fourth grade. So, these children who were attacked tonight are mostly seven year olds, eight year olds, nine year olds, some 10 year olds. Absolutely horrific to think about. We want to highlight one of the little girls who are missing tonight. If we can pull up this photo.\par \par \uc2 A father came to us, very emotional this evening. His 10-year-old daughter is missing tonight. She is a student here at Robb Elementary. Her name is Annabelle Guadalupe Rodriguez. He has not had contact with her since the shooting. He is fearing the worst, hoping for the best, so many other parents in the same position tonight wondering if their children are OK. Take a listen to what that father had to say to us earlier.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I was working and I got info, my daughter was at school where they were shooting. And I'll wait for more details and nobody never called me back on detail. And now I've come back in town looking for my daughter and I can't find her now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MELUGIN: And again, Uvalde is just a small city of just about 15,000 or 16,000 people. It's very tight knit here. Everybody knows each other. Just to give you some perspective. The mayor told me a short time ago, two of his staffers just found out, they lost loved ones in this mass shooting just before you came live to us. We were talking with a grandfather off camera who told us that his granddaughter is also missing, another 10 year old inside this school. He has not had any contact with her. And it almost makes you choke up. He was saying that she did not want to go to school today. And they told her no, you have to go and they have not heard from her. They're hoping that she is still alive.\par \par \uc2 One more thing to point out we are told by border patrol sources that an elite Border Patrol agent, a BORTAC agent was actually one of the law enforcement who shot and killed this gunman in the school earlier. We're told that BORTAC agent went rushing into the school while Texas law enforcement were engaged with him in another part of the school. The shooter was barricaded, engaging in a back and forth shootout with Texas law enforcement. That BORTAC agent, that federal Border Patrol agent went in with other officers in what it's called a stalking motion where they went in together and they were able to take down that shooter.\par \par \uc2 I'm told that BORTAC agent was injured in his leg either with a gunshot or with shrapnel. So, Laura unfortunately, the latest update we have is not a good one. 19 deceased children, two deceased teachers tonight, the shooter dead as well. We'll send it back to you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They'll have a father or mother waiting for news on a child they can't find this, the most terrific thing imaginable. Thank you, Bill.\par \par \uc2 So, as we saw tonight and details all-day long, a horrible unspeakable tragedy occurred today in Texas. Every mother, every father, every American with a heart and an ounce of compassion can feel at least a small sliver of the heartache of all of those who died and their families, adults children in Uvalde, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Now, a crazed 18-year-old killer with a firearm went to the school for the sole purpose of killing. And he did and the community, the families they'll never be the same again, never. We're just beginning to learn about the alleged killer who himself was killed by a border patrol agent that Bill 