he nation at a time of tragedy and try to shame the rest of us. Because we know what time it is, we know what's really going on.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Charlie Hurt, Fox News Contributor and Washington Times Opinion Editor and Monica Crowley, former Trump Assistant Treasury Secretary for Public Affairs. Monica and Charlie, a horrific day of news. I mean I just - I felt like throwing up all day long, it's just horrific. I know that community. It is an amazing community of people and families and they're playing soccer or baseball on the weekends, just like so many communities across this country.\par \par \uc2 Charlie, your reaction to what happened, the tragedy? And then sadly, we're going to have to talk about what happened tonight with the attempt to exploit it.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE HURT, WASHINGTON TIMES OPINION EDITOR: No, I think that you and - obviously, Bill Melugin did a very good job of encapsulating how so many of us feel, it's just absolutely, it's unspeakable. And as a parent, you look at these, this - these images, and you think about those children, and it's hard to kind of wrap your brain around it. And obviously, there's a whole lot that we don't know right now. And there's a lot that we need to learn in the coming days and weeks.\par \par \uc2 But I think that it's safe to say that there's not a soul in America today, who wouldn't give everything to prevent this sort of thing from happening again.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Monica, we've had these school shootings before. And it's, you know, there's a lot that goes into this, a lot of personal tragedy and families that are broken, a lot of mental illness. We'll learn more about this shooter as time goes on. But tonight, when we are still finding out that people are missing, the president rushes out. reaction to that.\par \par \uc2 MONICA CROWLEY, FORMER TRUMP TREASURY ASSISTANT SECRETARY: Yes, the murder of children is a singular evil. And what we saw today is just beyond comprehension. One o