onal loss.\par \par \uc2 CROWLEY: Yes. I mean--\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Is there anything more selfish than that? I think it's the epitome of selfishness. And it's why people hate politics.\par \par \uc2 CROWLEY: Yes. And it's one of the reasons why \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's poll numbers are circling the drain. It's his policies that are absolutely catastrophic for every American, of course, but it's also the fact that this man does not project any kind of understanding, compassion, sympathy with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . It's all politics all the time, even in this kind of crisis moment, where the president's job is to bring the country together. And look, he went out there with a policy agenda today, we got off an airplane after 17 hours coming back from Asia. So, he was jet lagged. I'm sure they handed him the speech and he said, great, and he just read it by rote.\par \par \uc2 But he actually believes what he conveyed tonight. I mean, and let me just say this, Laura, the propaganda press is going to amplify this. They're already running with this. So, he's got the support of the press on gun control, and the other agenda items that he wants to move forward with. So, he thinks he's got his wingman protecting him on this. And he's not going to get criticized and the press won't. But the American people see through this farce tonight.\par \par \uc2 They're hurting for these parents who have lost their children and other loved ones. And they see their president come out with this kind of callous, crass political statement tonight. No, I expect his poll numbers to drop even further after this.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, yes, in fact, Charlie, I mean, I believe it was today that the White House released its new, much anticipated rules for federal use of force guidelines post George Floyd and the Breonna Taylor deaths. And so, how ironic that their focus is, let's - definitely - make the - make the problem here, the law enforcement in America and that only applies to federa