an exceptionalism.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Monica, first of all, no one thinks a killer is American exceptionalism. So that's an idiotic point. But this is how they view America.\par \par \uc2 CROWLEY: Yes, oh, absolutely. And they will use a tragedy with dead children still lying on the ground as a cudgel to beat up on the United States of America. They do not believe that we're worthy of superpower. And they believe that we're morally inferior. So yes, that argument, you're going to hear this now for days from the Left, and they're going to try to gain the political advantage for the Democrats into the fall. It's not going to work despite the support of the press, but this is who they are. And when they tell you who they are, when they show you who they are, particularly in these kinds of sensitive moments, believe them.\par \par \uc2 Now, if there's always an excuse to erode Americans freedom, freedom of speech, freedom of assembly, your Second Amendment rights, they will always look for an excuse to do that, Charlie, Monica, we're going to probably check back with you later in the show. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Now joining me is Andrew Pollack. Who knows tragedy all too well, of course, his daughter Meadow was killed in the 2018 Parkland shooting, he since spend his time advocating for our schools to be safer, so that children don't have to be vulnerable to these types of crazed killers? He's also the Chief Public Safety Officer of \uc2 Byrna\uc2 , a self-defense company.\par \par \uc2 Andrew, what these parents are going through, and I know your heart is breaking for them tonight, your reaction to what you've heard so far?\par \par \uc2 ANDREW POLLACK, FATHER OF PARKLAND SHOOTING VICTIM: Laura, I'm so angry that I'm practically shaking right now, at what happened, what these parents have to deal with. And just thinking that my daughter was murdered and we put a commission in Florida together to look into all the failures and this 