going to go to Bret Baier, FOX News chief political anchor. Bret, we'll get your thoughts on the primaries first, and then we'll go to their horrific tragedy in Texas. But what are you seeing so far in these primary races? Any surprises?\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Not a ton of surprises, but we'll just bounce around a little bit. The governor's races, first Georgia. It was not even close, with Kemp taking this. In fact, look at these counties. These are all Kemp counties. It's not clear that \uc2 Perdue\uc2  is going to win a single county here.\par \par \uc2 You heard Aishah mention the race in Alabama. It does appear that Ivey is moving forward, but whether she gets over that 50 percent mark, that is a real question.\par \par \uc2 Let's go out here to the House races. You just heard about the House race in Texas, Congressional district 28. This is a big deal. For Cisneros, who is the progressive to be up like this, we've got 77 percent in. Cuellar, a moderate, well-liked in the district, but the progressives went after him. So the Squad, I'm talking AOC, \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  went out there. Cuellar is one of if not the last in the House pro-life Democrat, and he is at risk of possibly losing this particular race.\par \par \uc2 And then as we take a look at the Senate races, it wasn't even close here for \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 . That is the walk. He goes now up against \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , which should be an interesting race, to say the least. You have the update in Pennsylvania, which is fascinating. We are still out roughly just under 1,000 votes with Mehmet Oz leading. And as of tonight, all of the counties are said to be in, and there are some provisional ballots. There are a few military ballots, but it does not appear anywhere close to the number that McCormick would need to overturn that.\par \par \uc2 Now, the recount, 0.5 percent, it's allowed, it's triggered, but McCormick could concede before that. Out of the last six recounts in the state of Pennsylvania, statewide, three were waived off by the opponent, said no, you don't have to do it, three that went forward increased the lead for the first person going in. So it costs about $1.5 million to do the recount. We'll see what happens in Pennsylvania in probably a couple days. Laura?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Bret, the news that, I guess it's not all that surprising, that Texas attorney general's race, NBC News in other outlets, I guess, were also reporting now that \uc2 George P. Bush\uc2 , the first Bush, I guess, to lose statewide office ever in Texas to \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 . Again, the Bush star power is still very strong in Texas, but Paxton was able to hold off that challenge.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yes, and he was endorsed by former President Trump. Paxton kind of won that easily over \uc2 George P. Bush\uc2  who was the land commissioner in Texas.\par \par \uc2 The other surprising one when the other way. It looks like in Georgia the Secretary of State \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  is going to win that contest. Not over yet, but it looks like it's heading that way. And he obviously was targeted for the former president who supported his opponent. So it's a mixed bag tonight, but overall, former president Trump still obviously has a big lead as far as his endorsements and win-losses. Tonight's big loss, though, was obviously Georgia where the incumbent Brian Kemp went on to win.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And the secretary of state loss, that is a big one as well. But I think you're right, on the ledger it goes the other way. All right, Bret, thank you, great to see you tonight.\par \par \uc2 And as Bret just said, in this Pennsylvania race, which we've been covering every night, fewer than 1,000 votes separate Dr. Oz and McCormick. Again, this is a critical state for the Republicans if they want to take back the Senate. So McCormick today took his battle to the state supreme court in what is a last minute bid to try to close this gap.\par \par \uc2 So back with us tonight is Salena Zito, national politics reporter for "The Washington Examiner." Salena, we heard the details, some of them from Bret, but is this too little too late? How is this being seen?\par \par \uc2 SALENA ZITO, "WASHINGTON EXAMINER": Well, this is probably the last-ditch effort, right. This is the -- they filed an extraordinary release application to compel the counties to count the ballots that are signed and time stamped, but not -- the voter didn't write the date on the ballot. And that is what it's whittling down too.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow, the department of state is going to hold a press conference. I suspect at that moment they will address how many up outstanding ballots there actually are out there and if the runoff is going to be triggered. I think that's what we'll find out tomorrow. I think tomorrow we'll have more defining understanding as to where this race stands.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Salena, is this the closest race in Texas (ph) history for a Senate primary? It has to be.\par \par \uc2 ZITO: No, no, no. \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2  and Arlen Specter --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, that's right. That's right. I forget about Arlen Specter. Oh, my gosh, how could I possibly forget about him. All right, Salena, thank you so much. Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 Up next, what we're learning about the gunman who killed 19 young children in a Texas elementary school today. We'll tell you about it when we come back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We're learning more tonight about Salvador Ramos, 18-year-old who officials say killed 19 children and two adults in Uvalde, Texas. FOX's chief breaking news correspondent Trace Gallagher is in our west coast newsroom with all the details. Trace, what do we know?\par \par \uc2 TRACE GALLAGHER, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Laura, Texas Democratic State Senator Roland Gutierrez says the shooter, 18-year-old Salvador Ramos, brought to assault rifles on his 18th birthday, but we should note that we have zero confirmation on what type of weapon or weapons were used. In fact, Texas Governor Gregg Abbott says the shooter used a rifle and a handgun.\par \par \uc2 And for clarity, we should note in Texas you can buy a long gun when you're 18-years-old, but you cannot buy a handgun, at least not from a licensed dealer. You can buy a handgun at 18 from a private citizen in Texas. Investigators and journalists are in the process of scouring the shooter's social media footprint, and we have also pulled up sites that match the name and the description of Salvador Ramos, including posting that show pictures of weapons and messages to young women that appear to indicate he was planning something nefarious. We won't show you the posts because we have not yet confirmed them.\par \par \uc2 FOX's Bill Melugin, who is on the scene in Texas, is reporting that when they shooter went into the school, and here is video showing Ramos doing just that, he was followed by a Border Patrol agent who went in with a police tactical team and shot and killed Salvador Ramos. Apparently Ramos was hiding behind a barrier.\par \par \uc2 And we should note the agent was also injured in the leg, but it's not known if that was by a gunshot or shrapnel. But the agent was able to walk out of the school under his own power.\par \par \uc2 Finally, this now becomes the second deadliest primary school shooting in U.S. history. When \uc2 Adam Lanza\uc2  opened fire at Sandy Hook Elementary School in Newtown, Connecticut, he killed 20 six and seven-year-olds along with six adults, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Trace, thank you.\par \par \uc2 And joining me now is Chris Swecker, a former assistant director of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . Chris, we're hearing drips and grabs about this shooter, who is now dead, pictures reportedly on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  that have been deleted of his weapons and these messages reportedly to women in his life. What is your initial assessment of all this?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS SWECKER, FORMER \uc2 FBI\uc2  ASSISTANT DIRECTOR: Again, Laura, unspeakable cowardly acts. I have grandchildren, one that turned nine today. I can't imagine what these parents are having to deal with, with their hearts ripped out.\par \par \uc2 Like every mass shooter, especially the young ones, this one was flashing red, it appears, which is no surprise. They seem to always communicate threats. They seem to articulate what they're thinking, their state of mind. The people around them can't help but notice that. We don't know whether anybody reported this and whether any law enforcement officer ever had any contact with him over this. But I do school security assessments quite often, and I advocate always for an armed security guard at every school, especially the elementary schools where the little ones can't run, hide, fight. You can do that with the little ones. They don't have the acumen and the wherewithal to do that. So there is a lot to take in here, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: A lot can be done, as Andrew Pollack, who lost his daughter Meadow at the Parkland school shooting, there's a lot that can be done even short of having an armed security officer at the front of every entrance or exit. Whether it's bulletproof glass, whether it's intercom only ring in someone who is previously cleared. There are barriers to entry that can be put up, but they're inconvenient. And it's a wonderful community, Uvalde, it's an incredible place. So they just go by the wayside, that's human nature, until a tragedy occurs.\par \par \uc2 SWECKER: Security is a tough field because you don't get any attention, you don't get any resources unless something bad happens. It's hard to make that case when something catastrophic has not happened. But you're right, one of the most important things you can do is control access, especially after school has started. And in this case, there ought to be one access point, especially for an elementary school, which is fairly small, and a great assessment team inside the school. If someone is flashing red or somebody is exhibiting behaviors, there needs to be a team that gets together and assesses what is going on and gets law enforcement involved.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Chris, I'm actually surprised we don't know more about this shooter yet. With the world that we have and the how fast information flies, that there aren't more people who actually knew him well who have already spoken out. Are you a little bit surprised about that? Is that a loner profile, perhaps?\par \par \uc2 SWECKER: I am, and I sense that a lot is being withheld right now. For example, I think there was a chase involved. The accident tips me off. The fact that he was in some -- he had just shot his grandmother, that the officers were on the scene so quickly. I hear about independent school district officers, they were already there very quickly. I sense that there might have been a chase involved. The father said that, actually, in a quote.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, well, Chris, we are going to stay on this. Thank you very much for joining us tonight.\par \par \uc2 We're going to be right back. We have more details just coming in on this evil, despicable Texas shooting. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: As a nation, we have to ask, when in God's name are we going to stand up to the gun lobby? And the gun manufacturers has been two decades aggressively marketing assault weapons, which make them the most and largest profit. For God's sake, we have to have the courage to stand up to the industry.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Courage to stand up to the gun lobby. I'm looking at them ABC News headline from 2016, this was in December of 2016, "Four years after Sandy Hook, Obama," and Biden, obviously, "leaves a legacy of little progress on gun laws."\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, AWR Hawkins, Second Amendment columnist for "Breitbart" and political analyst for Armed American Radio. All right, AWR, you've seen the reaction, evil -- I don't even have words. I've been sick to my stomach all day. This is the most disgusting, despicable act of cowardice and violence against innocent children. And yet a few hours after the shooting, President Biden comes out and essentially gives a political speech about gun manufacturers and so forth. Your reaction to this tonight?\par \par \uc2 AWR HAWKINS, BREITBART SECOND AMENDMENT COLUMNIST: I'm like you. It's sickening. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  did it before him earlier in the day, and then \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  did it, and then Biden has done it, as you said. Biden started soft, and I thought he might surprise us all. But it wasn't long until he started my God, my God, and he started his attacks. And as you say, then he ends it, basically, by saying we to stand against the firearm industry. The firearm industry did not do this. The firearm industry wasn't there today. An attacker was there, and he picked a soft target.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The conversation moves to assault rifles. Obama and others used the phrase "weapons of war." They did also the same thing after the El Paso shooting. There have been a lot of school shootings. In between 2020 and 2021 there was a record number of school shootings across the country. Something is going on out there. There's something happening to our national psyche or to families or to mental illness. I don't know what it is, but there's something very corrosive happening in our culture. And that we have to get to the bottom of.\par \par \uc2 HAWKINS: I agree with you. I don't think it has anything to do with guns. I think it has a lot to do with the shattered family, the lack of disciplines in the various schools that are sometimes attacked. I think it has to do with a fact that there is no longer any belief that they here and now is not the only thing is here and now, that there is something outside of us that is also important. We live a narcissistic life, and I think we bear the fruit of that, we see fruit born of that with these kinds of attacks.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think, we don't want to talk too much about who this individual is, because that's part of the problem as well. You have individuals who are copycat killers, or who admire the evil handiwork of others. This has been the case throughout history, that one seeks to top the other seeks to top the next. So we certainly don't want to become part of that problem tonight. But the fact of the matter is, there are 19 families of small children who are just beyond heartbroken today, tonight.\par \par \uc2 HAWKINS: Right, and --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And I mean, -- I just can even get the words out.\par \par \uc2 HAWKINS: Yes, I have children, and they were small at one time. And I can't imagine how that would feel. But I think, as I spoke with a friend today, Laura, they were mentioning mental illness and all these possible things. I said never forget evil. Never forget evil. Evil will drive people to do this. Evil people do evil things. And I hate that this evil has befallen the people in that town. I mean it. I hate that it happened to those parents. But the answer to it is not to give away your guns and give up. The answer to it is to love each other, pray for each other, embrace each other, and then when you wake up tomorrow, try to be prepared.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Michael Moore spoke out tonight, the filmmaker, on MSNBC. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL MOORE, FILMMAKER: Who will say on this network or any other network in the next few days it's time to repeal the Second Amendment? You can't say that. Why not? If they had any idea that there would this be this kind of carnage, you have to believe that the founders of this country wouldn't support it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Michael Moore speaking for the founders of America tonight, AWR. I have to say, I respect this much about Michael Moore. He is not hiding what they really want to do. They want the Second Amendment gone, they've always wanted it's gone. And this is a tragedy that they think perhaps will propel that effort.\par \par \uc2 HAWKINS: Right. As you know, Laura, there is a process. If they want to amend the Constitution and get rid of it, have at it. But the problem is, as you and I know, even a poll today that I'm writing on Breitbart, people do not believe more gun control will end mass shootings. People running for office say it will. The people in office who need to stay in office say it will. But when you talk to Americans across the country, gun control is not nearly as popular as somebody like \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  or \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  would tell you it might be.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: AWR, are you one of those that believes that we should have an armed officer at the entrance to each elementary school, or some type of security procedure? Yes, or no?\par \par \uc2 HAWKINS: Yes, but an armed officer with one entry points, that combination is important. One entry point, armed officer, yes, I believe that.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think Andrew Pollack's point tonight that he made earlier, AWR, about we send $54 billion over to Ukraine for humanitarian and military assistance. And we need assistance to protect our young children, sad to say. But maybe that money could be used to actually fortify schools and schools districts that have budgets that are being stretched because of lockdowns and everything else that occurred. But that would be really nice.\par \par \uc2 AWR, we appreciate it. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 And I want to end tonight on what we learned about one of the victims, Robb Elementary school teacher Eva Mireles. According to "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 " she been a teacher for 17 years, and taught fourth-graders at the school. She was shot and killed by the gunman while trying to protect her students. This was according to her aunt Lydia Martinez Delgado. She is in her early 40s. She was married. She had a child of her own. She's an avid hiker. And her aunt described her as the fun of the party.\par \par \uc2 Every victim has a story and a family and a circle of friends that are hurting tonight. America cannot politicize a tragedy while we are still trying to mourn for the victims. But this is why, my friend, so many people tune politics out, but this is at a time where we have to engage, care for each other, love one another. And I hope, pray for America, for our country, for some unity. We need it now more than ever.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for watching. It's America now and forever.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020220525ei5o00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden's Plan To Send Ukraine Limitless Military Aid; Biden's Foreign Policy Designed To Destroy America; Biden's Plan To Start War With China; Biden's Open Border Endangering National Security; Biden Promotes 'America Last' Overseas; Biden Ignores Americans Suffering At Home; The Georgia "Voter Suppression" Lie Crumbles; Georgia Democratic Gubernatorial Candidate \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  Draws Criticism For Her Comments On Living In Georgia; Archbishop Of San Francisco Denies House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  Communion Due To Her Support Of Abortion Rights; Biden Administration Officials Walk Back Comment President Biden Made About Possible U.S. Military Intervention If China Invades Taiwan\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham \par \uc2 7,915 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 May 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: We hope you'll set your DVR, so you never miss an episode. And don't forget, by the way, for the latest news, information, foxnews.com, hannity.com.\par \par \uc2 And in the meantime, let not your hearts be troubled. Laura Ingraham is up next with THE INGRAHAM ANGLE. We thank you for making this show possible. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: I'm Laura Ingraham. This is INGRAHAM ANGLE from Washington tonight. Thanks for joining us.\par \par \uc2 First, Biden's plan to destroy America. That's the focus of tonight's 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 Now, if you wanted to devise a plan for America's foreign policy that work totally at cross purposes, you'd be hard pressed to match what Biden and his team are doing right now. Now, let's go through the steps one by one.\par \par \uc2 Number one, destroy America's energy independence. Like, we all know this. He aims to obliterate our oil and gas industry. Our energy supplies from Louisiana to Pennsylvania to California would power us for about 400 years or so.\par \par \uc2 But the greeniacs pulling Biden's strings want to shut down. And as a result, well, Americans are suffering. High prices for everything, and still they're climbing. And Biden's sappy anecdotes about his childhood, they don't help.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT, UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: We're going through an incredible transition that is taking place. This is bad. The price of gas at the pump is something that I told you heard me say before, it would be a matter of great discussion on my kitchen table when I was kid growing up.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He's still with that tired old line. Now, the transition, come on, I love the meaningless euphemisms by Biden. Day-by-day this anti-fossil fuel obsession is making us weaker. So we've gone from self sufficient to dependent. We're beggars for energy from despots around the world.\par \par \uc2 Now, step two is to make China rich and powerful.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Competition as healthy is good. This is the reason why I've held the view for so many years and continue to hold the view that a rising China is a positive development.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So of course, 11 years later, Biden will reward China for all that good behavior during COVID by lifting Trump's tariffs on Made in China goods that enter the United States. Yes, I wish I were joking.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Are you considering taking down some of those tariffs?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I'm talking with the Secretary we get home. I am considering it. We did not impose any of those tariffs. They were imposed by the last administration, and they're under consideration.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Clearly, this is what they'd like to do, lift the tariffs. And the only reason he's not done it yet is because he's afraid of the voters. And pathetic as it is the GOP leadership, they also want them lifted like yesterday. And our enrichment of the CCP also extends to America's colleges and universities that gladly matriculate more than 300,000 Chinese students every year.\par \par \uc2 Now, when Biden was