 \par \uc2 Now, the nuance is, they have to be postmarked accurately, right? When they come into the election bureau, they have the correct postmarks. And so they came in on Election Day, or by Election Day. However, it's supposed to also have the date on the outside which is supplied by the voter. And that's what the - and that is sort of the quibble between the Oz team and the McCormick team.\par \par \uc2 The McCormick team says, Hey, these ballots should be counted. They got in. They just didn't put the data outside. The Oz team is like, No, this is just like the Democrats. Just don't get involved with courts and voting. And so here's where we are.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, a lot of candidates have gotten involved in courts, right, disputing the election. So - I mean, which is fine. It's with their right, that's our system of laws. I don't have a problem with that.\par \par \uc2 I mean it's a tough argument, because you would say that you don't want any people to be disenfranchised, because we believe everyone has the right to vote. So it's a question of what is disenfranchisement versus following the law as it is on the books? And is that such a minute detail? It doesn't matter. That's for the court to decide.\par \par \uc2 How many ballots are left to be counted in this challenge in all those counties? Do we know?\par \par \uc2 ZITO: We think it's around 5000, but we're not 100 percent sure. That number keeps changing. And we don't know what that - if these new ballots are being counted. How much that adds on to it. And so, that's - we're in the I don't know stage.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Have all the military ballots been counted? I can't believe we're still talking about this election all these days later. Have they all been counted?\par \par \uc2 ZITO: They don't get counted. They're not doing until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Selena, I've been feeling we're going to be having you on for a while. So you don't go anywhere. Selena, it's great to see