elieve this -- if it was -- if this case was not brought in D.C. and I'm sure Durham had to bring the case to D.C., there's no way that Sussmann would not have pled guilty. Sussmann's best case right now is that he can get one or two jurors to hold this up, to let him off scot-free. If not, none of their story adds up.\par \par \uc2 So the good thing that we are learning from this is that for the first time, Durham is actually able to bring direct evidence that Mark and Jim Jordan, some of us, we didn't have some of this direct evidence. We only had circumstantial evidence.\par \par \uc2 But for example, I think one of the things that came out today that's plainest day, testimony, you know, in Washington, D.C. there, you have -- we now know journalists who were meeting directly with the Democrats, taking this horrible story and willing to go and put it out there just to destroy Republicans, destroy President Trump before the election.\par \par \uc2 I think -- so there's a lot coming out in this and I would say, I don't know what's going to happen in the magical kingdom. I'm sure they're grooming people there now to make sure that they get off.\par \par \uc2 But here's going to be the problem: Danchenko trial starts here in a couple months. It's going to be in Virginia, probably a far different jury when they get to Virginia.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, I mean, it's so corrupt. You know, it's funny, I'm honest with my audience where I stand, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 . I'm a member of the press, I do news, I do investigative reporting.\par \par \uc2 I do opinion. I state that up front I am a conservative. We do social issues. I'm like a whole newspaper.\par \par \uc2 But these people claim to be journalists. They're not. They're talk show hosts like me, aren't they?\par \par \uc2 MEADOWS: Well, listen, it's not just talk show host. They have an agenda and we know that Chairman Nunes did a good job at -- of getting to the bottom of it. You were willing to cover it.\par \par \uc2 But here's the interesting thing is, it was journalists that were out there spreading a lot of this false information that they knew was false.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: False and unverifiable. I mean, think about that, and no apology, no correction, no we're going to get better. By the way, Truth Social now on desktop. Congratulations, Devin, tonight. And --\par \par \uc2 NUNES: Thanks a lot. Thanks a lot.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Coming up, BLM's financial records show a pattern of hypocrisy and real corruption. We'll break it all down, Leo 2.0 Terrell, \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2 . They're next, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, BLM co-founder Patrisse Cullors is now admitting that she was shocked at the tens of millions of dollars that flooded into the group following the death of George Floyd, calling it, quote, white guilt money. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PATRISSE CULLORS, BLM CO-FOUNDER: Yes, it was a major shock. It was also a lot of like, oh, wait, this -- I did not see that coming. You know contrary to what, you know, has been reported, much of the funding that came in was from individual donors. And that was a lot of white guilt money.\par \par \uc2 (END AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And that's not all because we are now learning more about the shady financial practices behind the scenes as the BLM group now paid nearly $4 million to the board's secretary, Cullors' brother, and even the father of her child. And that's all in addition to using donor funds to get that lavish $6 million mansion in L.A., in addition to the $1.2 million the group spent to lobby Congress on anti-Trump witch-hunts like impeachment and far-left fantasies like abolishing the DEA.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2 , Leo 2.0 Terrell.\par \par \uc2 Larry, your take?\par \par \uc2 LARRY ELDER\uc2 , HOST OF THE \uc2 LARRY ELDER\uc2  SHOW FOR EPOCH TIMES: You know, Sean, whoever said that compound interest is the greatest force of the universe has never encountered white guilt. Not only is BLM increasingly being exposed as a scam, you pointed out all the money going to family members, also to her mother, it is also premised upon a lie. And the lie is that the police are engaging in systemic racism.\par \par \uc2 And don't go by me. There's a guy that used to work for \uc2 Thomson Reuters\uc2  -- emphasized used to work for him -- he's a data scientist. I interviewed him. The interviews on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , and he did a study.\par \par \uc2 He initially supported BLM. He's a progressive and found out because of this lie causing the police to pull back, causing morale to go down, so the police are undermanned. There are hundreds of so-called excess deaths in cities where these high-profile shootings took place. He compared the same size of city, same demographic of the city and came out with hundreds of people, mostly Black people, who otherwise would be alive if the police were doing their job. But they're not doing it for fear they're going to be accused of systemic racism.\par \par \uc2 So, BLM is also -- it's not just a scam, not just a lie, it's a scam and a lie, Sean and Leo, that is getting people killed. Mostly the very black people that black lives matter purports to care about.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And, you know, Leo, we forget, but the group \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2 , they're the ones that chanted "what do we want, dead cops, when do we want them, now", "pigs in a blanket, fry them like bacon". I'm never going to forget that part.\par \par \uc2 LEO TERRELL, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, I'll tell you, Sean. Let's be very clear. The only black lives that matter, Patrisse Cullors, her baby daddy, her -- and her brother. Those are the only lies they care about.\par \par \uc2 This is not a non-profit organization. This is a political action committee that was going after President Trump. I mean, think about this: there needs to be a congressional investigation, all that money, all that property has to be seized. But what happened was that they have basically used Black people to advantage themselves.\par \par \uc2 Thank God, never -- Larry and I never been a member of \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2 , and never will. But the problem here is the exploitation. And what they said what she said about white guilt, let me be as clear as possible, they shook down corporations. They scared them. They intimidated them, because they were trying to play the race car, all for the benefit of Patrisse Cullors.\par \par \uc2 One final point, she was the only board member of the board, never had a board meeting. It's a sham organization.\par \par \uc2 Republicans, when you take the Congress in November, you have to investigate. I know of a good civil rights attorney, Leo Terrell, who can lead the investigation.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm all for that.\par \par \uc2 You know, I look at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  going to Buffalo early in the week, Larry, and then we look at the numbers every weekend and the shooting in California where you are this week in that Church and I look at every weekend in Chicago, nobody ever talks about it. Nobody talks about violence in other big cities like your city, Los Angeles, or New York.\par \par \uc2 It's so obvious why because they get -- they don't get any political benefit. So if they really cared about the lives, they would be out there every day and they'd fix the problem, wouldn't they?\par \par \uc2 ELDER: Well, it advances their narrative of systemic racism against Black people by the cops. Look at a city like Baltimore where Freddie Gray died in a police van. You're talking about a city where the mayor is Black, number one.\par \par \uc2 And number two, people heading up the police department in Baltimore, Black city council, all Democrat, majority Black. The state attorney who blocked charges against six of the officers, Black, three of the six officers Black, the judge before whom two of the officers tried their case is Black, the U.S. attorney general at the time, \uc2 Loretta Lynch\uc2 , is Black, oh and by the way so is the president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 And we're talking about systemic racism when a bunch of Black people are running the system. It's a joke. And again, it's a joke that is getting people killed.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's not a joke. It's sad. Those are every life matters.\par \par \uc2 By the way, Leo, we have unfinished business with Larry. Where's the Larry 1.0 hat? You were supposed to get him one. Where is it? Larry 1.0.\par \par \uc2 TERRELL: In a mail, coming in the mail.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Larry never changed. You changed.\par \par \uc2 TERRELL: I got the Hannity hat. I got the \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2  hat.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We're going to have it. Next time you're here, we're going to have it, right?\par \par \uc2 TERRELL: Yes, yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Just checking.\par \par \uc2 ELDER: Leo, I applied for \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2 , they rejected my application.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: More HANNITY right after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Unfortunately, that is all the time we have left this evening. As always, thank you for being with us. You make this show possible. Thank you for that.\par \par \uc2 Please set your DVR so you never miss an episode. Always stay with foxnews.com, hannity.com for the latest news and information all you need.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, let not your hearts be troubled. Laura is up next. "THE INGRAHAM ANGLE." Thank you for being with us. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020220519ei5i00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Primary Races In Key States Shows The Initial Pulse Of Voters For Their...\b0\par\par\uc2 Charles Payne, Jesse Watters, Kennedy Montgomery, Geraldo Rivera,  Dana Perino, Tyrus Murdoch \par \uc2 8,164 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 May 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: The Five\par \uc2 FOXFIV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Primary Races In Key States Shows The Initial Pulse Of Voters For Their Candidates; Most Candidates Endorsed By Former President Trump Won In Primaries But Not For Madison Cawthorn In North Carolina Whose Been Rejected By Voters Due To His Own Self-Inflicted Wound; Democrat Primary Candidates Like John Fetterman Doesn't Express Much Interest Of Getting Help From Either Of President Biden And Vice President Harris; Violence Is Reportedly Going To Erupt This Summer As Protesters Are Getting More Upset Over The Possibility Of Overturning Roe v.\par \par \uc2  Wade; The Baby Formula Crisis Is Going Way Worse After Two Young Kids In Tennessee Were Hospitalized Because Their Parents Couldn't Get The Right Food For Them; Democrats And Their Allies In The Media Are Pointing Fingers To Everybody For The Looming Baby Formula Crisis And Completely Shielding President Biden From It; Baby Formula Crisis Takes Dangerous Turn; Disinfo Board Paused After Free Speech Uproar; Free Lunch Chaos: \uc2 Grubhub\uc2  Frustrates Hungry Customers With Promotion\par \par \uc2 CHARLES PAYNE, FOX BUSINESS HOST: All right, folks. That will do it for us. Of course, make sure you catch me on Making Money Fox Business 2 p.m. Now listen, this market is in serious, serious trouble right now. Take a peek of what we're going to do tomorrow. I've got you covered. In the meantime, here comes THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS HOST: Hello, everybody. I'm Jesse Watters along with Kennedy, Geraldo, Dana, and Tyrus. It's 5 o'clock in New York City, and this is THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 Epic primary battles unfolding across America, setting the stage for what sure to be a blockbuster midterm election. It's still down to the wire in Pennsylvania where \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2  and Trump backed Dr. Mehmet Oz are neck and neck, and only separated by just a few thousand votes. But both candidates are confident of victory.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MEHMET OZ (R), PENNSYLVANIA SENATE CANDIDATE: When all the votes are tallied those tallied, I am confident that we will win.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 OZ: We are making a ferocious charge. But when is this close, what else would you expect? Everything about this campaign has been tight.\par \par \uc2 DAVE MCCORMICK (R), PENNSYLVANIA SENATE CANDIDATE: We fought it on the ground. We knew --\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 MCCORMICK: -- we knew it was working. We knew our message.\par \par \uc2 We can see the path ahead. We can see victory ahead.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And it was a big night for other Trump backed candidates who won in there in Pennsylvania, in North Carolina, which is a historic contrast to President Biden. Democratic candidates like John Fetterman and Tim Ryan have kept their distance from the big guy. And Kellyanne Conway knows why.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KELLYANNE CONWAY, FORMER COUNSELOR TO PRESIDENT TRUMP: This is really the reflection of what's going on with the two political parties and their heads right now. So, everybody wants \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's endorsement. That does not happen in the Democratic side.\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman, the new Democratic nominee, thank God he's recovered, he does not want \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  went to the state and he was never to be found until the bridge collapse and he showed up in his shorts and sweatshirts. They don't want joe Biden and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaigning with them. And it tells you the tale of the two parties right now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: That comes as Mr. Unity goes negative. And who report claims President Biden is finally going to try to stop working with the GOP and instead go on the attack as he looks to create a contrast between his job performance and ultra MAGA candidates in his words. Dana, what was your reaction to what we saw last night?\par \par \uc2 DANA PERINO, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: I think there's -- well, how much time are you going to give me here?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes, go for it.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: All right. Well, a few things. One, if you look at the Senate race in North Carolina, the Trump backed candidate there, \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2 , ran away with it. I mean, the cat ran away with a spoon. It was caught at like, 8.02 p.m. There was no question that that was going to go in \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2 's way. And McCrory just go away, I mean, it's like by 35 points.\par \par \uc2 Madison Cawthorn losing, that is something that's kind of, you know, this is a young man who maybe he's -- we'll see where he is in five years.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: OK.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: You know, does he take this experience and decide to do something different. One of the things he said is that he decided to hire mostly communications people. He didn't need policy people. Well, if you don't have that, you don't have victories to run on or accomplishments to run and you end up basically running on a messaging and ended up getting viciously attacked. I'm not saying it wasn't meritorious but, so he is no longer there.\par \par \uc2 But I think the Pennsylvania race is something that is just so interesting. One on the Republican side, if I could comment on the Democrats real quick. So, John Fetterman, also the cat ran away with the spoon in that one. he just destroyed \uc2 Conor Lamb\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Conor Lamb\uc2  was the guy who was considered like, you would think he was the perfect candidate. Straight out of central casting for a moderate Democrat in a state like Pennsylvania where he could appeal to the working class and he could also rub elbows with the tech guys that want to build more companies and in Pennsylvania and Pittsburgh and he just could never get any traction. Why?\par \par \uc2 So, John Fetterman, the lieutenant governor he ends up in the hospital. Gets a stroke. This guy, though, absolutely destroyed \uc2 Conor Lamb\uc2 . And so, this tells you where the Democratic Party is going. Fetterman oozes charisma and authenticity. He is an original Bernie bro.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Right.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: He wants Medicare for all and he is going to be tagged as a socialist. But I'm telling you that Republicans should not sleep on him because this race is also going to be really very tight. It's not going to be tight in North Carolina. But Pennsylvania will remain tight.\par \par \uc2 On the Republican side of things, I would say that there's only one candidate, presidential candidate that has one Pennsylvania since 1909 -- 1988. And that was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And he ran a race that was different. It was wild. People are following it. The -- he created this amazing base of support. And any Republican who is not him has to run a near perfect race.\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  today said he believes that whoever wins in Pennsylvania that they feel very strongly that they can win in Pennsylvania. But I will tell you I think that Republicans are just make sure that while they have this fight and they might have a recount. John Fetterman's campaign is already off.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Fetterman. He is about your size, I think, right?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE 'TYRUS' MURDOCH, FOX NEWS POLITICAL COMMENTATOR: He's shorter, but yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Six-nine?\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Shorter.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And he doesn't --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: He's smaller.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: He doesn't like suits.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: No.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: He wears sweats.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: Yes. I like him in the sense that he is different. But looking at what I saw was a fever of just battles from top, like Republicans who had votes going 3D. Which means the numbers when you look at who was showing up to vote, the numbers of Republicans that were coming out to vote, I don't hear if you are Superman running for a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 You should really be afraid because yes, your campaign is getting started early. But the sheer numbers, third place is running strong.\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY MONTGOMERY, FOX BUSINESS HOST: That's true.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: Which means that when all of them come together --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And they have to come together.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: -- and I think they will, I think the Republicans get it. Their - - you know, they know, they've seen what's going on. They want their police forces back. They want respect back. They want to get inflation down. They want to get America back at least in the top five of importance in this country right now.\par \par \uc2 So, we're seeing big numbers. And I'm just looking at how many people are showing up at the ballot and it's a huge difference. I think the only ones who are showing up for the Democrats are the progressives.\par \par \uc2 MONTGOMERY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: Because the moderates are going, you know what? We are kind of better off with the other guys.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: That's a good point. Do you think that the Republicans are going to coalesced around Mehmet or McCormick or whoever it is?\par \par \uc2 MONTGOMERY: I do. Absolutely. And I think that John Fetterman probably doesn't want to go up against Mehmet Oz because not only he is a battle tested in a really tough primary, he's got name recognition. And if you are talking about socialized medicine who better to dissect what the government has done to ruin healthcare in this country than a doctor who has enriched himself in the free market not only in medicine but in entertainment as well.\par \par \uc2 So, he really cares about that issue and I hope he pins John Fetterman down on this because with inflation where it's at and you know, taxes, a tax hike on the horizon, you compound that with Medicare for all, we cannot afford that. The healthcare industry cannot afford that.\par \par \uc2 So yes, I do think it's going to be very tough. I thought the Madison Cawthorn thing was interesting because he had been polling ahead. And I thought that perhaps the former president's endorsement of him last minute might help. But he so far lost only by a couple percentage points.\par \par \uc2 And you're absolutely right. There has to be something there. It has to be substantive. There has to be policy behind the person. We can no longer become attached to people because of their characteristics or their interesting life stories, how they lead and how they flees us (Ph) -- far more important.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Flees us.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Geraldo, looking at the endorsements, does \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  still have that magic touch?\par \par \uc2 GERALDO RIVERA, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: No doubt about it. I think the fact that for my state in Ohio, everybody was, you know, looking for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to endorse him and this very, very (Inaudible). He had a couple of misses here and there. We discuss Cawthorn and some others.\par \par \uc2 But I must say, a couple of quick points. Number one, John Fetterman is enormously charismatic. He does remind me a lot of you, Tyrus. And I believe that he will cross over. It's not just progressives. It's cool. He is a very cool guy. I like him a lot. I endorse if I could endorse Dr. Oz, a long-time friend of mine. Wife Liza, wonderful people. They are great on TV. But more than that, they are very good people.\par \par \uc2 And I was very, very disturbed by how he was slimed by \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2 . \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2  was also a very attractive guy. He's a G.I., a self-made multimillionaire. He is a bronze star. You know, award of a bronze star.\par \par \uc2 But going up with Mehmet Oz, a lot of it was Muslim hate. You know, for family born in, you know, his parents were from Turkey. Oz served in the Turkish army. You know, I really found that extremely distasteful. I felt very bad that he had to endure -- endure those attacks, very unfair attacks.\par \par \uc2 But I want to say one other thing about elections. When I was a kid, election day was a day. One day. You go to vote. You go to vote. Most people went in person to vote, you know, older or disabled people and now I am probably a number among them got absentee ballots, mail-in ballots very rare though as a percentage.\par \par \uc2 But everybody showed up. And that night, you could gather around the TV and you knew who won because the absentee ballots, the military ballots, the provisional ballots, all these ballots were -- like Florida does now after the disaster of the hanging chad, now you get the account. You keep the running tally of the people who vote early. And election day, you do it, not this torture. It makes people lose late in the system. I --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And we get better ratings when they announce it --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 MONTGOMERY: Even when it's in that middle of the night. How exciting is that.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes, stay up. Watching.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: Absolutely not between 11 and 12 p.m. I know at certain --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Right. OK.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: Very upset. Chester Butterfield.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: He is always upset.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: He could be your lifeboat.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: VIP (Inaudible) shallow water.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: All right. Coming up, get ready for a summer of rage. What the far left is planning if they don't get their way at the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: America could be in for a summer of rage. Similar to the protest we saw in 2020. The \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  now bracing for violence ahead of the Supreme Court expected ruling overturning Roe versus Wade. Protesters already showing up outside of justices' homes.\par \par \uc2 And a right to life building in Wisconsin was hit with a Molotov cocktail. A new memo revealing that the agency believes there will be more threats targeting, quote, "justices, members of Congress and others associated with the abortion debate are likely to persist and may increase leading up to and following the issuing of the court's official ruling."\par \par \uc2 The White House pressed on this issue earlier.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: DHS is worried if Roe v. Wade is overturned, there could be violence against the Supreme Court building or Supreme Court justices. Are these threats from pro-abortion activists or anti-abortion activists?\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: So, the president is clear on this question, he believed the right to peacefully protest in this country is fundamental. But he also believes that violence, threats and intimidation have no place in political discourse anywhere.\par \par \uc2 It seems like to us, it is a very one sided on what we call out as intimidation or as violent. So, we want to make sure we are calling out on both sides of what is happening and what we are seeing.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: OK. So that's what she is saying, Tyrus, is that the DHS has obviously, intel and information or something telling them that they need to put up this memo to say that the left is intending to have -- to foment violence if this Roe -- Roe v. Wade decision comes down the way we expect.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: So now they are going to telegraph before they dropped the ball. One thing you see in this administration whether it's Afghanistan, whether we're dealing with dealing getting baby food, it's always the same thing. There's always a plan after the fact. So, this time they are trying to get in front of it.\par \par \uc2 But again, what would curtail this stuff would be adding -- providing more security for justices, which would mean, what? More police officers? More things of that which they fundamentally have gone against and depleted and disrespected.\par \par \uc2 So, this is not going to have the same effect as they did before where you are going to see people on TV going, it's a mostly peaceful protest. Americans are sick of this. Now they are going to see it being standing outside the Supreme Court justices' house and doing these things is only going to inspire more and more Americans to vote right.\par \par \uc2 Because they are going to see this is going down. And you've seen what happened before. You've seen this course, and now the best thing you're telling us is look out, it's coming. But again, where is the plan? What are you doing? National Guard? What are you doing to protect our justices? Nothing you're talking about. It's like they ae going to make a web site of where you can report somebody protesting on somebody's house. That's probably what we're looking for. So, again, it's a bad -- it's a missed point.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: These web sites are very helpful as we've seen, Jesse.\par \par \uc2 MURDOCH: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I don't put a lot of stock in government warnings, whether it is hurricanes or COVID hotspots. They don't have a great track record. But I don't think the left, if they do get violence is going to do anything to tamp down the violence if it happens. And someone like let's say the McCloskey's get outside their house. They'll get indicted for just trying to protect themselves.\par \par \uc2 You know how this play. They are not going to go in the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and infiltrate the radical left wing pro-choice movement and concoct stings like they did against the Gretchen kidnappers. I guess they weren't kidnappers. That was a sole set up.\par \par \uc2 So, it looks like if you are running a Supreme Court justice into hiding, that's a return to normalcy. That is restoring the institution to this country because that's what they said they were going to do. But you are going to see that, because I think it's a very emotional issue, abortion. And a lot of people don't understand it.\par \par \uc2 There are women who are past their prime who can't even get pregnant but you will see them out there, screaming at the top of their lungs almost resorting to violence because it's just, it's a religious tenet to these people. And we have to understand that.\par \par \uc2 I would stay away from these people all summer if you hear about a protest in your city, I wouldn't engage. I'd go to the beach. Even on a social level, if it' not your friend or your family, don't involve yourself with a very, you know, turbulent conversation about it. It's really not worth it.\par \par \uc2 I would give advice to these protesters if this does the way we think it is. There is a Democratic process. You can go, you can petition, you can run for office if you want to. And you know what, if that doesn't work out in your state, you can move states. That's the great part about this republic. You can move states and live a totally different lifestyle if it doesn't work out for you in the state you are living in right now.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Geraldo?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Well, I think that you may be that last person in America that that group will take advice from just to say.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: True.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I believe that Jesse is right in this regard. I think there is a storm coming. I believe that this issue is very central to the identity of tens of millions of women and o