Club for Growth denies the allegation. Seems pretty obvious to me. That's my conclusion.\par \par \uc2 Now, according to Barnette, if she loses the primary, she's not going to support whoever the GOP nominee is, not a good idea. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: If you do not win tomorrow, do you intend to support the Republican nominee, whoever it is?\par \par \uc2 BARNETTE: I have no intentions of supporting globalists. I believe we have ran out of room on this runway for this nation. I believe we have very little rope left to just roll the dice and we'll see how it all works out on the other end.\par \par \uc2 (END AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I cannot even put into words how critically important this race is.\par \par \uc2 As I've said many, many times, it might well decide the balance of power in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  after this midterm. The late great William F. Buckley Jr. once stated: Be for the most conservative or right viable candidate, one that could win.\par \par \uc2 I like Kathy Barnette, I think she has a great life story, but she has not been vetted and she does not seem to meet that criteria at all in any way shape manner or form.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania is a must-hold Senate seat and if you look at real conservatives, one you will hear from next, that will in fact have not only a great chance -- I predict will win the general election if he wins the primary tomorrow, we'll hear from Dr. Oz as we continue straight ahead after the break.\par \par \uc2 Please stay with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. As I said tomorrow, Pennsylvania voters will head to the polls in what is a high stakes primary battle, especially surrounding the Republican nominee for the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  where a new poll shows -- from Emerson, by the way -- shows Dr. Mehmet Oz, who I have endorsed, along with former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with a five-point lead over Kathy Barnette 