hat where we had information sharing with other countries, in some cases, allied countries. And now even in the law, the law that was just passed recently, that was co, if you will, sponsored by Senator Gillibrand and Senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , where it says, now we are enjoined, we must, we have to work with our friends and allies on this topic. It's no longer an option. We have to do it.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So you've just -- you've set -- you've answered your questions. One, the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  has had full awareness of this for 60 years. This was in the 1960s you said. And second, we know for dead certain these are not foreign military aircrafts.\par \par \uc2 ELIZONDO: Yes, I mean, look, Congress is doing the right thing by having these hearings. And I'll tell you something else, I suspect there's going to be more hearings after this. This is just establishing the baseline for Congress.\par \par \uc2 But we know again, about Project Bluebook. We know about some efforts beforehand. And we know about my program AATIP and then after that we had the UAP Task Force. But what about the 47 years in between? What other efforts did the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  have? What did we learn in that time? And is there a way we can get that information now under a single tent so we're not in essence reinventing the wheel? We can compare and contrast information we learned from before as compared to what we're learning now with better and more capable equipment.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: This is inherently significant story, and maybe that's why it's been written off as the province of crazy people. You've persisted though. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Lue Elizondo, thanks so much for that preview.\par \par \uc2 ELIZONDO: Thank you for having me.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Thank you. So abortion enthusiasts are promising a summer of rage and you've already seen people who really can only fairly be described as unhinged, taking to the streets on that subject in favor of this ritual. We will bring you the very latest on what's happening outside your door, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Ever since someone inside the Supreme Court broke centuries of tradition and law by leaking \uc2 Sam Alito\uc2 's draft opinion in which he argued for overturning Roe v. Wade, abortion enthusiast have harassed Supreme Court Justices and their families at home. They've attacked police officers in LA, they firebombed a pro-life group in Wisconsin. On Sunday, Planned Parenthood held a quote, "Pro-abortion Protest" at the Arizona State Capitol. Remember safe, legal, and rare? No. Not anymore. They're just for it now and they're saying it.\par \par \uc2 The journalist, Drew Hernandez attended that protest and shot some pretty shocking footage of the people who were there. Here is a sample.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (PROTESTERS chanting "Keep your laws out of [bleep].")\par \par \uc2 (PROTESTERS shouting "Eat [bleep]. Eat [bleep].")\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Coat hanger dodger, coat hanger dodger.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I don't even know what that means.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: That means your mom stuck a coat hanger up her hooey and tried to get rid of you, but she failed.\par \par \uc2 (PROTESTERS chanting "Roe v. Wade.")\par \par \uc2 (PROTESTERS chanting "Roe v. Wade.") UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Do you guys want to sign up? Do you want to sign up?\par \par \uc2 We are for women's rights, would you like to sign up?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: You've killed, you've killed. You've killed no matter what. Every month, when you have a menstrual cycle, you're killing.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: That's not a baby.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, it is. It's DNA.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: You don't have to be a religious person to see that there's a spiritual component to all of this.\par \par \uc2 Alison Centofante is a pro-life advocate. She joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Alison, thanks so much for coming on. So, this doesn't -- it seems like we've left the realm of a political debate or even a debate over rights and moved into another realm entirely.\par \par \uc2 ALISON CENTOFANTE, PRO-LIFE ADVOCATE: Yes, what you just played it's so hard to watch right, Tucker, because it's human beings treating human beings the worst. But yet time and time again, pro-life individuals go out, they try and make the case for life. They were willing to take this verbal beating, this verbal harassment because you know someone who suffers more than that pro-life individual out on the streets is the preborn child. That is what we're fighting for in the pro-life movement.\par \par \uc2 Every single child lost to abortion is violated. They are dismembered and poisoned and starved of nutrition. And so that's why these pro-lifers keep going out trying to make the case, keep trying to have the debate. That anger, that vitriol is not going to change anyone's heart or mind.\par \par \uc2 But yet, we on the pro-life movement are still showing up. We're trying to serve them education. I mean, listen, some of the things that were just said, they're not even medically accurate. I mean, these people need a lesson in science and prenatal development, embryology, they're just completely wrong.\par \par \uc2 And I really feel for a lot of these young women, because they've been lied to, Tucker. They've been lied to by Big Media, Big Abortion, Planned Parenthood who tell them these things that are lies. And so I'm really glad you're covering this. And I'm really grateful for a diverse pro-life movement who is continuing to push back on all these lies.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, it's just interesting that we see this in terms of religious faith and I think that there is a component of this that revolves around religious faith. But I mean, you have the Treasury Secretary of the United States say the other day, abortion is essential for the economy, because if women choose to have families, to do the thing that brings people the deepest joy, have their own children, they're detracting from the big companies they should be dutifully slaving away for. Maybe that's the reason that big companies support one side of this debate?\par \par \uc2 CENTOFANTE: Yes, I just saw \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is also saying that they're going to pay for people to go get abortions. Well, isn't that convenient when big corporations pay you to end the life of your child rather than actually supporting women employees.\par \par \uc2 I would love to work together. We would love as the pro-life movement to work together with these pro-abortion, you know, women to say, look, we got to find some common ground here. These employers should not be paying you to kill your child. No man is put in that position in order to succeed here.\par \par \uc2 We need to take care of women and the pro-life movement, you know, listen, if we're going to have this summer of rage, Tucker, then we're going to have a summer of service. As my friend in the pro-life movement, \uc2 Chuck Donovan\uc2  said, we're going to have a summer of support. We're going to continue to support women and moms and create innovative ways to make sure that we are represented, that we are taken care of, that we are not told we have to end the life of our child in order to succeed.\par \par \uc2 And just like you said, I mean, there's something dark about the way that the left is pursuing their arguments right now. It is abortion at all costs, at any point in pregnancy, for any reason, and no one can question that.\par \par \uc2 You know, we at the pro-life movement are willing to have the debate, we're willing to answer hard questions and answer concerns that maybe some of these people have about, you know, life of the mother or ectopic pregnancies. We see lies about miscarriage management going around. We're answering them, but they refuse to have the debate. That looks like desperation, that level of anger is desperation.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, well, to tell people that they're going to get more fulfillment working for some stupid company than from being parents is such a lie, and I think a lot of people are going to turn 50 and realize it's it is a lie and feel really sad. I hope that's not true.\par \par \uc2 Alison, great to see you. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CENTOFANTE: Thanks, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Very much.\par \par \uc2 So whenever you think of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and we're guessing if you're watching this show, you're not like a passionate fan of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ', you've got to give her credit for being the single most inadvertently entertaining person ever to hold public office in this country. The tape proves it. And tonight, we've got an amazing one, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Everybody makes fun of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  because why wouldn't you? It's just too easy, even an old boyfriend, Willie Brown doesn't like \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  anymore.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , one thing you can say for her, she is underrated as a philosophical voice. She could literally do a page a day calendar, a kind of Khalil Gibran for our time.\par \par \uc2 Remember it was \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who once pointed out and we're quoting, "It is time for us to do what we have been doing and that time is every day." In other words, today is the first day of the rest of your life. Children are our future.\par \par \uc2 Now, we didn't think she could get better than that, but we underestimated her, as we so often have. Here she is, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  our page a day calendar Vice President speaking to the State Department telling us about the importance of working together.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2  (D), VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Our world is increasingly more interconnected and interdependent. That is especially true when it comes to the climate crisis, which is why we will work together and continue to work together to address these issues, to tackle these challenges, and to work together as we continue to work operating from the new norms, rules, and agreements that we will convene to work together on, to galvanize global action."\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So if you were to take a truckload of cliches and put them in a blender, that's what you get. Congratulations, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We will see you tomorrow. Have the best night with the ones you love.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document TCARL00020220517ei5g00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; International\par \b \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  Speaks Out; \uc2 Twitter\uc2  Drama; Border Battle; Key Primaries; Biden vs. Bezos?; Buffalo Mass Shooting\b0\par\par\uc2 Kelly O'Grady, Bill Melugin, Connell McShane, Edward Lawrence, Ted  Williams, Alexis McAdams, Charles Payne \par \uc2 9,053 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 May 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Your World w/ Neil Cavuto\par \uc2 CAVU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 CHARLES PAYNE, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: You're looking live at Buffalo, New York.\par \par \uc2 Officials there expected to hold a news conference any moment now, as the investigation continues into the shooting at the Tops supermarket over the weekend that left 10 people dead.\par \par \uc2 Police say the 18-year-old suspect, who is white, planned to continue this shooting rampage in a predominantly black neighborhood.\par \par \uc2 Welcome, everyone. I'm Charles Payne, in for Neil Cavuto.\par \par \uc2 We're going to take you to that news conference as soon as it begins, but first to Alexis McAdams, who's in Buffalo, with the very latest -- Alexis.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS MCADAMS, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Charles, right now, it's an active and ongoing investigation here in Buffalo, New York, waiting to get new information that is supposedly -- supposedly, rather, should have some new information about the gunman and possibly how long he was here in Buffalo casing this area.\par \par \uc2 Investigators telling us he had been inside of that grocery store before and even possibly talked to some of the employees there in the past. As we wait for that new information, there, you can see that crime scene tape is still behind me at that active scene.\par \par \uc2 Also, getting into this, you can see this as new video was shot, Charles, earlier this afternoon. It shows the \uc2 FBI\uc2  here on scene trying to canvass the area. There, they're taking some pictures of the scene and marking several bullet holes that were left in the building where the gunman opened fire in what's been called a racially motivated hate crime.\par \par \uc2 Out of the 13 people shot here in Buffalo, New York, at that supermarket, 11 are black. Investigators now believe the gunman's rampage was not going to end there. They say he was planning to continue shooting people in the neighborhood that he apparently chose because it has the largest 