ess to them, they didn't know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  the way I did, and they all came around eventually like Kathy did.\par \par \uc2 Look, opinions can change. People evolve. That's okay. But there are so many questions, so many controversial statements, so many controversial tweets that Barnette is either unable or unwilling to answer. Like why she initially slated, you know, was slated to speak at a QAnon conspiracy theory event.\par \par \uc2 Why is she backed by the shady swampy? I mean, I am done with the Club for Growth. They're giving her now millions of dollars and I suspect that's because they want the Trump-endorsed candidate to lose and I wonder because they now need to answer these questions. Why they're supporting Kathy Barnette, with all these millions of dollars and all these extreme statements and positions?\par \par \uc2 Club for Growth needs to come on the show and answer those questions. And what about all of the holes in her resume? She said she worked for two major financial firms, but her campaign won't tell us where. She claims that she once served as an adjunct professor of corporate finance, we can't find any evidence of that.\par \par \uc2 She also claims to be an army vet, but when "The Washington Examiner" reached out for proof her campaign refused to provide any documentation. I'm not saying it didn't happen. Why not answer?\par \par \uc2 And when the "Free Beacon" called for a comment on this issue -- well, her campaign manager hung up on them. Today, like yesterday, we also reached out to her campaign on a variety of issues but they refused to answer any of our questions. When we did, somebody on my staff got a hold of her yesterday and asked about these tweets, she basically said she had no memory of these tweets at all whatsoever.\par \par \uc2 Is she claiming that somebody hacked her \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account?\par \par \uc2 Anyway, Kathy Barnette is running for the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  in what has to be described as a purple state