se, Democrats, well, were spending hawks, who weren't there when it came to enforcing our border under Trump.\par \par \uc2 If it means fewer illegals in the United States, they wanted no part of it, and they fought it every step of the way.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PELOSI: We're to going for the $5 billion for the wall. We simply are not.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We're just not willing to acquiesce to a government shutdown and pay a $5 billion ransom note.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHUCK SCHUMER\uc2  (D-NY): They're not getting it for the wall, plain and simple.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: One eight the price of the Ukraine package. And now we're getting no enforcement, of course, at the border. Illegals pouring across and being flown all across America, crowding our schools, spreading illness and disease, working for under market pay.\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Kat Cammack spoke to one of our sources at the border and discovered something that will infuriate you.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. KAT CAMMACK (R-FL): He has been a border patrol agent for 30 years. And he has never seen anything quite like this. He is a grandfather. And he is saying that his own children can't get food - baby formula for his grandkids. But he, as a border patrol agent, just took in pallets, pallets of baby formula for all of the illegals that are crossing into United States.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That alone should win the election for the Republicans in November. Democrats just don't care. No one is convinced by today's staged White House baby formula event either that Biden did. These people are only serious about one thing, getting you used to living with less, lowering Americans expectations.\par \par \uc2 When even the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  is hitting Biden's wishful thinking on inflation, you know it's bad, and it gets worse.\par \par \uc2 The liberal leaning website Vox is reporting that Biden's bipartisan spend (inaudible) the American rescue plan actually caused a three-point jump in inflation. What we predicted, of course.\par \par \uc2 So skyrocketing costs are hammering American families. The Biden brigade has its sights on delivering relief, not to them, but to Ukraine. This is a complete outrage.\par \par \uc2 Here's what's actually in the bill. $4.4 billion to emergency food assistance in Ukraine and around the world. And $900 million goes to assistance for Ukrainian refugees, including English language services. Every single Republican should say no to this, but the old guard is still in charge so they're all on board. No questions asked.\par \par \uc2 In fact, McConnell, God bless him, is leading the charge. He wanted that money fast track by golly. \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  is the only one of a handful of Republicans who are standing up for sanity here.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. RAND PAUL (R-KY): My oath of office is to the national security of the United States of America. We cannot save Ukraine by dooming the U.S. economy. If this gift of Ukraine passes, our total aid to Ukraine will almost equal the entire Military budget of Russia.\par \par \uc2 And it's not as if we have that money lying around, we will have to borrow that money from China to send it to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And while we're on this subject, why is nobody in the Military leadership of the United States been held accountable for the 13 American service members killed during Biden's botched Afghanistan withdrawal, or for all the failures of ours in Iraq?\par \par \uc2 Trillions of dollars spent, thousands of lives lost, and to what end? When is the last time America won a real war outright? And the answer, by the way, is World War II.\par \par \uc2 Writing blank checks to the Pentagon is not going to make America stronger. Accountability will make America stronger. We need to take care of