e Lehman moment since 2008.\par \par \uc2 I got to be careful with this. But, Neil, obviously, the -- it's more than a theoretical possibility, as you know.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Very good point. Very good point.\par \par \uc2 All right, Charlie, thank you for the warning and just sort remembering history and trying to avoid a repeat of it.\par \par \uc2 Charlie Gasparino on that, star of \uc2 FOX Business Network\uc2 , which, you don't get, you should demand. A lot of you already got it, and you know all this. So this is just sort of an update.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, updating you with what's going on, on the border right now and something that could get a hell of a lot worse in a matter of, oh, about a week or so -- after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, you don't have to wait for Title 42 ending to see the surge growing, just as our Bill Melugin had warned some weeks back, back at the border, back at Eagle Pass, Texas, with more.\par \par \uc2 Bill, what's it look like?\par \par \uc2 BILL MELUGIN, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Yes, Neil, good afternoon to you.\par \par \uc2 I can tell you, in just about a 24-hour span or so, we saw three separate massive groups of more than 100 illegal immigrants crossing right here when we're standing in Eagle Pass, the last one being earlier this morning.\par \par \uc2 Take a look at this video we shot, again, right here where we're standing. This was a group of about 150 illegal immigrants who crossed in broad daylight right in front of Border Patrol and the Texas National Guard. Had a chance to talk with some of them, most of them being from Cuba, Venezuela and Colombia.\par \par \uc2 And when the video shifts to our drone up in the air, you will get a really good perspective of just how big this group was. When they initially crossed, there were only two Border Patrol agents on hand here. They had to call more resources in because they were so overwhelmed.\par \par \uc2 And that's what depletes manpower elsewhere along the border. When they have to process these big groups, they have to call agents in from elsewhere. That leaves gaps in security. And that's when those cartels decide to push their drugs through.\par \par \uc2 Another thing we want to show you is, take a look at this piece of video right here. This is a 2-year-old girl who was abandoned here at the river in Eagle Pass. The woman holding her is not that little girl's mom. She said she was told by two smugglers on the other side of the river to take the girl and bring her here to the United States. She did that.\par \par \uc2 That little girl had a note on her that had her name, her mom's name, and her mom's contact information in Dallas, Texas. The local landowner here, she actually called that little girl's mom and spoke to her. She was pretty nonchalant about the whole thing, essentially saying, oh, that's great that she made it across.\par \par \uc2 One other piece of video we want to show you, take a look at this. We shot this yesterday, again, here in Eagle Pass. This was a Haitian family crossing the Rio Grande. They were having some trouble. And you will notice the man in the group was really struggling. He had an infant with him, a newborn infant, a little baby.\par \par \uc2 And at one point, before we started rolling, he went underwater and used his arms to hold the baby above his head in an effort to protect it. Incredibly dangerous.\par \par \uc2 And the last thing we'd like to show you is this wild video, if we can pull this up, out of the Rio Grande Valley. This is the end of a human smuggler pursuit with Texas DPS. The smuggler crashes the vehicle, rolls over. And you will see 11 illegal immigrant -- illegal immigrants bail out on foot. And they go running all over the place.\par \par \uc2 Texas DPS later reports that seven of those illegal immigrants got away, including the human smuggler.\par \par \uc2 And back out here live, the fate of Title 42 might be decided tomorrow. Tomorrow morning, there's a federal court hearing in Louisiana, where a federal judge is expected to potentially decide whether or not he is going to issue a preliminary injunction on whether or not to block the Biden administration from their plans to get rid of Title 42 on May 23.\par \par \uc2 FOX will be in the courtroom. And we will update our viewers accordingly, Neil -- send it back it to you.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Thank you, Bill Melugin. Appreciate it, my friend, very, very much.\par \par \uc2 Let's just say Ohio Senator Rob Portman was very doubtful that the administration or the \uc2 Homeland Security Department\uc2  had any idea what was going to happen to folks once they are captured there.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. ROB PORTMAN (R-OH): Would you like to change your assertion that asylum seekers who do not prevail are promptly removed from the United States?\par \par \uc2 ALEJANDRO MAYORKAS, U.S. SECRETARY OF HOMELAND SECURITY: No, we're doing that to the fullest extent that we can.\par \par \uc2 PORTMAN: Well, you're not doing it to the fullest extent you can. And you know that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: So, where's this going?\par \par \uc2 To Senator Rob Portman.\par \par \uc2 Senator, that wasn't an answer. And I'm sure it didn't ease your angst. What did you think?\par \par \uc2 PORTMAN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 Well, Neil, he went on to say that my numbers were not accurate that they had only deported a small number of people relative to the huge surge. I said 59,000. And then he said it was actually 74,000. He came back and said, actually, your number is right, Senator.\par \par \uc2 So, look, that's about an 80 percent reduction of where they were back in the Obama administration in terms of deportations, and about a 70 percent reduction from where they were in the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 So it's about Title 42 ending. It's about this surge of people coming. But it's also about the fact that, throughout the system, from the border all the way to the interior, we're just not enforcing the law.\par \par \uc2 And, look, all of us, I think, in America, believe in legal immigration. It enriches our country, but we want it to be legal and orderly. And everything that Bill just told us about the border is total chaos. It's not legal. It's not orderly. It's not humanitarian. It's not good for anybody, certainly not for those who lose their lives in this dangerous journey north, and certainly not for the Border Patrol who are trying to deal with this situation, losing operational control of the border.\par \par \uc2 So let's not double the numbers, which is what Title 42's expiration would mean, because about half the people are being turned away by Title 42 now, and make it even worse.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes. And to your point about our open arms in this country, better than a million people are becoming citizens year in and year out in this country, no matter who's president here.\par \par \uc2 PORTMAN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: So this issue is sort of overwrought, to the point of talking about cruelty and all of that.\par \par \uc2 But the numbers are even going up as we speak, Senator, ahead of this Title 42 issue. So maybe it's already out of control, no matter what happens.\par \par \uc2 PORTMAN: Well, it may well be.\par \par \uc2 And it's getting worse and worse, because what the smugglers are doing -- and, Neil, you know this because you have been reporting on it -- is, they go to these families and these countries that -- where there's a lot of poverty and say, hey, that the U.S. border is virtually open now, as of May 23, even more open, because they're not going to turn you back because of a health care issue with COVID.\par \par \uc2 And so people are saying, OK, well, I will give you 10,000 bucks, you get me to the border, and -- because they're being told they're virtually assured of getting into the interior of the country. And you know what? They're not necessarily wrong, because, when you come up to the border and you claim asylum, you're allowed into the country.\par \par \uc2 There's then a backlog of now about 1.6 million people, I believe. And there's a wait of about five, six, seven, eight years before your court case is even heard.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes. OK.\par \par \uc2 PORTMAN: And, by that time, you're in the community, you're in school or in -- at work, and you're having kids. And...\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: You're here.\par \par \uc2 PORTMAN: And then, again, people are not being deported.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: And you're here, and you're not going.\par \par \uc2 All right, Senator, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 PORTMAN: Thank you, Neil.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: I apologize for our truncated time.\par \par \uc2 We will see exactly how this sorts out. This hearing could be crucial, in terms of seeing what happens next. But, right now, the surge continues.\par \par \uc2 And now "The Five."\par \par \uc2 THIS IS A RUSH TRANSCRIPT. THIS COPY MAY NOT BE IN ITS FINAL FORM AND MAY BE UPDATED.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document CAVU000020220512ei5c0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Inflation Hovering Near 40-Year High; Biden Rages During Speech To Union Members; White House Has No Handle On The Formula Shortage\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Piers Morgan, Leo Terrell \par \uc2 7,969 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to HANNITY.\par \par \uc2 And breaking tonight, the new inflation numbers, they are out, and the numbers are a complete disaster for our economy. Even as interest rates rise, the economy is still contracting. Inflation is still hovering at a four-decade high, a whopping 8.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 On a very serious note, this is an extremely dangerous period in our country two-thirds of American live of Americans living paycheck to paycheck. It is killing the poor. It is killing the middle class. It is hurting people on fixed incomes.\par \par \uc2 While incomes go down, the stock market has been plunging that means retirement funds are getting destroyed the cost of everything you buy in every store you go to is continuing to spike.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake: economic devastation is here with no end in sight, sadly. Gas prices, guess what, we hit another record high today. Diesel also another record high. And there may soon be a diesel fuel shortage.\par \par \uc2 Utilities in this country, they're up a whopping 22 percent. Fuel oil is up a whopping 80 percent. Used cars are up anywhere between 22 and 40 percent.\par \par \uc2 New cars are up over 13 percent. And by the way, when you finally find one, the MSRP sticker shock above MSRP is going to be massive.\par \par \uc2 Looking for a plane ticket, that's up 33 percent; meat, 14 percent; eggs, 22 percent; milk, 14 percent. According to economists, Americans will need to fork over, over $5,200 more per household this year because of Biden inflation.\par \par \uc2 And over $2,000, by the way, every American that drives a car, they'll pay an extra $2,000 on gas prices alone. Already, as I said, two thirds of Americans live paycheck to paycheck, according to CNBC.\par \par \uc2 Now, sadly, all of this as we've been telling you could have been prevented. More than a year ago, our economy recovered from COVID lockdowns and got red, red hot, and Biden just continued to pump and spend federal money. Even as inflation started to rise at a very alarming rate, Biden pushed for even more spending.\par \par \uc2 In fact, as we speak, he still wants to pump trillions of more dollars into the economy. This is madness. This is insanity.\par \par \uc2 And that's not all, Biden also restricted oil and gas production, immediately put all these restrictions on the gas and oil industry. He killed the Keystone XL pipeline. By the way, we'd be taking in 900,000 barrels of Canadian oil a day by now. That would lower the price of everything.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, it was Biden that ban drilling on public lands, he closed ANWR because of course he is an adherent to the religious climate alarmist cult that now run his entire party because it's certainly not him.\par \par \uc2 Now, Biden and sat back did nothing as gas prices went up and up and up, except make excuses. A year ago today, Biden, Psaki, Yellen were all telling us gas prices would come down. That inflation was temporary or there were transitory. They were all lying or stupid or thinking about the economy in that, you know, magical way as \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  was reporting.\par \par \uc2 But get this, now as the economy is imploding \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is rip-roaring mad because Americans, they're not giving Joey the credit he thinks he deserves. Oh, we should say thank you for the $5,200 Biden inflation tax, the $2,000 extra year we're going to pay for gas? Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: We inherit an economy on the brink of a great depression, millions of people losing their jobs, losing their homes, but even more importantly, losing hope. Remember those long lines you'd see in a television -- people lining up on all kinds of vehicles just to get a box of food in their trunk. How quickly we forget people were hurting and what did the MAGA crowd want to do? Forget it, forget it.\par \par \uc2 God, this is the United States of America, the idea that people would have to wait in line an hour or hour and a half to get a box of food in their trunk, it's just unbelievable.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, your presidency is unbelievably awful.\par \par \uc2 Now, while Biden is worried about getting the credit he deserves, millions of Americans are now worried about how they're going to feed their children and I mean literally and pay their rent and pay their mortgages.\par \par \uc2 As we speak, a nationwide shortage of baby formula now is causing panic, rightly so, among parents. As one "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 " report reads, quote, a baby formula shortage now leaves desperate parents searching for food. It continues, some parents are now driving hours at a time in search of supplies. Others are watering down formula or rationing it, hoping for an end to the shortage.\par \par \uc2 I talked to a friend of mine. They're trying to import it from Europe, but then of course it gets banned. We're not stopping the opioids and the fentanyl, but we'll stop that baby formula coming in from Europe.\par \par \uc2 This is an urgent crisis. The Biden administration obviously doesn't care. They have no clue what to do.\par \par \uc2 Aboard Air Force One earlier today, Biden's new press secretary actually laughed when a reporter asked about the ongoing shortage. Not sure what's so funny here. I'll let you decide.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Who's running point on the on the formula issue at the White House? You mentioned the White House is involved.\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , INCOMING WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: I mean, I -- at the White House, I don't -- I don't know. I can find out for you and get you a person who's running point. But I don't have a person or name.\par \par \uc2 (END AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm not sure what's so funny but unfortunately it's not only baby formula. We could soon experience a severe shortage nationwide as America's farmers, the people that are the heart and soul of this country, that feed all of us, with the most sophisticated technology, the science involved in farming today -- yeah, they're struggling with all these rising energy costs transportation costs supply chain issues.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, they're looking at three times the increase in the price of fertilizer. That would be necessary. The Biden administration said, maybe you should compost, maybe you should use manure.\par \par \uc2 Okay, they need fertilizer. Look at your screen the four major types of fertilizer are all at record highs. Look at these numbers. You like to eat, I like to eat, I go shopping every week, I have sticker shock every week. But look at these, up by as much as 115 percent.\par \par \uc2 By the way, the farmers got to make a living. They got to raise their prices on everything, so they can keep their farms going. And fear not, because today, Joey actually visited a farm, once again reminded everyone that his home state of Delaware has a lot of farms. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: One of things I want to put to rest everybody looks at me and says, have you ever been on a farm? And I remind them that no -- but nobody knows, I come from the state of Delaware. I represented Delaware for 36 years in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  before I became vice president. Single largest industry in Delaware and the Delmarva of Delaware, Maryland, Virginia Peninsula, that peninsula that goes down is agriculture. It's a $4 billion industry, $4 billion, that whole peninsula. And we have more chickens than there are Americans. More broilers.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Maybe, maybe it's progress he wasn't bragging that his state was a slave state as he once did.\par \par \uc2 Now, of course, Biden has never worked as a farmer. In the past several decades, he hasn't held any real job outside of government and maybe -- just maybe that's a big part of the problem.\par \par \uc2 Here now with more on how we can help America's farmers is the president of the National Black Farmers Association, \uc2 John Boyd\uc2 , Jr.\par \par \uc2 John, welcome aboard. Thanks for being on the program. More importantly, thank you for what you do. You know, I don't think we give farmers enough credit because everything we buy in our grocery stores, you know, come from farmers and ranchers like yourself, and it's not an easy profession.\par \par \uc2 I understand you may disagree with me politically, that's fine. Take me on, on any issue you want.\par \par \uc2 But I want to know the challenges that farmers are facing because not only do you feed this country, you feed the world on top of this country. And we need American farmers to have everything they need to do their great job.\par \par \uc2 JOHN BOYD\uc2 , JR., PRESIDENT OF THE NATIONAL BLACK FARMERS ASSOCIATION: Thanks for having me tonight.\par \par \uc2 Right now, we're in a crisis in America as it relates to farmers. We're facing an all-time high in diesel fuel that -- here in Virginia, I'm paying five dollars and 63 cents a gallon for diesel fuel. We're at an all-time high for fertilizer. I'm paying $900 a ton. People, that's $900 a ton for fertilizer, $25,000 fertilizer bill that we're looking at right now.\par \par \uc2 Now was the time for America to come together and support America's farmers. We just provided relief for Ukraine where -- we're going to be looking at some losses there and the form of wheat and other commodities, but we just provided Ukraine with $40 billion in aid, and nothing in that spending package for America's farmers.\par \par \uc2 I know Chairman Scott was trying to work across some lines and get some things done, but America has to come back together and work together by the same seam that is divided right now. We're divided here in our country on race. We're divided on bitterness and hatred. But, you know, love is always greater than hate.\par \par \uc2 We've got to find a way to work together so that we can get something done and this is for America's farmers.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: John, let me ask you -- this is where maybe we part ways politically. I'm -- and there's no hate in my voice here, there's frustration that I'm feeling. I'm frustrated. I'm frustrated that two- thirds of Americans are living paycheck to paycheck and I believe that's unnecessary. I believe giving up American energy independence was one of the dumbest things this country has ever done, begging OPEC, begging Iran, begging Venezuela, that doesn't make sense to me. Maybe, maybe you agree with that. I don't.\par \par \uc2 Not having fixing the supply chain and making sure that we have the fertilizer for hard-working farmers like you is unconscionable to me. You feed the entire country.\par \par \uc2 BOYD\uc2 : Well, you know farmers are the last on a totem pole as far as getting recognition in this country. You know we may not need a doctor or a lawyer today, but every day, we need an American farmer in this country to help feed this country. And we don't get the recognition that we need and at this particular time, we're not getting the support that we need.\par \par \uc2 You know, as African-American farmers -- National Black Farmers Association, our members are waiting in for $5 billion in federal aid that we didn't get from last year. It's always the weight gain. But the example that I was making that we were able to swiftly provide Ukraine with $50 billion and I'm not against helping that region of the country and the cost of the war and the effects of the world all of those things.\par \par \uc2 But we have to take care of those at home.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you this, I agree with you.\par \par \uc2 BOYD\uc2 : It's America's farmers.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm an America first guy. So you don't have to convince me.\par \par \uc2 Can I ask you what do you farm? How many acres do you farm? Tell me a little bit about what you do every day.\par \par \uc2 BOYD: Well, I'm -- I've been farming for 39 years, and I've raised corn, wheat, soy beans, head of beef cattle and I would like to say that I've urged the administration to move swiftly to provide aid to America's farmers. And what I said at the top of the show, we had a crisis. And when we're in the crisis in America, America always finds a way to rise up over all of the obstacles that's in the front of us.\par \par \uc2 And that's what we're going to have to do right now for America's farmers. If we don't do that, and people -- have you been to the grocery store lately? I'm going to ask that question. Look at the prices in today's grocery shopping.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I go every week.\par \par \uc2 BOYD\uc2 : They're going to continue, they're going to continue to rise if we don't fix the problem. We have to be able to get our crops in the ground right now, and what the president was talking about providing aid for double cropping and federal crop insurance, I farmed from -- been farming for 39 years. If I have the choice between federal crop insurance and buying seed and fertilizer, I'm going to buy seed and fertilizer every time, every time, people.\par \par \uc2 Now is the time to move swiftly and to act precisely to get America's farmers the aid that they need and deserve to plant their crops on time. We have a 30-day window of opportunity to plant our crops this year. And anytime after that, any farmer can tell you, it's a wish and die and a gamble after that, people.\par \par \uc2 So we need the aid. Many of our black farmers right now don't have farm operating loans in place and they didn't get the debt relief that we were supposed to get in -- \uc2 USDA\uc2  is reporting these farmers as delinquents. So they're really struggling getting farm operating money. That's what we need. We as farmers need infrastructure, corporate 500 companies haven't done enough to help America's farmers. Companies like John Deere, they should be cutting interest rates at this time for farmers and Cog Hill and all these companies want to get bigger.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me --\par \par \uc2 BOYD\uc2 : Tell us how they're going to help the American farmer here.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I want to wish you -- first, thank you and your fellow farmers for all the great work you do.\par \par \uc2 BOYD\uc2 : Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And I wish you the best. You feed all of us, you don't get enough credit for what you do. I appreciate you being with us and really shining a light on how bad this is. Thank you, \uc2 John Boyd Jr\uc2 . Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 All right. Now, while the administration does little to solve America's many problems today, the ladies of "The View" -- well, they did their best to run cover for Biden's many failures blaming you-know-who for our economic woes. Of course, when all else fails, Putin, Trump, you know, pick him on any given day.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOY BEHAR, THE VIEW CO-HOST: A Democrats in office, the deficit goes down, the economy flourishes. And then a Republican comes in and destroys it all.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Well --\par \par \uc2 BEHAR: And then the next Democrats to come in and whip it up, and do it.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I can defend the former guy because I won't but I will say until the pandemic, the economy was soaring. We had a record economy --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Well, we had President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . We got the Affordable Care Act. We got stuff done.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Here now with reaction, founder of the Elder for America PAC, \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2 , along with former senior counselor to President Trump, Kellyanne Conway is with us.\par \par \uc2 Well, I don't really go to ABC and Joyless Behar for my news and information, Kellyanne. I think she's got it ass backwards, that's a typical day for her. But there is a reality here and that is this is failing on a spectacular level. It's now impacting almost -- two-thirds of the country, but it's really impacting everybody and I see no even openness to consider getting out of the problems they're causing.\par \par \uc2 KELLYANNE CONWAY, FORMER SENIOR COUNSELOR TO PRESIDENT TRUMP: That's right. No course correction.\par \par \uc2 Look, Sean, this is very simple. Let's just compare the facts, Trump versus Biden. In fact, under Trump, 50-year low unemployment; under Biden 40-year high inflation. Under Trump, higher wages and income -- on record higher wages and income; under Biden, record high gas prices. Under Trump, low poverty rates record. Under Biden, record low approval ratings.\par \par \uc2 I mean, there is no comparison. Look, I think this White House and their enablers in the media are doing them no good by telling America don't believe what you see, believe what we say. And that's not America.\par \par \uc2 Look, there's a cause and effect going on here. Their policies are poor, they have no incentive I think to get out of it other than to insult. Hillary -- Hillary insulted them as deplorable and irredeemable, but Biden's actually injuring them.\par \par \uc2 Folks, this is no laughing matter. It'd be fun to like make fun of the Democrats and bumbling Joe and absent \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , but people are suffering, Sean. Mothers can't get baby formula in the United States of America. Folks are paying more for everyday consumables.\par \par \uc2 Everyday life is less affordable and less secure under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . And people know that you know what I hear from people all the time, they don't just say, we're America, we're resilient, we'll look forward, it will get better we're optimistic and hopeful. They say it was better not that long ago and I want that back.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well said.\par \par \uc2 You know, Larry, I look at the wreckage. I spent a lot of my adult -- early adult years struggling paycheck from paycheck. You know, when I started broadcasting, I worked for free. My first paid job was $19,000 a year. I never thought I'd be successful at it. I still think somebody somewhere made a mistake and God bless me more than I deserve. And I mean that, I'm serious.\par \par \uc2 I know what it's like, but I still have that mindset. And when I fill up my gas tank and I'm paying twice what I paid a little over a year ago, it pisses me off. When I -- when I go shopping every week, yes, I do my own shopping. I don't know why people ask me in the grocery store, why are you here? I'm like, obviously, I like to eat.\par \par \uc2 You know, it's -- that pisses me off. But for other Americans, this is now -- 66 percent of this country is living paycheck to paycheck, Larry, this is really bad and it's getting worse.\par \par \uc2 LARRY ELDER\uc2 , HOST OF THE \uc2 LARRY ELDER\uc2  SHOW FOR EPOCH TIMES: You know, Sean, and the good news is that the scapegoating is not working. Only two percent of Americans believe the economy is, quote, very good, and the overwhelming majority blame \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's policies.\par \par \uc2 A memo to the ladies on "The View" however. \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  presided over the worst economic recovery since 1949, the only time we've ever had a recovery since then, we didn't have at least one year where the GDP was 3 percent.\par \par \uc2 And they're running out of scapegoats. Biden has blamed Putin. He's blamed supply chain. He's blamed greedy farmers, greedy oil companies, greedy meat producers.\par \par \uc2 He's running out of people to blame. The only thing he hasn't blamed so far has been their favorite Republican, and that's \uc2 Abraham Lincoln\uc2 . I think what's next, Sean, is he going to blame -- blame the inflation on racism. They're running out of scapegoats.\par \par \uc2 And the problem is, as Kellyanne Conway pointed out, there's no course correction. They want to spend more. They want to raise taxes and they want to regulate more.\par \par \uc2 They should be cutting regulations, cutting spending, cutting taxes and the economy will turn around. But they're clueless. You said you don't know whether or not it's -- they're lying or they're stupid. I put my money on stupid, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's scary. You know what? There's not going to be at the era of big government is over or the end of the New Green Deal is over, or the adherence to the climate alarmist religious cult is over, sadly.\par \par \uc2 Kellyanne, thank you. And, \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2 , thank you.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, Piers Morgan, he actually interviewed and took on the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  spokesperson in a very contentious interview. We've got the tape. We'll show you the highlights. We'll get Piers' reaction and much more as we continue, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. It's now been 270 days since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  abandoned our fellow Americans behind enemy lines in Afghanistan and surrendered to the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 . That doesn't include thousands of green card holders, that doesn't include, of course, our Afghan allies, many of whom have been murdered and the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  is now in full control, returning their -- right to their hard- line oppressive rule as we predicted sadly, oppressing women, young girls.\par \par \uc2 Now, Piers Morgan grilled a \uc2 Taliban\uc2  spokesperson on his new show, "Piers Morgan Uncensored", about these major human rights violations. Take a look at this..\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIERS MORGAN, HOST: A girl should be entitled to go to school in Afghanistan the same way a boy goes to -- you yourself said in August last year that they had nothing to worry about, nothing to be scared about.\par \par \uc2 SUHAIL SHAHEEN\uc2 , TALIBAN SPOKESMAN: The issue of secondary schools education for girls, they are under consideration.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN: Let me turn if I may to the issue of the now compulsory instruction for all women in Afghanistan to wear a full burqa if they go outside.\par \par \uc2 SHAHEEN: Ninety-nine percent of the women, they are observing hijab voluntary.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: His brand new show, by the way, "Piers Morgan Uncensored", as if there's any other Piers, airs new episodes four times a week at FOXNation.com.\par \par \uc2 All right. So watch very closely this interview with this \uc2 Taliban\uc2  guy. I predicted exactly everything that would happen. It was the worst debacle withdrawal ever. Even \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  says 126, he acknowledges Americans are trapped behind enemy lines, many of my congressional sources tell me that number is much higher.\par \par \uc2 Then we have thousands of people that have American green cards eligible to be in this great country, they were trapped behind enemy lines and our Afghan allies that we promised we never abandoned they're now being taken out in the streets and killed or taken and never to be seen again, never mind the billions of military equipment.\par \par \uc2 So the old \uc2 Taliban\uc2  is the new \uc2 Taliban\uc2 , Piers. This is exactly what anybody with a brain knew would happen.\par \par \uc2 PIERS MORGAN, FOXNATION.COM HOST: Exactly right, Sean, and it's a complete betrayal of Americans that were there and remained there in great danger, a betrayal of all the interpreters and other Afghans who helped the West in their efforts in Afghanistan. But most of all, a terrible betrayal of the Afghani women.\par \par \uc2 And in this interview did with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  official spokesman \uc2 Suhail Shaheen\uc2  was so disingenuous. He just basically told me a bunch of bare- faced lies. You know, and I eventually asked him one simple question, he has two daughters. I said, do they go to school? He's in Doha, yes, he said, they do.\par \par \uc2 And, of course, their -- right there is the hypocrisy which is riddle through the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  ethos. One rule for them and their children, another rule for these poor school girls in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 Just to be completely clear now, any girl after the age of about 12, 13 is not going to school. And he may say, well, they're entitled to, they're not allowed to. They're not going to school. They're having their education stolen from them, after two decades of getting used to having one.\par \par \uc2 And then you have this new draconian rule that Afghan women can't go out -- in fact, they're told to stay at home. If they do go out, they can only reveal their eyes. If there's any breach of that rule, then the male relatives or their male employer who may be held responsible, they are the enforcers. And if they don't enforce it, then they themselves face imprisonment.\par \par \uc2 So you're taking really a step back to the dark medieval ages with this, to the very worst of Taliban 1.0. There is no \uc2 Taliban\uc2  2.0. They are just as bad as they were before and the abandonment of these people I think is going to be on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's conscience now for the rest of his life because it was a catastrophic failure of foreign policy to just up and leave and basically hand the country back to the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  wolves.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, I'm glad you confronted him. I thought you did a really good job with that. What I don't understand is where -- where are women's rights groups? Where are -- where's the gay and lesbian community? Because if you're gay or lesbian, they will murder you. Where are human rights activist in all this?\par \par \uc2 Because they should be agreeing -- we don't agree on everything, but we agree on this. We agree that rights -- our God-given natural rights, from God, not from government, and these fundamental rights do not exist for these groups in Afghanistan and yet, you don't hear a peep out of most people, Piers. Nothing.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN: Nothing, and you know, we hear a lot from big corporations like \uc2 Disney\uc2  when they want a virtue signal down in Florida about sex education to young kids, but not a word from them about the oppression of millions of Afghani women in Afghanistan because, of course, it was a Democrat president that created this fiasco, and that shows a political bias for all these corporations. None of them dare speak out about this kind of thing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me switch gears to the issue of doxxing and the protesting. I call it intimidation and harassment of Supreme Court justices. I would imagine that we might be on other sides as it relates to the issue of abortion. That's not what this is about.\par \par \uc2 It's a big lie that if Roe v. Wade is overturned, that abortion will be illegal in the U.S. It will not be. States will decide what restrictions or what lack of restrictions they want. Liberal states will, I'm sure, allow abortion in some cases, they do now, up until the moment of birth, which to me is infanticide.\par \par \uc2 But the issue -- you call these people that are doxxing these justices and protesting in front of their homes, you go as far as -- you call them domestic terrorists, explain.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN\uc2 : think it is a form of terrorism. You know, I think when you mass protest outside of Supreme Court justices, many of whom have children, young children in some cases, and you are intimidating them. That is a form of terrorism.\par \par \uc2 And I'm all for peaceful protest, Sean. I think it's the fundamental bedrock of any democracy. But to go and find the homes of Supreme Court justices who already I think have extremely difficult jobs, often very dangerous jobs, they're dealing with huge constitutional issues where there are people who feel very emotive about it, very angry about it.\par \par \uc2 We know there are lots of crazy people out there. Do we really want to encourage them to go down to a Supreme Court justice's home and terrorize them and their families? I think it's unconscionable that this is happening. It shouldn't be allowed to happen, and I think -- I would say the same if it was the other way around politically, if these were right- wing protesters doing it to, you know, left-wing judges.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN: I'd say the same thing.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What do you think the media reaction would be? I would never do it.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN: -- they are trying to intimidate people into making a decision which should be completely left to these judges.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Could you imagine for a second if I did anything similar? Which I would never do, it's too dangerous. But imagine what the reaction would be or if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did it, imagine what the reaction will be again.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN: It would be outrage, outrage.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Rightly so, rightly so.\par \par \uc2 Piers Morgan --\par \par \uc2 MORGAN: Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- thank you.\par \par \uc2 Don't forget Piers show "Uncensored" on FOXNation.com.\par \par \uc2 Piers thanks for being with us.\par \par \uc2 And straight ahead, the polls for next Tuesday's Senate primary in Pennsylvania, they're rapidly tightening in a hotly contested three-way race. New developments tonight and some alarming news about the surging Kathy Barnette. We'll tell you all about it, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, tonight, there is a tight three-way battle in the GOP primary for the commonwealth of Pennsylvania that Republican Senate seat that's a must hold seat. Now, the American economy, Biden's failures, the border, abortion are all top of mind issues for voters in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Now, this was originally seen as a two-way race between Trump-endorsed candidate Dr. Mehmet Oz, who I have also endorsed -- we'll always tell you how I feel. That's part of the show. Also, Wall Street hedge fund CEO \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But according to a new FOX News poll, Kathy Barnette is now seeing a rise with Dr. Oz in the lead in this race by two points, two other recent polls have had Dr. Oz in the lead by two to three points.\par \par \uc2 Now, let me be very clear, now, the surging candidacy of Kathy Barnette -- I've interviewed Kathy. I like Kathy. She was very nice when I interviewed her, but the problem is, we're now looking at what is a must hold Republican Senate seat if the Republicans want to ever take the majority in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She up to this point in this race has never been vetted because up until this week, her polling frankly didn't really warrant it. And this is very important.\par \par \uc2 Don't forget, back in 2020, she was in a congressional race in Pennsylvania's fourth congressional district she lost that race that general election race by a whopping 20 points.\par \par \uc2 Also today, when "The Washington Examiner" reached out to her campaign, she declined to respond to very simple straightforward questions about her candidacy. These were questions like where was she an adjunct professor and when was she an adjunct professor? And when did she move from Virginia to Pennsylvania?\par \par \uc2 And that's not all, we did a lot of vetting ourselves. Like -- while Kathy claims to be a MAGA conservative, she has a very troubling history of attacking \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 , the 45th president.\par \par \uc2 During the 2016 primary season, she tweeted -- there's a lot of tweets -- quote: Did you see last the last presidential debate? Trump was horrid, followed up that with Trump is just as liberal as Democratic leaders we currently have in office. Morality matters and Trump does not rank high in it.\par \par \uc2 She also wrote: Trump is good for beer -- for beers and barbecue, not as a president, and claim that Trump's moral character is questionable. And, by the way, she even tweeted this about me. And there's me and says, oh, Glenn Beck -- actually Glenn Beck why does HANNITY support unprincipled \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 And it gets worse. More resurfaced tweets are even more disturbing. One from her \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account in 2016 reads, quote: Don't we get it. Obama is a Muslim. And there are lots of these tweets.\par \par \uc2 From another, 2013, she says: Please pray for my babies and me. We're about to board the plane to California and there's a homosexual female, and linking out to a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post.\par \par \uc2 Moments ago, one of our producers spoke to Kathy Barnette. She claims she cannot recall the context of the tweet about Obama or any of the other controversial quotes and when we asked her about the tweet about boarding the plane, she said to our producer, quote: I would never say that. Those are not my words.\par \par \uc2 I don't know if she's claiming that her \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account was hacked, but it's on her official \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account. So with only six days left in this campaign, there are serious real open questions about the surging Kathy Barnette campaign, and where she truly stands on issues and whether or not she can win a general election.\par \par \uc2 Republicans and conservatives, they better get these answers to these questions before next Tuesday. And just like I have been saying, I've been enthusiastically open about my support for Dr. Mehmet Oz, as the only America First candidate in this race. He's the only candidate endorsed by President Trump.\par \par \uc2 I pointed out repeatedly, he's pro-life, he's strong on crime, strong on the border, tough on China, supports our Second Amendment. And one very important point, I see him by far as the Republican candidate in this primary that will win the general election.\par \par \uc2 This seat is a must hold seat if Republicans have any chance to win and hold that seat in November and he, unlike Kathy Barnette, is battle tested and he's been vetted and he can win in November.\par \par \uc2 So on Tuesday, Pennsylvania voters have a serious choice to make and the stakes could not be higher.\par \par \uc2 Here now, Pennsylvania Senate candidate, Dr. Oz.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Oz, I look at numerous comments about Obama, numerous comments incendiary comments about Muslims, even associations with QAnon. I look at controversial comments regarding race. I look at the trashing of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  again and again.\par \par \uc2 It's the most incendiary and she's never - she never stopped. There are many of them incendiary remarks about gays and lesbians. My question is this, she's not been vetted, Dr. Oz, and as I look at these comments and this information and nobody brought it up to -- brought it up prior to this show tonight, I don't see any way, any scenario under which she can win a general election. That is my 35-year broadcasting opinion.\par \par \uc2 I want you respond.\par \par \uc2 DR. MEHMET OZ (R), PENNSYLVANIA U.S. SENATE CANDIDATE: I concur with your diagnosis. She is a mystery. Barnette, they won't answer questions about her record, but what I do know concerns me. She's expressed mixed feelings about George Washington or, you know, the founding president. She's petitioned to build a statue to President Obama. Now, she claims to be an outsider, Sean --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: She wanted -- she wanted a statue of \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and she claims she's a MAGA conservative? I don't know many MAGA conservatives that are fond of \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 OZ: Well, during the BLM protest, that was one of the solutions she offered out there. But, you know, the fact of the matter is -- and this is why President Trump endorsed me. He said, I would win the general election. That's the most important goal for us to keep in mind as Republicans.\par \par \uc2 And you know, she says she's an outsider, but she's the worst kind of insider. She already lost running as a Republican in 2020 by, as you point out, 20 points to a pretty weak Democrat. She makes these homophobic comments, all kinds of phobias, by the way, going on with Kathy Barnette, and she is the best chance for Democrats to capture the Senate seat.\par \par \uc2 It will be a gift to \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and here's what makes it worse, Sean. This really bothers me. It is -- the swamp is out there doing anything they can to stop President Trump's endorsement of me and to stop President Trump period. We've got Washington money investing in Barnett to hurt Trump, but they're hurting the country by doing this. This is the same group that actually invested in Ohio to hurt President Trump's candidate there.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, isn't this the same club -- let's call names out here. Club for Growth, are they going to stand behind all these comments? They need to now be asked if they stand behind all of them, because I have -- I have a pile this high of them. This is not one comment, a one-off situation. This is not 20 years ago.\par \par \uc2 This is -- this is recent stuff that's out there, which I would argue -- and again, in my entire career, I've never called for canceling. I'm not woke. I don't believe in boycotts. I don't believe in demanding people be fired.\par \par \uc2 But my professional political opinion as a broadcaster, she cannot win a general election which might explain why she lost by 20 points in a congressional election lat -- at two years ago.\par \par \uc2 OZ: Well, thankfully, we got a couple days to fix this. I'm leading the polls as you pointed out. I'm a fighter. I'm focusing the campaign on Pennsylvania voters. I'm all over inflation and the energy that we have here that can help with that, the schools, COVID mandates still popping up and down, and why Washington's getting it wrong.\par \par \uc2 By the way, please go to DrOz.com if you want to help our campaign. We got a lot of things going down. We will win because we're focused on people that matter, but we have to address what Barnette represents. When Kathy started the surge, which is just fine, we ought to learn about answers to these important questions. Otherwise, you're taking a big risk with our Senate seat.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. I want to ask you. It was pretty funny, I didn't know I was in her \uc2 Twitter\uc2  feed. But Glenn Beck, why does \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  support unprincipled \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Well, it's interesting Glenn Beck now is one of Trump's biggest supporters. He never apologized. He doesn't have to. We were all friends. Kathy Barnette, I'll just assume she's apologizing for all of this.\par \par \uc2 Now, the question is will this now -- I've got to imagine that this is now going to become in the next 30, 24, 48, 72 hours, a political earthquake in this primary, because now the people of Pennsylvania are going to see voluminous amounts of material that they had not seen on Kathy Barnette.\par \par \uc2 And this is not to be against her. The question to me is very simple is, do you -- she obviously doesn't like President Trump. I have a whole stack of negative Trump tweets. How does she claim to be a MAGA conservative and trash Trump all the time?\par \par \uc2 OZ: Well, you know, two weeks ago, at one of our debates, she said that she was MAGA, that President Trump actually came to her and the other MAGA people in America. It wasn't his idea. He adopted their idea.\par \par \uc2 I was -- you know, sort of caught off guard by that commentary, but again, I'll post all these on DrOz.com if you want to see them. It's not hard. This is a nationally televised debate.\par \par \uc2 But that's the level of confidence she has in what she's articulating. But she is a mystery person. We don't know much about her. We have to be able to learn and she's not willing to share. So, it raises additional red flags when every day -- every hour of every day since she became on the radar screen. I've been finding out things that are very alarming to me, and it will be fodder for the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 This is our seat to lose folks. We will win the Republican seat in Pennsylvania. I am confident I will be able to do that. It's why President Trump feels so confident he's been so supportive and I appreciate his endorsement. But we don't want to throw this away with a candidate that's not well-vetted.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, I've been warning that when primaries become as contentious as yours has become, I've looked at ads about you, and I've known you. I did my own vetting process with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I did my own vetting process with you. I think you can confirm it was fairly intensive and you gave all the right answers, which is the only reason I supported you and believe in you.\par \par \uc2 They did the same thing with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . They're doing the same thing with you here. This is going to be a very interesting six days in Pennsylvania. I've got to believe the people of Pennsylvania are going to discover something that they didn't know in the days to come.\par \par \uc2 I'll give you the last word.\par \par \uc2 OZ: You're 100 percent right. Folks, do your homework. This is too important to make a mistake with. Learn who Kathy Barnette really is, and then go to DrOz.com and find out why you want to vote for me. Six days away from victory.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. And we're supporting your candidacy.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Mehmet Oz, thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, Chicago mayor -- we call her Mayor Lightweight -- exchange heated words with Congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  over the leaked Supreme Court opinion. We'll explain.\par \par \uc2 And Congressman Boebert and Leo 2.0 Terrell, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, Republican congresswoman from Colorado, Congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  is now exposing failed far left Chicago mayor -- we call her Mayor Lightweight -- after her tweets urging a call to arms ahead of the Supreme Court's abortion ruling. In response, Congresswoman Boebert tweeted, quote, insurrectionist -- which Lightweight replied: Excuse me. Insurrection is your thing, not ours.\par \par \uc2 To which Congresswoman Boebert fired back, quote: six killed, 18 wounded in your city this past weekend. Nearly 200 murders so far this year. Go fix your city, hack.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, here with reaction is Colorado Congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 , along with Leo 2.0 Terrell.\par \par \uc2 Leo knows this congresswoman. 2009, we started on this show, all the names of people that nobody ever hears about, all the people in Chicago shot, all the people shot and killed. We never cover those stories. I've done it for years, and nobody ever fixes a thing. She hasn't lifted a finger to make Chicago safe and secure.\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 LAUREN BOEBERT\uc2  (R-CO): Right. Sean, President Trump said to peacefully and patriotically make your voices heard. Chicago Mayor Little \uc2 Lori Lightfoot\uc2  just gave a call to arms. If anyone in America is an insurrectionist, it's little Lori.\par \par \uc2 And instead of coming at me on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , this failed mayor should be focused on protecting the good people of Chicago. Sadly, she refuses to do that. Let's just look at some of the headlines since this murder mayor took office.\par \par \uc2 From ABC 7 Chicago, one month old shot in the head. "\uc2 Chicago Tribune\uc2 ", 361 businesses closed in Chicago. "Chicago Sun Times", Chicago's most violent weekend sees 104 shot, 14 children wounded.\par \par \uc2 And from "Courthouse News", Chicago projects $733 million budget shortfall in 2022. "\uc2 Chicago Tribune\uc2 ", 2021 is Chicago's deadliest year in a quarter century. And just this week, Sean, NBC Chicago says \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is to move his headquarters out of Chicago.\par \par \uc2 Her city is a war zone, her people are suffering, businesses are fleeing. Little Lori needs to get off \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and make Chicago safe again.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, Leo, you don't bring props like the congresswoman does. I think you need to up your game a little bit.\par \par \uc2 LEO TERRELL, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Oh, no, I don't need to because first of all, I'm proud to be with the congresswoman, and I'm the lawyer. The congresswoman provided the evidence. Lori Lightweight is guilty based on the evidence you just saw presented by the congresswoman.\par \par \uc2 Look, when she calls for a call for arms, there's plenty of guns in Chicago, and she hasn't done anything during her tenure. I want to make sure this is very clear, this is a distraction from her disastrous administration as the congresswoman pointed out.\par \par \uc2 And, Sean, you can play the tape of what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said on January 6, peaceful, patriotically. You talked about all the riots. The Democrats do not handle any investigation regarding the rights because those are their clients. Those are their voters. Antifa, \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2 , they're not going to go after their own base, and that's why you have her trying to do a misdirection.\par \par \uc2 You see, Lori Lightweight has a war zone in Chicago, and she needs to take care of it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We have less than 20 seconds.\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman, I understand that a bunch of RINOs are trying to take you out in your seat and primary you on purpose. How's that race going?\par \par \uc2 BOEBERT: That's right, Sean. We do have some RINOs trying to take me out. But freedom is a great motivator and I need your people to go to LaurenForFreedom.com to join my campaign, help me in this fight so I can stay standing strong for Americans all across our nation. Thank you so much, Sean. LaurenForFreedom.com.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And, by the way, if you get mine and Leo support, you really --\par \par \uc2 TERRELL: I'll be in Colorado tomorrow. I'll be in Colorado tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: There you go. You got Leo's endorsement.\par \par \uc2 More HANNITY, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Unfortunately, that is all the time we have left this evening. As always, we thank you for being with us. Thank you for making this show possible. We can't do it without you. We hope you set your DVR so you never miss an episode of HANNITY.\par \par \uc2 Don't forget FOXnews.com for all the latest news, information when you want to catch up on what's going on around the world, hannity.com as well.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned. Let not your heart be troubled. Laura's next, "THE INGRAHAM ANGLE," straight ahead. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020220512ei5b00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Scranton Joe About To Sell America Out To China; Joe's Faux Empathy On Full Display; \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  Visited A Farm Today; Decoupling From China Shouldn't Be Controversial; SCOTUS Leaker Must Be Publically Revealed; Why Is It Taking So Long To Find The Leaker?; Lessons The GOP Can Learn From Dems' Failures; Dems Show America How Not To Govern; Ninth Circuit Court Of Appeals In California Rules Against State Ban On Semiautomatic Weapon Sales To Young Adults; Broadway Actress Criticizes Audience Member For Not Wearing A Mask; Singer Madonna Releases NFTs; China Arrests Cardinal In Hong Kong; Republican Pennsylvania Senate Candidate \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2  Interviewed On His Primary Campaign Message And View On U.S.-China Economic Relations\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham, Trace Gallagher \par \uc2 7,879 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: We can't do it without you. We hope you set your DVR, so you never miss an episode of Hannity. Don't forget foxnews.com for all the latest news, information, when you want to catch up on what's going on around the world, hannity.com as well. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Let your heart be troubled. Laura's next. THE INGRAHAM ANGLE straight ahead. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: I'm Laura Ingraham. This is THE INGRAHAM ANGLE from Washington tonight. Thank you for joining us.\par \par \uc2 All right. Right off the bat. We got old McBiden saw a farm. That's the focus of tonight's 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 All right. Put your mind at rest, people. Stop worrying about soaring food and energy costs, because today \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is on the case. He visited a farm. It was part listening tour.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Every day when that gets pushed back.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT, UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: Pushed back to the other crops.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Yes. And we usually run out of growing season, so we can't that. I can typically produce about 60 percent as a double crop. But yes, there's still always risk involved that I'm bearing by myself.\par \par \uc2 A couple of things that I wanted to be able to talk about here. What we had just walked through back there.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. Part meaningless, small talk.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: This one working. There you go. Please, sit down.\par \par \uc2 One thing is I want to put the rest. Everybody looks to me and says, have you ever been in a farm? And I remind them that nobody knows. I come from the state of Delaware, single largest industry in Delaware and the Delmarva of Delaware, Maryland, Virginia, Peninsula, that Peninsula goes down, is agriculture.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Thank you, \uc2 Rand McNally\uc2 . And more talk of spending money that we don't have.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Early this year, the \uc2 U.S. Department of Agriculture\uc2  announced that would invest $250 million to boost fertilizer production. Literally on the plane out here, on Air Force One, I turned to Tom and I said, Tom, double that. Make it $500 million. It's so desperately needed.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Why stop there? Well, what's desperately needed, though, is a president who doesn't offer fake empathy when what we need are real solutions. But fake empathy is all they can offer. And it's exactly what we got, when he went on to Chicago.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I come from a family, and I mean this sincerely, like most of you, where the price of gasoline went up significantly, price of food went up. That's what we talked about at the dinner table, the kitchen table.\par \par \uc2 I couldn't afford daycare. I couldn't afford childcare. Not a joke. I was making $42,000 a year, which is a lot of money as a U.S. senator. I couldn't afford it. Thank God, I got a big family. My dad would say, Family is the beginning, middle, and the end.\par \par \uc2