ategy here? Do you think - I'm trying to figure out motive. You know, I always think a motive at a crime scene is an ethical - crime ethical scene. What's the motive here?\par \par \uc2 SEVERINO: Well, I mean, a lot of people assume, I assume, is a liberal clerk, who thought - this is kind of a desperation move, right. This is a last ditch effort. We see what's going to happen. Roe is going to be overturned. By this point in the term, if someone was going to change at all, which is rare, it probably would have already happened.\par \par \uc2 So I think they thought this is the last ditch effort. I think it's clearly going to backfire. I mean, you were already seeing it backfiring with the broad opposition, even among Democrats to the crazy people protesting in front of justices' houses, the refusal of President Biden to say that that needs is beyond the pale. So it's backfiring.\par \par \uc2 And I think if anything, it strengthens the spine of the justices. But you know, these are 20 somethings, who I think maybe can't think very far ahead. And frankly--\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Do you think, it's coordinated, Carrie. That it's not just one person. I mean, I've got a number of friends, who probably - you haven't talked to them, but it's not just one person, they believe. And they think, it's a coordinated - more like what happened with the leak that led to the controversy over Justice Thomas' confirmation hearing.\par \par \uc2 SEVERINO: Well, it's just it's still so hard for me to wrap my brain around even one clerk leaking in such a ginormous way. I mean, some of these, other ones saying, leaking the amount of the judges on different things, that's bad enough. But the leak of an entire opinion, I don't know, if there's multiple people involved in this, that in theory ought to make it even easier for the Chief Justice to track them down, right? Because it's like--\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. Carrie, if you and I are a couple other former clerks, had all the clerks 