apital. It comes two days after pro-government mobs attacked peaceful protesters, triggering a wave of violence across the country.\par \par \uc2 And this is a live look at Brussels. One of the big stories there tonight, the \uc2 European Union\uc2  will no longer require masks to be worn at air plates -- at the airports, rather, and on air planes starting next week.\par \par \uc2 The decision comes amid the easing of coronavirus restrictions across the block.\par \par \uc2 Rules for masks may still vary by airline if passengers fly to or from destinations where the rules are different.\par \par \uc2 Just some of the other stories beyond our borders tonight. We will be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: Republican voters in Nebraska have pick hog farmer and veterinarian Jim Pillen as their nominee for governor. Pillen won despite an endorsement of his rival by former President Trump.\par \par \uc2 Charles Herbster\uc2  was hurt allegations that he had groped multiple women. In West Virginia several candidates supported by Mr. Trump won in House primary contests.\par \par \uc2 A Florida judges says a Congressional map approved by Republican Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is unconstitutional because it breaks up a district now held by a black Democrat, spreading Democratic voters across several Republican districts. The judge says he will issue a formal order on Thursday or Friday to keep portions of that map from taking effect in November's election. He made it clear that he would rule in favor of voting rights groups who were challenging the map.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina Republican Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  said President Biden might be the best person to lead and unite the country, that was following last year's Capitol riot. That's according to audio obtained by "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 " that first aired on CNN. Graham has since appeared to rekindle his support for former president Trump, saying that he hopes that 