ar \par \uc2 FOY: Critics filed a federal lawsuit to stop the arrests, alleging migrants are being illegally detained.\par \par \uc2 GERRY MORRIS, ATTORNEY: If the state wants to focus on a particular crime, criminal trespass, then they can focus on a particular crime. It's just they can't do it for this purpose regulating immigration.\par \par \uc2 FOY: New video tonight shows more than 150 migrants in Eagle Pass, this group coming from Cuba, Venezuela, and Columbia. Human smuggling cases are up, leading to dangerous chases through Texas towns. Ranchers are paying out of pocket for damage to their fences and lost animals. These two migrants spending four days on branch, separated from their group without food or water. The \uc2 Texas Department of Public Safety\uc2  uses drones to find the others, and troopers on the ground to arrest runners, which in Kinney County can mean jail time.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: If people realize that they will be prosecuted and sent to jail up to a year, maybe they will pick a different county other than Kinney County to come through.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 FOY (on camera): John, as of May 5th, Texas DPS troopers have arrested over 4,000 migrants for criminal trespassing as part of Operation Lone Star. Many of them have reached plea deals. We'll send it back to you.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: Nate Foy for us along the border. Nate, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court is striking down California's ban on the sale of semiautomatic weapons to adults under the age of 21. The Ninth Circuit Court ruled two to one that the law violates the Second Amendment right to bear arms. The group that brought the challenge says it is now optimistic that other age-based gun bans will be overturned.\par \par \uc2 Up next, the devastation left behind after the Russian occupation of a Ukrainian town near the capital of Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: The House has emphatically approved a fresh $40 billion Ukraine aid package that beefs President Biden's initial request. A senior Russian official is denouncing U.S. aid for Ukraine as part of a U.S. proxy war against Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, we show you some of the devastation left behind by Russian troops. Correspondent Trey Yingst is in Kyiv tonight.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 TREY YINGST, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Destroyed cars line the road outside the city of Kharkiv. This time last week, these small towns in northern Ukraine sat on the front lines.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE (through translator): These are our citizens who tried to evacuate. Unfortunately, they were with children. They were shot with an automatic gun. One car was hit with a canon.\par \par \uc2 YINGST: Ukrainian forces says say they've launched multiple successful counteroffensives in the city. As reports indicate, some Russian troops were pushed all the way back over the order. Speaking to a group of French students Wednesday, Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  detailed the thousands of innocent people killed so far in the war and the millions displaced.\par \par \uc2 VOLODYMYR ZELENSKYY, UKRAINIAN PRESIDENT (through translator): How could it have been possible? Why no global or European institution is not enough to stop this war? And you know I don't want that to remain a rhetorical question.\par \par \uc2 YINGST: Zelenskyy also discussed the southern port city of Mariupol where Ukrainian fighters remain holed up in the Azovstal steel plant. Russian troops who surround the plant continue to bomb the soldiers.\par \par \uc2 LT. ILLYA SAMOILENKO, UKRAINIAN ARMY: We are taking heavy casualties. We're taking losses. Every day might be our last here. The results of this might be our imminent death or capturing by the enemy, which also means death for us.\par \par \uc2 YINGST: Further east in the Russian occupied region of Kherson, Russian installed leadership claims they will ask Moscow to 