ey go and they like, just load up everything they need. I mean, and, of course, they had none at that CVS and so I went to the supermarket they didn't have any. And so now apparently, you know, people are hogging it and then selling it at all kinds of high prices, it's a shame. But you know what, Biden can't get away with it. He can blame -- he can blame the devil, I don't really care, but people know what the problem is.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I've seen gangs, Dana, of roving babies out on the street just taking the -- just taking the baby formula from other babies. It's like --\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Are you just eye level with them?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes, I'm eye level. It's disgusting. So, are you changing any of your birthday plans because of inflation, no bouncy castle?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: No, I had to let that one go, you know, it's too expensive.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: did you notice one thing, though, about how Joe supposedly has a reputation for empathy. However, when it comes to stuff like that, this, it's always like these things will pass.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes. It's interesting because we've talked before about how they don't listen to us but they don't have an early warning system at the White House --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Right.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: -- of like, this is going to be a problem.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I remember when I was the deputy, I had to read all the papers and there was this one story about the Dubai ports thing, and for days it was in the Washington Times like in the back pages. And I was like, I think this is going to be a problem. And everyone blew me off it's not going to be a problem. It became a gigantic problem.\par \par \uc2 This baby formula problem is not new, it's been going on for a few months. So it seems to me like nobody at the White House is going, excuse me, Mr. President, we're going to have a problem here.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And because you have moms were so anxious. I don't -- I talked to several moms today, we had actually had one on Newsroom as well. She goes, every family member in three states in Kentucky area looking for baby formula, they're looking everywhere and the White House can close its eyes, it can cover its ears and they can scream Rick Scott a thousand times and it's not going to change this fact. They needed to prepare people. I'm not saying that they can fix it overnight but they had -- all of a sudden, it's like the first time they're talking about it?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes. You know what's so -- I have to say this is so ironic. I mean, the media is more alarmed by an abortion shortage than a baby formula shortage. What does that say?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It's to blame.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It is kind of interesting. The moment this thing happened everybody exploded but this has been going on for a while, no one gives a damn.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Interesting.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: They have to follow the moms' groups.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I follow them.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Listen to the kids crying for their baby formula. I don't even know what it is. Up next, soon to be Twitter owner \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  now facing death threats. Find out why next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Wild times for the world's richest man. \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  setting the internet on fire with a very cryptic tweet hinting that his life could be in danger. Quote, "if I die under mysterious circumstances, it's been nice knowing you."\par \par \uc2 Musk had been threatened by the head of \uc2 Russia's space agency\uc2  over his attempts to provide Ukraine with internet service. And the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  is continuing their crusade against Musk's purchase of Twitter. The latest ridiculous attack claims women and people of color will suffer most from the buy-out.\par \par \uc2 All right,