uch. So, he has personal security as he should.\par \par \uc2 You would imagine that if these are threats coming from another government, that that is taken care of, and it shouldn't -- there should be no leaks about it. And there should be sharing of information as needed. What's interesting about \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is he seems to have made all the right enemies, right?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: So, the media is freaking out. The far left is calling him racist. The Russians are mad at him because he's willing to help the Ukrainians to have freedom. So, I think that when the history of this period is written, he will be seen as somebody who really was willing to take his wealth and try to do what's -- what he hopes will be good.\par \par \uc2 I think we'll see how it all turns out for Twitter, but I don't -- I just don't think that Twitter could possibly be worse if \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  takes over.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, Jesse, they say -- he says that he will quintuple the revenue. Is that possible?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I wouldn't know.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But he --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: But yes, he says he wants to cut costs and do some hiring and actually make sure we get paid for some tweets. So, I'm excited about that.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: And he'll charge people. He will charge for you too.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: With inflation, we could get paid for these tweets. We could make some of our money back. And getting rid of the bots is a good thing too.\par \par \uc2 The type of person that claims that they're about to die, it's four types of people. One --\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: Let me write this down.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: A Smollett. You remember him? He's getting hold off. Oh, I'm not suicidal. You know, those are the drama queens, right? And then there are the people who like in the liberal media that make a living destroying other people's lives, but if you criticize them on one little thing, oh my god, death threats. I'm about to die. Those are your hysterical narcissists.\par \par \uc2 And then there's people that actually get death threats, legit ones, like Gutfeld, who like actually people hate. Like, I get death threats all the time, but they're not specific. Greg gets really specific ones because as I said, he's so --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes. (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And then you have Musk. And I think Musk is trolling us. And you know, he's just having some fun. He's like the most interesting follow on Twitter since Trump got nuked. So, you know, if you say you're that dangerous, that kind of makes you a dangerous man, and that's good for your brand. But I didn't think the Russians would take him out. I thought the deep state would.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, but with deep states -- the deep state does, I mean, they're not going to say anything about it, but Greg, you want to put a final thought on this?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes. If there was a disease that killed all white men, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  would say, women and minorities did harvest. So -- but the point about the bedfellows in this. If you're not on the side of Musk, you end up being on the side of this \uc2 Russian space agency\uc2  who is against free speech, it's for the suppression of thought.\par \par \uc2 So, like you got -- you should probably consider that. But the best part about this story is him telling his staff, plan on working harder because that means you're fired. He's going to -- like, he's going to get rid of, I think 1000.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: 1000 people.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: The average, like, it's 200 grand. You know, it's a lot of money. And then if you start -- he's going to start making some serious money, but he's going to get rid of people. And he'll probably get rid of the marketing department because he's like Trump. He's his own marketer. He'll just tweet, tweet, tweet. So, that's, you know -- but you know, everybody that felt they needed a day of rest at Twitter because they have that, will be gone. You don't need them.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: The interesting thing about him is whenever he says he's going to do something, he does it.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Anyway, straight ahead, brand new details in the mysterious deaths of three American tourists at a Bahamas resort.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Why?\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: A luxury vacation turning into a nightmare in the Bahamas. A huge mystery surrounding how three Americans ended up dead and another one hospitalized while they were staying at the popular Sandals Emerald Bay Resort. The single survivor had to be airlifted to Miami and reportedly woke up and could not move her body. Investigators are reportedly looking into toxic substances that could have leaked from an air conditioning unit. And authorities say autopsies are being done today.\par \par \uc2 Jesse, obviously these stories -- this is not a political angle to any of this at all here. How do you -- how do you react to this? Is there something we should do?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I blame Biden.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: Let me write that down too. We blame -- here we blame --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I hope I do not have to launch another fake boycott of the Bahamas like I did with the Dominican Republic. Remember how the D.R. was not answering questions and was being very, very sketchy. And that boycott still is in effect. I have not gone --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Your fake boycotts --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: -- to the D.R. since those people passed -- yes.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: The minibar thing.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes. There's a lot of unanswered questions. And there are a lot of unanswered questions here as well. I'm not ruling anything out. And I mean, anything. I don't think investigators are either. I talked to a law enforcement source who told me carbon monoxide poisoning is his thing unless someone plays something in the air conditioning unit.\par \par \uc2 We have no idea. But we do have a better relationship with the Bahamas that you know, former British colony. Some guy, \uc2 Adam Stewart\uc2 , this Jamaican businessman, he's the chairman of \uc2 Sandals\uc2 . We expect answers within the next 24 hours and we're going to get the toxicology report, right?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And they're going to give us all the answers. We'll know everything.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: Greg, is this a story that --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Well, I don't know if I could follow up that in-depth analysis of this story. I will say that thankfully, this is rare. I think we get kind of drawn to this stuff because it happens in luxury vacations and exotic, but I'm sure this -- it's probably more common in the United States. When we say toxic substances, it may not have come from any machinery. I mean, you can -- like, if you ever go somewhere and you buy something and it's not reliable --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Like I said, we're not ruling it not ruling anything out.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: We're not ruling anything out. But I think -- I'm just going to make a suggestion to Fox News that maybe you should send a team. I could go just to do some fact findings for a few days.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Yes, I would agree with that. Can I come too as your deputy?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes, you can -- you can come as long as you bring the painkillers.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Not a toxic substance.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: Dana, have they handled this from a public relations standpoint the right way, Bahamas and the resort.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I think -- the first -- from what I can tell, I think as best as they could. I think that first reports are almost always wrong. I turned to the judge who will probably confirm that. Like, I actually am personally very concerned about carbon monoxide poisoning. I have been for a long time.\par \par \uc2 And I've not had any experience with it. I've had friends that have and it's a very, very scary thing. And that -- it sounds like when you can't move your body, like, that is one of the things that happens.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Does it? Is that its symptom?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: OK.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: Judge, is there -- are there legal issues here that the -- that the resort and the Bahamas have --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Oh, yes. Oh, yes. First -- let me tell you something. Are the bodies here --\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: This is the leading question.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, thank you very much. Are the -- are the bodies back in the States? Do we know that? Where is the autopsy being conducted? Who's conducting the autopsies? That's the first thing I want to know. The State Department says it's closely monitoring. Does that mean that they're not allowing the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to be a part of the investigation?\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: I think they took some samples in Philadelphia for them to be analyzed, but --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: They took some samples of them? Does that mean the autopsy was done there or are the bodies are here. Do you know?\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: I think autopsy was mad in the Bahamas, but I think the samples were sent back to Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK. I appreciate that. But the autopsy was done there. That doesn't help me if samples are sent to Philadelphia. I would want the body and the samples in the same place.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: I'm on your side. I'm just giving you the facts here.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I don't believe -- I don't believe in a break in the chain of custody, OK. I don't want to hear the bodies over there and we're sending samples on an airplane somewhere else. But here's the bottom line of whether they're criminally responsible, is an issue.\par \par \uc2 But there's no question this is a huge civil lawsuit. The civil plaintiff's attorneys are already down there. They've already bought -- their tickets