ou want to reassure people and make them less paranoid and suspicious, maybe just give them all the numbers and let them know what the truth is. Why don't they do that?\par \par \uc2 DR. AARON KHERIATY, CHIEF OF ETHICS, THE UNITY PROJECT: That's exactly right. Transparency is a basic principle of public health ethics. It was violated over and over with a mass vaccination campaign, and particularly with the vaccine mandates where people were not allowed to exercise informed consent, both because they were under the threat of school expulsion, as we heard in the last segment, or losing their job.\par \par \uc2 And even if they weren't under a mandate, they still didn't have access to all the relevant information. So we had to file this Freedom of Information Act, myself and some of my colleagues last September just to get the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  data. They wanted to slow walk it, wanted to take 75 years to release data that they were able to review at the F.D.A. in only 108 days.\par \par \uc2 And now we're starting to get that data after many people have already taken the vaccine. And as you mentioned, some of the safety data in the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  analysis is quite concerning, and we can talk more about that. And, of course, yesterday's announcement about the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine.\par \par \uc2 I'm glad actually the F.D.A. is acknowledging that there is there this concern about thrombosis, about blood clots with the J&J vaccine. But Tucker, I've got to be honest, I'm a little surprised that they're applying that level of scrutiny to the J&J vaccine, but not to the mRNA vaccines, not to the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 , and \uc2 Moderna\uc2  vaccine, because actually, if you look at overall safety issues, the J&J vaccine, probably has a better overall safety profile.\par \par \uc2 Now, it might have higher incidence of thrombosis, but there was another recent very important study on all-cause mortality. And I think last time I was on with you we talked about it. This statistic is a good way to cut through a complex issue and a lot of statistical noise. And it compared all three of the vaccines on all-cause mortality, are you more likely to live or die after you get this vaccine?\par \par \uc2 And the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  actually had a modest improvement, whereas the mRNA vaccine showed no improvement in all-cause mortality. So, I'd like to see the same level of scrutiny applied to all of the vaccines.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, and compassion and care for people who are injured by it. I mean, that's the least we can expect from our doctors.\par \par \uc2 KHERIATY: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: They are supposed to help us, not dismiss us or punish us for saying how we've been injured. Dr. Aaron Kheriaty, one of the truly reliable sane voices on this topic. No one is going to call you a kook, and we're glad that you came on tonight. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 KHERIATY: Thanks, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So an interesting thing that's happened in the wake of the Supreme Court leak about Roe v. Wade is all of a sudden, women exist again, no more burning persons, women, and they have bodily autonomy and whatever, but no one told the Associated Press, they're still on another track. And they've just issued new guidelines explaining that actually women don't exist. The term is pregnant people. Who is right? We will settle it after the break.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So we learned the other day that anyone who didn't vote for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is not only immoral, obviously, but a dangerous extremist. Now, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's F.B.I. has begun, of course, a purge of political dissidents from within the Bureau. FOX's Kevin Corke has that story for us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Hey, Kevin.\par \par \uc2 KEVIN CORKE, FOX NEWS CHANNEL WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: Hey, good to be with you, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 An incredible story, a real stunner of a report that has Congressional lawm