istrict of Virginia, crickets from these people, this is unacceptable. These are these are real threats against the lives of Supreme Court justices. And they need to step up right now and do something about this.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. And, Carrie, we'll get into the substance of what's happening or the lies about the opinion. But that is a question, is it not? We're at a time where we've had 60 months of Democrats screaming incitement, incitement, insurrection, insurrection.\par \par \uc2 And now, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is parsing her words, mincing your words about what this is, this intimidation campaign, which I'm calling terroristic, because I think it is, against the justices. Do they have adequate security dovetailing from what Mike just said?\par \par \uc2 CARRIE SEVERINO, FORMER JUSTICE THOMAS CLERK: Oh, I sure hope so. I mean, I agree. I think this is one of the most concerning things about this leak. Not only does it strike a blow at the trust inherently in the internal workings of the court, but this is a real act of threat against the justices themselves.\par \par \uc2 I know that they are ramping up security. But as - this is why I think and a lot of us that said, let's just issue this opinion quickly. I think it's no surprise, though. I mean, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , remember used to work for demand justice. This is like the most radical left-wing dark money group out there.\par \par \uc2 These are the people who were praising the leakers saying, we need more Supreme Court leaks. This is the people who have a board member who says, the Constitution is trash and should be scrapped. They want to have more justices yesterday, they said in the court. They're trying to use this to pack the court, so even if they can't switch this decision now or for some of them even said, let's pack the court before the end of midterm.\par \par \uc2 Oh, my goodness, it is no-holds-barred. It's any means justify the end here. And that's what's so disturbing about this leak and the threats that we're seeing.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. Mike, these are people who claim to be threatened by pro- life people praying outside abortion clinics, just silently praying. They think that's a threat. OK. But now, given what's happening, it's like, well, yes, we respect the right to privacy.\par \par \uc2 Here's how the CNN framed the threats against the Supreme Court today. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JIM SCIUTTO, CNN HOST: Law enforcement officials are preparing for potential violence in the Capitol and nationwide. \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  are warning. The far right is calling for violence against a religious group planning to rally for abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 WHITNEY WILD, CNN LAW ENFORCEMENT CORRESPONDENT: There is a potential for violence against abortion clinic providers, abortion clinic staff.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Mike, this isn't journalism. This is just pro-abortion propaganda. We've had pro-life centers vandalized in just the last 24, 48 hours, which happens regularly. But now the threat is from right wing. I mean, no one should be threatening anyone here. But that's the framing of this?\par \par \uc2 DAVIS: Yes. I mean, it's gaslighting. It's laughable. They're saying that these pro-life groups are threatening conservative justices. That doesn't make sense. I mean these conservative justices are getting threats against their life online and elsewhere right now. And the justice department needs to step it up. They need to start making arrests for conspiracy, for obstruction, for assault.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Carrie, I want to read a recent passage from a website a lot of lawyers read, it's called \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  blog. And "Start from the premise that there were actually at least two leakers, and three leaks. The first leak was to The Wall Street Journal editorial board last week. In substance, it was at the court had voted to overrule Roe. But that the precise outcome 