ally condemn these terroristic acts on the part of activists. And say, this will not stand and they need to find this leaker or leakers, I should say, out of the Supreme Court. This can't be this difficult, if it really wants to be found out.\par \par \uc2 Carrie and Mike, great to see you both. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 And the left wants you to avert your eyes to the reality of what is happening around you. Now, they were quick to celebrate, of course, the jobs numbers today. But they forgot to mention that 363,000 Americans left the workforce at a time when we have a record high number of job openings.\par \par \uc2 Now, they forgot to mention that while wages went up 5.5 percent, inflation is up 8.5 percent, wiping out any of your gains and then some.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, we find out that 28 Republican senators and I've been warning you about this, they chose to sell out made in the USA by making it easier and more desirable for American companies to offshore operations, meaning jobs overseas, especially in China, because they're getting rid of tariffs. That's what they want to do.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, \uc2 Kayleigh McEnany\uc2 , former White House press secretary; and Jason Chaffetz, Fox News contributor.\par \par \uc2 Kayleigh, the White House is engaged in this bizarre attempt. It's a victory lap after this week. When economists are now just debating, has the recession already begun, or is it right around the corner? So what is the White House trying to do here?\par \par \uc2 KAYLEIGH MCENANY\uc2 , FORMER TRUMP WH PRESS SECRETARY: Yes, create an alternate reality. Laura, I went on Chief of Staff \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2 's \uc2 Twitter\uc2  feed. There were 19 retweets, celebrating the jobs numbers today. All 19 tweets painted this rosy picture of the economy.\par \par \uc2 Jobs are coming back, of course. Jobs coming back is a rather organic thing after lockdowns. But put that aside, the only number that matters, though, the only one is the approval ra