d $125 to fill up their F150. It just doesn't happen.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No. Oh, just go out and buy an electric car, Jason. Stop complaining.\par \par \uc2 All right. Well, Kayleigh, Biden's new press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is already raising some eyebrows for what has been called a potential conflict of interest, I guess, given what's a long-term relationship she has with CNN's Suzanne Malveaux.\par \par \uc2 Kayleigh, so Psaki, Symone Sanders, they go to MSNBC, and now they have just a direct line to another outlet, CNN. So now there was a lot of comments online about, well, talk about being in bed with the press - press and with politicians. I mean, this is now taking it a step further.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Yes, I have a feeling CNN will be called on often, so too will MSNBC among other friendly outlets. I also have a sneaking suspicion just to guess that KJP, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  may end up at CNN rather than MSNBC, like her two colleagues, because three Biden officials at MSNBC would be quite a lot.\par \par \uc2 But you're right. This administration is kind of rife with these conflicts. But how can you not be when 99.9 percent of the press is, in fact, liberal? It's this revolving door between liberal outlets and the press room and softball questions and not asking follow-ups. There's no Jim Acostas in that room, or Kaitlan Collins shouting questions.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, my gosh. Jason, so the economy, it's tanking. We all know it. But racial justice groups are now apparently pressing Biden to form a Reparations Commission. We knew this was coming.\par \par \uc2 I have no doubt in my mind that this will be yet another thing that they're going to do to try to distract from the shiny object of gas prices and supply chain and inflationary concerns. That, Ok, you're going to get reparations if you just vote for the Democrats, despite how lousy your life is getting. Jason, your thoughts on that?\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Again,