nstitutional law?\par \par \uc2 And that's what these justices if that decision, somehow becomes final will return Roe v. Wade to the states where it belongs not in the Constitution, not on the federal government, but to the state. 50 laboratories in a federal system, Martha.\par \par \uc2 So, Nomiki, Rachel Carmona, who is the executive director of the Women's March that we remember after President Trump was elected, she came out and she said this, we will be ungovernable until this government starts working for us, until the attacks on our bodies let up, and until the right for abortion is codified into law.\par \par \uc2 So, she is saying we will be ungovernable. What would you say to the individuals who are committed to, and protests obviously, as an American right? And peaceful protest is absolutely an American right.\par \par \uc2 But what do you say to those individuals who are considering going into churches, into masses this weekend? And potentially, you know, to the front steps of these justices homes?\par \par \uc2 NOMIKI KONST, HOST, THE NOMIKI SHOW: Well, you know, they're not doing anything that isn't peaceful. Going into a church and expressing your feelings and walking and dressing a certain way, is incredibly peaceful, especially if you are a member of that congregation, as they're calling for people to do.\par \par \uc2 The majority of Catholics in this country support legalized abortion. The majority of Americans support Roe v. Wade, which, by the way, sir, was already ruled on with the court that you supposedly respect so much.\par \par \uc2 So, what you're saying now is that we should reverse a decision that was already ruled on, and it's supported by most Americans, because there is a conservative movement that is well funded with extremists, extreme right- wing conservative justices that have been groomed for decades.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TERRELL: That's shameful. Shameful.\par \par \uc2 KONST: For decades.\par \par \uc2 TER