es are rising, we had big wage cost numbers today. Real incomes are - real wages after inflation are falling. It's very difficult.\par \par \uc2 Consumer confidence is down. Small business confidence is down. So no, I don't think we're in a recession right now. But as I say, I think it would be virtually impossible to avoid a recession, either later this year or next year.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Larry, here's how one of Biden's economic advisors actually views the economy today.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JARED BERNSTEIN, MEMBER OF WH COUNCIL OF ECONOMIC ADVISERS: Is this country, is this economy in a position of strength to face what's coming at us? The answer, if you look at our job market, if you look at our GDP growth, if you look at household - how households incomes are doing, or their savings are doing, you would conclude that we are approaching this moment from a position of strength.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Larry, GDP shrank last month and inflation is destroying savings. People are getting poorer in the United States. What are these people talking about? And does this in any way calm the markets?\par \par \uc2 KUDLOW: You know, I want to say, Jared Bernstein is an old friend of mine. And personally, he's really a good - he's a lovely man.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'm sure he saves kittens from trees, Larry. But this is the country going down the two. I've got to say, I love you, and you're one of my favorite people. Everyone's friends with everyone in Washington and New York. We all love each other. We all - that's great.\par \par \uc2 Our country is falling apart. And these people are lying about it. I don't think we can mince words at this point. They're lying to the American people. I'm sorry to jump on you. I'm fed up with us.\par \par \uc2 KUDLOW: Yes, I understand. But analytically, I don't know what Jared is talking about, because in fact, he's talking about consumer incomes. Well, look, consumer incomes after inflation are falling. And small business incomes after inflation are falling. So I'm not sure where he's coming from on this.\par \par \uc2 I mean, look, the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  blew this a year ago. I don't know why \uc2 Jay Powell\uc2  has been reappointed. He certainly doesn't deserve it. He has - the people do not have confidence. He was out there yesterday, Laura. And he tried to whitewash the whole problem. He sounded like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  blaming inflation on \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and COVID. That's nonsense.\par \par \uc2 The problem here with too much federal spending, too much federal borrowing, and too much central bank money printing. And the Fed has got to stop whitewashing the problem and go to it, otherwise the longer they wait and the more they tried to avoid these issues, which is what Biden is unfortunately doing, the worst the recession is going to be.\par \par \uc2 I mean, the worst possible combination is inflationary recession, a double barrel of poison. That's the worst thing you can have. And that's my concern right now. Again, the Fed's not taking action. We're still spending too much in Washington. You got - these guys are talking about raising taxes, which should be the worst thing in the world.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They should all be fired. Is it any one of these people, Larry, are there any single one, Yellen, \uc2 Jay Powell\uc2 , the Council on Economic Advisers? Do - I mean, friends and - should any of these people be in this position after they blew off the inflation concerns that you raised and \uc2 Larry Summers\uc2  raised a year ago? Any of them be still working? Because in corporate America they all would have been fired. On a basketball team that they were coaches, they'd be fired. Long ago.\par \par \uc2 KUDLOW: Well, I'll put it a little more positively. You mentioned \uc2 Larry Summers\uc2 , who got this right. You - \uc2 Jason Furman\uc2 , got this right. I mean, I think moderate Democrats wi