e more trade with Asia, or we have to spend more money to send our values, which our children are taught are racist values, overseas. So they're comfortable, and maybe on tax issues, but they don't like the other issues. So you do believe those issues are important? Then we'll let you go.\par \par \uc2 MASTERS: Absolutely. I want to be the party of low taxes. I like low taxes, absolutely. But the Republican Party cannot just be the party of low taxes, right. If that's all we are, then will lose. What about ESG scores, right? We need to ban those from Fortune 500. We need to de-wokify this country. We need to stop Chinese style social credit systems before it happens here. You need new energy in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 . That's what J.D. represents. That's what I represent. We need a vibe shift. You get us in there, we will materially change how the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  works. And if you're interested in helping, go to BlakeMasters.com.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And Blake, I like the young vibe coming from a lot of you guys. I think we need to mix it up. It's time for this generation to come in.\par \par \uc2 MASTERS: We need it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Blake, great to see you. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 And last night we told you what Vance's win signified, that Americans, especially the burgeoning GOP of today, they do not want war. But some big revelations should have America worried. "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " reported that the U.S. has provided Ukraine with real-time intel that has led to the killings of Russian generals. Just in a few hours, NBC news reported that U.S. intel helped Ukraine sink the Russian flagship Moskva.\par \par \uc2 Here now is \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , former Congresswoman and presidential candidate, lieutenant colonel in the U.S. Army Reserves. Tulsi, the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  says no, that's not true, the intel specifically targeting Russian generals. How dangerous is this American involvement getting?\par \par \uc2 TULSI GABBARD, (D) FORMER HAWAII REPRESENTATIVE: This is just one piece of the larger reality that we, the American people, are facing, which is that the Biden administration has already gotten us into a war with Russia, not just a cold war, but a hot war. And they are using Ukraine as a proxy.\par \par \uc2 We heard Secretary of Defense Austin say the other day very clearly what our goal is. And I'm going to quote him. He said, we want to see "Russia weakened to the degree that it cannot do the kinds of things it's done in invading Ukraine," end of quote. So what does this actually mean on a practical level? It means the United States and \uc2 NATO\uc2  will use economic and military means to decimate Russia's economy and military. That means taking out hundreds of thousands of their troops, tens of thousands of their tanks, their vehicles, their planes, and so forth.\par \par \uc2 And that will be not the end of it, though, because Russia will see this, even if we get close to achieving this, Russia will see this as a threat to their very existence. And they've already said how they would react. They would react with nuclear weapons starting with tactical nukes. And you and I know very well that once the pandora's box is opened of nuclear war, there is no way to close it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Forget about it.\par \par \uc2 GABBARD: That means the American people, the people of Europe, the people of the world, we face destruction because of this nuclear war.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The east coast of the United States threatened. West coast of the United States threatened. It's all threatened under this scenario.\par \par \uc2 Now, I want to listen, Tulsi, and I was watching the other networks today, about how the national security community, ex-CIA, is spinning this "New York Times" reporting. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DAVID PRIESS, FORMER CIA OFFICER: There is an important distinction between giving the Ukrainians information in order to target individual leaders and giving the Ukrainians information that helps them prosecute the conflict which, by nature of conflict, will occasionally include senior commanders who are in the field.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Tulsi, I've heard a lot of parsing of words in the past, but that's pretty much on top of the list.\par \par \uc2 GABBARD: Parsing of words and mumbo-jumbo, really trying to obfuscate, again, what their goal really is. And their goal and what they are doing, the actions and policies we're seeing has put us directly in war with Russia, which the American people don't want. People are struggling. You've talked so much in this show already tonight about how people are struggling all across the country. Higher gas prices, crazy high inflation, high rents, to speak of what the cost and consequences would be to continue to escalate this war with Russia.\par \par \uc2 And that's frankly where I have hope, because the power is in our hands. We have seen now primary elections are going on, the general election will be here very soon. Now's the time for we, the American people, to take a very strong stand for a future of peace and prosperity, and thoroughly reject any Democrat or Republican who will not work toward that future of peace and prosperity, and who will not reject this war with Russia that threatens our very lives and the well-being of our families, our children, and our future.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Tulsi, wonderful to see you. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 We got a clue, tonight's "Wit's End" segment. You love it, admit it. It's going to revealed at the end of the show, the answer. Here it is -- the left is using a best-selling author to salvage their election prospects. So who is it? Tweet me your guesses @IngrahamAngle and we're going to see if you get it right.\par \par \uc2 But up next, we got a lot of reaction to our \uc2 Bill Gates\uc2  versus \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  examination. And wouldn't you know it, ther