s this person who will literally bring home a stranger from the grocery store because she met them and they had nowhere to go and they may move in with us. They may stay for a few meals.\par \par \uc2 I mean, my mom, for her, it wasn't just a Sunday thing. I mean, it was very real. This is every day. This is how we treat people and be humble. You are sinner saved by grace, but thank God. God loves you and accepts you and we're made in His image.\par \par \uc2 And if you view other people that way, I think it gives you a great perspective on just respecting people whether you agree with them or not.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, and you can tell he means it by the way they treat other people and I can affirm you actually mean it. So, I love to see you succeed, and I love to hear you talk about it. Shannon Bream. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Thanks, Tucker. Great to see you.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Great to see you.\par \par \uc2 Well, here's a story you kind of knew you would see. George Gascon, that's the Soros-backed pro criminal prosecutor in LA County who has done so much to wreck our second biggest city -- has decided not to file felony charges against the man who physically assaulted comedian, Dave Chappelle, during a performance at the Hollywood Bowl a couple of nights ago.\par \par \uc2 No. The man is facing a misdemeanor charge for running up on stage at Chappelle with a knife. Oh, why? Why the lenient treatment? Because Dave Chappelle made fun of the trans movement. Try that at a Michelle Obama event and see what happens. Probably not getting a misdemeanor charge, right? You see how it works.\par \par \uc2 We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: That is it for tonight. The Biden administration is giving us so much to worry about existentially as they say, we kind of missed this. F.D.A. issue shocking new warnings associated with vaccine risk. We'll tell you what it means tomorrow night.\par \par \uc2 In the mea