ally smart because there are 13 states right now that if -- if the Alito draft comes to fruition will immediately make abortion illegal or it will go to six weeks and that's fairly making it illegal.\par \par \uc2 Pass something a little more moderate to get it done and that might have some prayer of passing the Senate. So, in the House, have a conversation about a 15-week ban when you're staring at 13 and I think it's 20 states that have these trigger laws.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Right.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Get something done that then you have to put moderate Republicans on the back foot in the Senate to have to come forward and explain why they won't to take this middle ground approach. You're not saying abortion is legal up until nine months. You're saying 15 weeks, same as most of Europe, what the Mississippi laws is, and make them make a decision.\par \par \uc2 So, that's where I think they'd be smart to go, but they will pass something in Congress and then it will fail in the Senate and then we'll be back to square one on this and will continue to be ugly. I think what we saw from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and I don't think that his comment was anywhere near having the impact of the deplorables comment was because talking about MAGA Republicans is separate than talking about Republicans as a whole.\par \par \uc2 He is talking about people that are big Trump supporters and people who had been calling liberals, you know, libtards and people with TDS and crooked Hillary and --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PETE HEGSETH, FOX NEWS HOST: -- when he's got 90 percent support inside the Republican Party?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: That's half the country.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Well, it's 60 million people or 70 million people who voted for him, but it isn't really half the country for (inaudible) -- more people should participate. But there are a lot of people who vote for a person who is on the ballot because they support the policies of the party when they don't really