ople.\par \par \uc2 Because politics is religion for them and as a result, they're going to go the ends always justify the means. And I think in this particular case, they're ramping up the fear because they don't have any alternatives. So, peg the fear meter to max on Roe V. Wade even though everyone knows this is going back to the states. The Congress or the Senate is not going to pass - -\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: But that does mean an abortion ban on a lot of states.\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: And that's what people vote for. They live in those states. They don't believe abortion --\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: You're yelling. No one else is yelling.\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: Okay.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, thank you.\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: That's what people vote for. They vote for representatives who pass laws on their behalf. The closer to the people that government happens, the better off. That's what democracy which the left talks about is always for.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Right.\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: And then they're ramping up the fear on the MAGA crowd. Demonize the opponent and make the opponent the bad guy. Mischaracterize the strawman and hope you can win against and I don't think they can.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, you know, Greg, so it comes to you. I mean there are a couple of issues right now. The president and the left is now trying to convince everyone this is the end of gay marriage, interracial marriage, contraceptive, Loving versus Virginia, Griswold versus Connecticut, all of these states.\par \par \uc2 When the opinion is three separate places says this decision has nothing to do with those other cases. And I could read it. If anyone is interested, they can e-mail me.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS HOST: Well, I mean, they are counting on the fact that no one is going to read it. And the fact is, no one really does except for people like -- you read it. I didn't read it. I trust you though when you talk about it so I know that you're telling the truth.\par \par \uc2 But most people, they are on their phones doing other stuff. They're not going to read it. So when they hear this stuff from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , which made no sense, he combined like three different issues when he was talking about this. It was -- he's such an -- it's actually not -- you don't get mad about it. You kind of get sad because he's an empty vessel, which is why he repeated the slogan.\par \par \uc2 It was like the software was put in, right? They put the MAGA software in and it sputtered and came to life and he got stuck. Maga, maga, maga. Anyway, but this is the latest example of a comment or a smear. Whenever you think about Trump, right, being mean, prone to ridicule or whatever, he always punched up.\par \par \uc2 He went after the media. He went after politicians, celebrities, and even athletes. He never really -- I don't think he ever singled out a Democratic voter or Democratic voters because he wanted them. That's part of the salesman's -- the salesman wants to get everybody. But the Democrats are -- the Democrat leaders not Democrats. But the Democrat leaders punched down and they do it in two ways.\par \par \uc2 They smear millions of people under one thing, whether it's MAGA or deplorables, or they chase an individual down in the media, whether it is for posting a meme or wearing a MAGA hat. Why are you doing this? Why did you say that? That sort of thing.\par \par \uc2 But this is part of a larger trend, which is because the modern woke frames everything as moral or immoral when you are talking about like religion, politics as religion. It's actually a flip from the Republicans of the 80s. The moral majority is now on the left and so there's no room for forgiveness and that's why cancel culture was able to explode without any breaks.\par \par \uc2 You couldn't -- nobody could come (ph) to the breaks because the brakes are forgiveness. So what you're seeing is this incredible flip, which is the Democrats now are less forgiving and more judgmental and the Republicans are the open tent. And you're seeing all of these new and unusual Republicans. Kaitlin Jenner, you're getting people that were normally ex- liberals.\par \par \uc2 And this is an overarching theme if you look at the masks against the unmasked, the denigration of parents, the altar of woke sex ed, the let them eat cake narratives about food shortages and gas prices. There's a disdain for the unwashed masses, and it's always -- what we always thought the country club Republicans were. That was the stereotype. But secretly it's always been the modern regressive left who hates the masses and I think this is part of it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes. Interesting. Coming up next, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's DHS secretary totally clueless on how Scary Poppins got to be the country's disinfo czar.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Beautiful day in New York folks. So the DHS Secretary Mayorkas grilled by senators and kind of revealed that he didn't actually know that much about his newly hired disinformation czar, despite calling her -- he was quite clear that she was eminently qualified. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOSH HAWLEY\uc2  (R-MO): She has for starters consistently misinformed the public about the Hunter Biden laptop story and spread the lie that it was Russian propaganda. Used social media and the public to launder propaganda herself.\par \par \uc2 Were you aware of disinformation when you chose her?\par \par \uc2 ALEJANDRO MAYORKAS, DHS SECRETARY: I was not.\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: How could you not be? Did you do any research on her?\par \par \uc2 SEN. JOHN KENN EDY (R-LA): Was the department aware of her TikTok videos?\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: Senator --\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: They are really quite precocious.\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: Senator, I was not --\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: He got the little Mary Poppins reference there, right? They're really quite precocious. He's so funny, Senator Kennedy. All right, so 20 GOP-led states are threatening to sue over the disinformation board and Republicans making an issue over the lack of vetting for the new disinfo chief.\par \par \uc2 Nina Jankowicz's newly uncovered video shows her dismissing concerns about critical race theory in schools. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 NINA JANKOWICZ, DHS DISINFORMATION CZAR: Critical race theory has become one of those hot button issues that the Republicans and other, you know, disinformers who are engaged in disinformation for profit, frankly. There are plenty of, you know, media outlets that are making money off of this too, have seized on it.\par \par \uc2 It's no different than any of the other hot button issues that, you know, allow disinformation to flourish. It's, you know, weaponizing people's emotion.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes. So you get it, yes. Pete, let me start with you on this. So she's -- what I loved is when she said, if you find yourself getting emotional, there's a good chance that someone is just manipulating you. So, just like cool yourself down and say, you know, I'm just being manipulated. I'm not going to let it happen to me because I know what they're up to.\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: You are right. And the other statement -- the other part of that statement was the Republicans and other disinformers, as if there are other -- we know the Republicans are disinformers and the other ones that disinform too. And all those parents that are protesting at the school board because they really are all in it for the profit.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: This is -- it is a dripping irony of our moment that the person in charge of the governance board on disinformation is herself a disinformant intentionally on one side of the aisle. Mayorkas may not have known exactly what she said but make no doubt about it. The people that hired