ion access.\par \par \uc2 Right now, not enough support for it. But we're also hearing tonight that the White House is going to stand alongside protesters that plan to show up at the justice's houses.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Let's celebrate today.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): As the president celebrates Cinco de Mayo.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I'm glad some woman in this crowd loves me.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Abortion activists are organizing protests at six private residences of Supreme Court justices, all marked on a map published on their website. Calling themselves Ruth Sent Us as a nod to the late Justice Ginsburg. Organizers write, announcing walk-by Wednesday, May 11th 2022. At the homes of the six extremist justices, three in Virginia and three in Maryland. If you'd like to join or lead a peaceful protest, let us know.\par \par \uc2 The group's financial backers are unknown for now. But they are offering to pay people to show up advertising stipends available. A new non scalable fence now surrounding the Supreme Court isn't enough for concerned lawmakers. So, a new bill aims to give the Supreme Court authority to provide around the clock protection to potentially endanger justices.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOHN CORNYN\uc2  (R-TX): This risks violence against members of the Supreme Court and their families.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Democrats are on the same page.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 MARK WARNER\uc2  (D-VA): People should not serve in public life and feel that outrageous extremists on either in the political agenda suddenly have license to physically verbally attack public officials.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Chief Justice Roberts told a group of lawyers in Atlanta. The Roe v. Wade draft may have been leaked by a "bad apple" and called the release "absolutely appalling". Some Democrats agree with them.\par \par \uc2 WARNER: I completely condemned the leak and whoever leaked it, you know, should be 