ilding. And the fury is growing toward President Biden. It is astounding.\par \par \uc2 Now, I don't love drowning you all in numbers. I hate that. But I'm going to make an exception tonight, because it's that important. 66 percent disapproval for Biden's handling of the economy. My question is, who are these 34 percent who approve of it?\par \par \uc2 As for Scranton, Joe's answers for the middle class. Only 36 percent say, he's helping with the middle class. That's down from a whole 5 percent from February. And Americans see what's happening, I think, look at this. They're getting poorer as days go on.\par \par \uc2 They remember how Biden's dim-witted Treasury Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 . Remember, when she just brushed off inflation concerns a year ago. We made a big deal of it here on the 'Angle'. And today, we saw a historic rate hike. A desperate move with terrible consequences for hardworking Americans.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Those interest rate hikes mean it will be more expensive to borrow money. If you're trying to buy a home, experts say, the asking price may not be much higher than it is now. But--\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE SINGLETARY, AUTHOR OF "WHAT TO DO WITH YOUR MONEY WHEN CRISIS HITS": The cost to buy that house has got to be higher, because mortgage rates are going up.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: That means many new homeowners will not only be paying higher interest on their mortgages, but could also get less house for their money.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, great. And if you've built up some credit card debt over the past year.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SINGLETARY: If you've got credit card debt, it's going to cost you more. If you're buying a car, it's going to cost you more because the rates of the - to borrow that money to get that car is going to go up.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, it's infuriating. And just a few years ago, you all remember this. Under Trump, economic optimism, I was looking back in November and December 2019, it was climbing.\par \par \uc2 Young Americans, minorities, women of all backgrounds had record low unemployment. There was rising wages, no inflation, no new wars, cheap gas. And now, everything's going in the wrong direction. And on top of that, everyone's being told, Oh, just lower your expectations.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BRIAN TODD, CNN CORRESPONDENT: What can many of us do to brace for these higher interest rates that are coming? The analysts we spoke to say if you can hold off on that major purchase of a house or a car that you've been thinking about, hold that off for as long as you can.\par \par \uc2 For some, they say, it's time to think outside the box regarding your living situation. Living with relatives or sharing a residence with anyone else. They say they can - that can help you ride out some of these rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, you want to move back home live with mommy and daddy, right? So naturally, this is - in this entire grim environment with a midterm wipe out looming for the Democrats, they're just left to caterwaul from stage left. Fear mongering and lying about the court's draft decision to overturn Roe just like they did during COVID.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. CATHERINE CORTEZ MASTO (D-NV): Make no mistake. This is about controlling women. Far-right politicians are working to restrict all family planning services, denying a whole generation of women the freedom to plan for their future.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now Nevada's \uc2 Cortez Masto\uc2  has no answers on New Mexico's inflation, the illegal immigration issue that's plaguing the state. But she does have talking points from Planned Parenthood. Yay!\par \par \uc2 First, the issue is just returned to the States. Apparently she doesn't understand how to read a legal draft opinion. Second, the congresswoman or Senator thinks so little of women's intelligence that she believes women can only plan pregnancies by aborting their offspring. How insulting!\par \par \uc2 And another effort to change the subject came from the woman who has a heartbeat away from the presidency, yet pretends that liberation is found in stopping the heartbeats of the unborn.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Those Republican leaders who are trying to weaponize the use of the law against women. Well, we say, How dare they? How dare they tell a woman what she can do and cannot do with her own body? How dare they try to deny women their rights and their freedoms?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: She just hopes the prompter doesn't go down. Also, she's just another Democrat who doesn't trust the voters to make decisions for themselves. She'd rather have nine unelected justices make those decisions.\par \par \uc2 Well, until at least the ruling went the other way. Then she's left sputtering inane platitudes about bodily autonomy after she and her party still try to force vaccines on women who didn't want them. None of this, by the way, is principled.\par \par \uc2 But she's so apoplectic about the GOP tsunami that's about to swap them, she's even trying to convince you that the movement that resulted in 50 million babies being aborted is, wait for it, it's patriotic.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: If you stand for freedom, for self determination, for the right to privacy, if you stand for these principles, stand with us. Because you see, women's issues are America's issues.\par \par \uc2 Let us fight for our country, and for the principles upon which it was founded, and let us fight with everything we have got. God bless you, and God bless America.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So now she's saying the principles on which it was founded, the country, included aborting children. No one believes that. It's not going to work.\par \par \uc2 Now, back in the 70s, 80s, even into the 90s, many liberals supported abortion for sure. But now, liberalism is defined by abortion. There are no real pro-life Democrats in Congress and good luck finding one in your friend group.\par \par \uc2 Liberals in 2022 have zero hesitation about things like selling out to China, a dictatorship that brutalizes women who are Uyghurs or Christians, or who - just are women who want to have big families.\par \par \uc2 Liberals in 2022 line up with the Military industrial complex, which wants war with Russia. Liberals in 2022 support restrictions on movement, citing climate change, which is why they love the lockdowns.\par \par \uc2 Liberals in 2022 support restrictions on speech under the bogus rationale of disinformation. And those same liberals who used to be about tolerance, now site hate speech to bar people from speaking in public to be part of public life. Of course, their definition of hate speech is purposely vague. It's always changing.\par \par \uc2 Suffice it to say that, liberals who say things that denigrate entire groups of Americans based on political affiliation, they're never guilty of hate speech. They've evolved and changed and gone 180 liberals have on so many issues, but not on this one.\par \par \uc2 It doesn't matter how much fetal medicine has improved or imaging, or the wide array of birth control that's available, or the number of couples desperate to adopt. Democrats have become abortion fanatics. It's the most important issue among a handful of issues that make up their holy grail of issues. It's a dreary, dark world they're creating. And one where women are the ones who really end up suffering the most.\par \par \uc2 The left's answer to everything is, I don't know, it's kind of summed up by more pot, more porn, more abortions, more sexual identity indoctrination in schools, more racial recriminations, more American traditions trashed, more statues smashed. Their idea of empowerment includes lovely activities like slut walks.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (CROWD SHOUTING IN UNISON)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: One leftist writer in salon recently argued that women's path to happiness means shrugging off prudence and proudly embracing promiscuity.\par \par \uc2 But I think women are onto this game. And they're on to the game that the Democrats have been playing for a while now. Because they feel it they know that life is getting harder for them and their families. And they know who's responsible. They're smart. And as the (ph) WHO sang, they're not going to be fooled again. And that's the 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Amala Ekpunobi, PragerU personality, former left-wing activist; and Ohio Republican congressional primary winner, Madison Gesiotto Gilbert. So wonderful to see both of you tonight.\par \par \uc2 Amala, I'm going to start with you. Why does the left think that it can appeal to women through this one issue which they equate with the, again, the holy grail of freedom is the freedom to abort. Does that work in the end?\par \par \uc2 AMALA EKPUNOBI, PRAGERU PERSONALITY: You know, I think, it's not working on women who are wiser and have a little bit of wisdom and life experience. But unfortunately, as a young person myself, I'm 21. I see it's working with young women.\par \par \uc2 They're selling them on this emotional narrative that is not based in fact, it's not based in science, in convincing them that this lifestyle, that this attitude, that this outlook on life is empowering and something that they should be emboldened to do.\par \par \uc2 And it's not just when it comes to abortion, it's this whole radical feminist movement as a whole. Feminism has accomplished what it has set out to achieve. We are equal. There is no right that men have in this country that I don't have. There's no privilege that they have that I don't have.\par \par \uc2 But now radical feminism, instead of saying, we've accomplished it, let's leave it aside now and morph into something new. Now, we're teaching young women that they don't need love. They don't need protection. They, God forbid, they have a family. In fact, they should just be subservient to corporations their entire life and not strive for anything based in American traditions, or American foundations.\par \par \uc2 And at the end of that, when you're depressed and anxious and sad, you must convince yourself that you've been empowered and that you're happy. It's so unfortunate.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. And obviously, the economic picture that we're looking at across the country that directly affects the women who make a lot of the budget decisions in families, directly affects their choices and their ability to live the free life that they want to live with the money that they normally could make.\par \par \uc2 Now, Madison, I want to remind our viewers who may have forgotten this moment on the 'Angle' four years ago. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You were Miss Ohio for - in Miss USA pageant. And you just took the bar, passed the bar. Congratulations. Awesome.\par \par \uc2 MADISON GESIOTTO GILBERT, MISS OHIO USA 2014: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You're going to go on be a lawyer. And so many people who are in these, pageants, competitions, go on to do incredible things.\par \par \uc2 GILBERT: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You're going to be a huge success. It is great to have you on.\par \par \uc2 GILBERT: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, congrats on the primary win last night. I saw it all those years ago. But why do you think that there is this surge now in young women who are stepping forward in politics to answer, Madison, the Emily's list Planned Parenthood crowd?\par \par \uc2 MADISON GESIOTTO GILBERT, OH PRIMARY WINNER ENDRORSED BY TRUMP: Yes, thank you so much, Laura. And what a great moment from four years ago. I think the reality is that across the country, women are fed up. We're sick of sitting on the sideline and we're sick of us sitting back and watching career politicians destroy our lives.\par \par \uc2 People in my district are fed up. They're feeling the impact of the bad policies coming from Washington of the horrific disaster, that is the Biden administration; of inflation; of the lack of security at our southern border; the drug crisis and opioid epidemic once again coming to the forefront here in Ohio. And of course, on top of all of that, the energy crisis has impacted us greatly.\par \par \uc2 So these are the issues people are talking about on the ground. And here in my district, specifically, I think women are fed up because the left and the mainstream media want people to believe that they know what's best for women, and they're going to tell us what's good for us as if we can't think for ourselves. Very similar to what you and I talked about four years ago when talking about the Miss America Pageant and the misogyny and hypocrisy of it, of them telling women what they should and can do.\par \par \uc2 I mean, we're seeing that right now with what's going on. They want women to be one issue voters. That's not the reality. Women will be turning out as they did last night in incredible numbers for conservatives here in Ohio. And they will be turning out, I think, in very similar numbers in November because of the fact that they have been put in this box by Democrats, who don't believe that they're able or that we're able to speak for ourselves on these issues.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, women are more Democrat than they are Republicans still. Although, the numbers have shifted somewhat. And Ohio has become like a flashpoint for all these issues of globalization and so forth. And especially your district, you ran that race so far, really, really smartly.\par \par \uc2 Amala, Fortune Magazine just published something that I'm so glad they published a shocking article recently about how inflation is hurting women at the grocery store. Some are eating less in order to feed their families.\par \par \uc2 "The food inflation has to be taken into context, said Joel Berg, CEO of Hunger Free America, nonprofit working to end hunger in the United States. About 75 percent of callers in 2021 to the nonprofit's National Hunger Hotline were women."\par \par \uc2 And yet, Amala, the Democrats want to scream like the Elizabeth Warren sending dogs to cover their ears across the country as they're screaming at the Supreme Court that every state is going to outlaw abortion. It's going to be over. You have no rights. All that's a lie, first of all. To let people what think that they're going to be able to survive the way the economy is still going, or have them forget about it.\par \par \uc2 EKPUNOBI: Right. Exactly. Using the problems that they created to galvanize their own arguments, it's really unfortunate. And for people who are watching this, what I will call nothing more than political theater. They should be able to look at them and see that this is all farcical. It's all fake.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren with her perfectly ironed pink suit coming out there and screaming about abortion as if she cares. Guys, your states are going to make these decisions and that'll be more representation for you.\par \par \uc2 And what unfortunately is going to happen is that these leftists are coming in, they're creating this horrific economy, this destabilized country, and they're going to use that as a justification to push forth more abortions and more pro-abortion legislation, because they're going to look at young women and say, Well, in this economy, you're going to want to bring kids?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Right.\par \par \uc2 EKPUNOBI: And God forbid, you even try to buy a house, because the corporations are buying them up. Go ahead and abort that child. That's what they will do.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, it's an economic entity. It's not a human being with a soul. Amala, Madison, great to see both of you.\par \par \uc2 And speaking of Ohio, where Madison just won, Republicans who are eager for war should reflect on J.D. Vance's big Senate primary win last night.\par \par \uc2 Now, for the past few months, his position on the conflict between Russia and Ukraine was tagged as extreme and unpopular by the typical establishment types in the media. But as usual, they were lying to you.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 J.D. VANCE, OHIO SENATE CANDIDATE: It is not America First to give \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  more power. It is not America First to ignore the problems of your own country and to focus instead on Ukraine. And it is not America First to allow our sons and daughters to die in a war that is not in our national interest.\par \par \uc2 Enough with the war mongering, enough with the escalation. Let's focus on our own citizens, our own problems.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Bingo. Republican voters do not want war with Russia. Period. I don't think Democrat voters do either, in general.\par \par \uc2 What they do want is a government focused on helping Americans. That was Trump's whole point. That's why Trump got behind J.D. Vance. Not borrowing untold billions from China and other countries to fight a proxy war against China's ally Russia. Makes no sense.\par \par \uc2 Have you seen the streets of American cities lately? Philadelphia, Baltimore, Chicago, our nation's capital, LA. Instead of cleaning up our own houses, our ruling class is set to approve another $33 billion in aid to Ukraine. How could you ever be against that?\par \par \uc2 Well, let's look at exactly what your hard earned dollars are going to fund in $33 billion. Turns out it's not just bullets and bombs. It gives the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  the authority to put Afghan refugees, including spouses and children on an immediate pathway to citizenship. And one of the most egregious line items, it takes 8.5 billion to fight among other things, disinformation around the globe. What?\par \par \uc2 If you're sure GOP candidates want to win? They need to call this out and they need to call it out now. J.D. Vance could have joined the old guard Republicans and supported unlimited aid to Eastern Europe. But he won by sticking to the American first agenda.\par \par \uc2 All right. And remember, if you can't watch us live, come on, you are going to watch us live. But if you can't, make sure hit that series DVR - series record DVR and you won't miss any episode of the 'Ingraham Angle' every weeknight at 10pm. Have your children do it, if you don't know how to.\par \par \uc2 But up next, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took a wrecking ball to our economy, forced the Fed though to do something it hasn't done now in 20 years.\par \par \uc2 Plus, while the left has made it its mission to destroy \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , why they allowing an actual predatory billionaire to tear this country down? We're going to explain a little later. (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's damage to our economy and American sentiment has been as broad as it is swift.\par \par \uc2 Now, in a new Fox News poll, 77 percent of Americans say the economy is in bad shape. And more than twice as many also say, they are worse off financially than they were two years ago.\par \par \uc2 Now, in response to runaway inflation. Today, the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  took its most aggressive interest rate hike in more than 20 years. Now, despite the reality we all see, just looking at us, the Fed's own version of Baghdad Bob says that, Look, it's all roses and sunshine.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JEROME POWELL\uc2 , FEDERAL RESERVE CHAIRMAN: The economy is doing fairly well. It's - we expect growth to be solid this year. It's a strong economy and nothing about it suggests that it's close to or vulnerable to a recession.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Here now, \uc2 Kevin Hassett\uc2 , former chair of the Council of Economic Advisers and visiting fellow at the \uc2 Hoover Institution\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kevin, you were on last week, I believe, on the show four weeks ago. Yes. Explaining why we were already in a recession. Now, Powell said the economy is strong today. Has anything changed your mind on your analysis of a month ago?\par \par \uc2 KEVIN HASSETT\uc2 , FMR COUNCIL OF ECON ADVISERS CHAIR: Yes, that's right. So we got the report on how GDP is doing, which is the national income and in a recession, it shrinks; and in a boom, it grows. And it was negative 1.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 This is long after you and I talked and I said we're probably in a recession already. And to put that in perspective, I looked back all the way to the Second World War. And 94 percent of the time if you had decline in GDP that large, you were about to have a recession or already in recession.\par \par \uc2 94 percent of the time. And so we've got a number that's so bad that 94 percent of the time it's signaled that we're in a recession or about to enter one. And it's just not responsible, I think, for J, who I like very much. I had lunch with him a lot when I was the chairman of the Council of Economic Advisors. But I think on this one, he's incorrect, or being poorly served by the staff.\par \par \uc2 The fact is that Biden has done and we could go into the details, an enormous amount of damage to the economy. And it's showing up, not only in the inflation numbers, but in the income numbers and the output numbers now too. People aren't even buying these cars anymore, because they just don't have the money.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, the interest rates are going up, cars, houses. It's going to affect us across the board and people would have to borrow.\par \par \uc2 And listen to how the Treasury Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  responded when she was pressed again about inflation.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JANET YELLEN\uc2 , TREASURY SECRETARY: It's the time that President Biden was inaugurated. We had an economy where forecasters were envisioning very high unemployment for a very long time. And you look at the labor market now, and you see the state that it's in. This is really a measure of huge success.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: To call this economy, the economy of this President, a huge success. Is that delusional, or am I missing something here, Kevin?\par \par \uc2 HASSETT: It is. No, no. The thing that she's hiding is that the unemployment rate is very low, but forecasters saw that coming. In fact, you probably heard \uc2 Larry Kudlow\uc2  say far too many times, right. He said it excessively. V-shaped recovery, and that means that we're going right back up, and we did.\par \par \uc2 And so, Biden inherited a V-shaped recovery. The unemployment rate is still low. But the reason is that there's so many people that left the labor force during COVID that haven't gone back in that you don't count as unemployed unless you're looking for a job. And so, the number of people there, the percentage of Americans that actually have jobs is way below where it was before COVID hasn't recovered at all.\par \par \uc2 And that's why there are these, what they call, supply chain disruption. It's because we don't have enough workers to get people the stuff they need.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Kevin, I will take issue with you on that. Because if that was the case, real wages would be going up. Real wages, median wages and income are not going up, not to meet inflation. So if you believe in supply and demand, wages should be up, up.\par \par \uc2 I know a lot of your fancy friends want to keep wages low. We'd like wages going up as they were during your administration.\par \par \uc2 HASSETT: No, I'd like wages going up.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. All right. Well, we agree on that.\par \par \uc2 HASSETT: Yes, but they are declining sharply. You're right. Yes. They are declining sharply right now, real wages.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I just got my economics degree via \uc2 Kevin Hassett\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HASSETT: You did, I know.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It is good to see you. Thanks for your - thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHUCK SCHUMER\uc2  (D-NY): To the American people, I say this. The elections this November will have consequences, because the rights of 100 million women are now on the ballot. To help fight this Court's awful decision, I urge every American to make their voices heard this weekend this year.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Democrats like Schumer, of course, they believe that this big Roe reveal in the leak from the court is kind of just paper over all the destruction they've caused. Supply chain, inflation, wages not keeping up with inflation. But they're wrong and we have the evidence.\par \par \uc2 The day after Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  died, Democratic donors contributed more than 30 million into Democratic campaigns and groups through their chief fundraising arm. And the day after the draft opinion that leaked though, they took in just $9 million.\par \par \uc2 Here now, Arkansas Senator Tom Cotton. Senator, that's one barometer that may be the emotion can't - of the Roe leak can't override the cold hard facts of what's happening to the family budget. You've been on Capitol Hill, you've witnessed the emotional turmoil that they are trying to create. Will this work?\par \par \uc2 SEN. TOM COTTON (R-AR): No, Laura. It won't. They're looking for any harbor in the storm, because they can see how unpopular \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democratic agenda is.\par \par \uc2 First, they're saying that this is going to motivate so many of their far- left progressive voters. Well, what do they think it will do to millions and millions of devout pro-life activists, who have toiled in the vineyards for years to protect innocent unborn children to finally see the fruits of their labor? Our voters are going to be galvanized this fall if this opinion is, in fact, the final decision of the court.\par \par \uc2 Second, for all those people who aren't activist on the issue, what do they think it's going to do when they see just how extreme Democrats have become, supporting late-term, partial birth abortion and other gruesome practices?\par \par \uc2 And then third, as you were saying with \uc2 Kevin Hassett\uc2 , for all voters, of course, they're still the fact that they can't afford gas, or electricity, or food. certainly can't afford to take the kids on summer vacation or put them in summer camp. They see crime in the streets. They see a border in chaos. So the Democrats are still on path to an electoral wipeout this.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Your colleague Joe Manchin, he's always the focus of so much of consternation on both parties, but he said when he was asked if Roe will be the defining issue this November, this is what he said.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. JOE MANCHIN, (D-WV): Inflation is the number one driving factor. I believe in my state right now it's hurting everybody, not just at the pump but at the grocery store, at the drugstore, at the pharmaceutical, everything they do.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The voters of West Virginia are overwhelmingly pro-life, are they not, Senator? He's listening to his constituents. They're watching the bill at the gas pump.\par \par \uc2 COTTON: There's no question about that, Laura. In fact, Joe and I were having a conversation today. We were talking about which state is more pro- life, or who could claim the mantle of most pro-life state in the union? And I think it's a close run thing between Arkansas and West Virginia.\par \par \uc2 And what Joe hears in West Virginia is what I hear all across Arkansas. So many families struggling in the last week of the month to pay the mortgage, to make car payment, to pay bills, to put food on the table, much less to have any extra money left over to save a little bit or to take the kids out to a movie or to go on a summer vacation. And again, that's the main issue. There are other issues as well in addition to rising crime and a border in chaos.\par \par \uc2 And again, if this is the final decision of the court, I think the Democrats will not be able to conceal just how extreme they have become on the issue of abortion in recent years, far beyond where they were, or at least where they said they were for the benefit of public opinion in the Clinton era that abortions should be safe, legal, and rare.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, no, that's way out --\par \par \uc2 COTTON: You couldn't find any Democratic Senators today say it should be rare.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No, they celebrate it in giving a standing ovation in Albany. Remember the New York state legislature celebrating, standing ovation, Ralph Northam. We know the drill.\par \par \uc2 Senator, great to see you tonight.\par \par \uc2 And OK, I've got a clue, tonight's "Wit's End" segment, I know you love the segment now, thank you for tweeting about it. OK, end of the show we'll reveal the answer, but here is the clue -- what group is the American government trying to attract with, well, nude photos? Tweet me your guesses @IngrahamAngle. Don't do research. Guess, and we'll see if you get it right.\par \par \uc2 But up next, the dangers of putting on a show for the \uc2 White House Correspondents\uc2 , wobbly liberators, and even comedians. Raymond Arroyo has it all, "Seen and Unseen" next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's time for our "Seen and Unseen" segment where we explore the cultural stories of the day. And for that we turn to FOX News contributor, Raymond Arroyo. Raymond, this segment is all about the dangers of putting on a show.\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yes, starting with the \uc2 White House Correspondents\uc2 ' dinner, Laura, the annual weekend of journalistic self- congratulation jammed with politicians and assorted celebrities. But it turns out Trevor Noah's comments proved prophetic. Listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TREVOR NOAH, COMEDIAN: Is my great honor to be speaking at this most distinguished super-spreader event. No, for real, people, what we doing here? Let's be honest, what are we doing?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 NOAH: Did none of you learn anything from the gridiron dinner, nothing? Do you read any of your own newspapers?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Apparently not, Laura. CNN is reporting that multiple correspondent dinner attendees from various news operations are testing positive for what "The Daily Mail" describes as a super-spreader. By this is with same-day testing and multiple boosters needed for admission. But the tedious affair revealed more than the participants, I think, imagined. They attempted to pass this nerd prom off as the Oscars on the Potomac.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It's the \uc2 White House Correspondents\uc2 ' dinner, with special appearances by Gayle King, Cecilia Vega, Yamiche Alcindor, the president of United States.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, you can't make this stuff up. Over at CNN they convened what appeared to be the entire \uc2 U.N. Security Council\uc2  to sell this thing, complete with a red carpet reporter. What are they wearing?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I saw Kim Kardashian, Pete Davidson, Caitlyn Jenner was here as well. If you're a fan of "Succession," there was one of the -- I'm blanking on -- Gerri from "Succession."\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Does anyone believe that the people trying to afford gas and put food on the table care if Gerri from "Succession" is dining with these pampered D.C. journalists and politicos? All of whom, by the way, fail people in various ways. They suppress stories they didn't like. They spent like drunken Kardashians. And now we've entered a recession. So why are they congratulating each other, Laura?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All I know is that they are really upset always when a bunch of people gathered in a house of worship or at an SEC football game.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But have we entered a different stage of the pandemic? Is it the end of the pandemic? Or are we just getting going, Raymond? It's always hard to figure it out.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Well, typical of a bad awards show, this \uc2 White House Correspondents\uc2 ' dinner has a lame skit with James Corden and the president. And the president appeared to have no idea who James Corden was. Biden also had no idea that he was reading a joke from the teleprompter.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Just imagine my predecessor came to this dinner this year, now that would really have been a real coup if that occurred.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Little tough, huh?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So sad, so sad.\par \par \uc2 Trevor Noah barely laid a hand on Biden, Raymond. We watched the clips. Though he did make this important observation though.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TREVOR NOAH, COMEDIAN: You guys have integrity. You would never allow personal connections to affect your ability to be good journalists. Isn't that right, Chris Cuomo? Where is Chris, by the way? Is he here?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: He was probably watching at Jeff Zucker's house, Laura.\par \par \uc2 There are a few things Trevor got wrong, however, including who was in attendance. He repeatedly claimed Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  was there. He called DeSantis out. The next day DeSantis held a press conference.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. RON DESANTIS, (R) FLORIDA: I would never attend that. I have no interest in that. So here they are saying how important they are, that they're somehow these paragons of truth. And yet there they are lying about something that is readily verifiable.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: And again, this is why their ratings and trustworthiness among the public, Laura, is at an all-time. Among 46 countries we are the lowest in media trust.\par \par \uc2 Oh, and Trevor Noah recognized you from the podium as well, Laura.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TREVOR NOAH, COMEDIAN: How about that FOX prime time lineup? \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 , Laura Ingraham. Oh, Laura Ingraham, wow.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: OK someone named Matt Gertz from Media Matters tweeted "Laura Ingraham was at the \uc2 White House Correspondents\uc2 ' Dinner." So tell me, Laura, how was the food. Did you see Pete Davidson? What happened?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I was with you and all of our friends at the New Orleans Jazz Fest. There we are.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: This is true.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We had all of our buds. I think that was at The Who, when The Who performed, Roger Daltrey, Pete Townshend, and Ringo Starr's son on the drums. That was actually a fun time, that whole day. I wasn't at the White House.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Unlike this \uc2 White House Correspondents\uc2 ' dinner.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: And Laura, as long as we're talking about dangers of putting on a show, I'm sure Ukraine now feels very safe and secure since the United States has sent its best and brightest to support Zelenskyy.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (MUSIC)\par \par \uc2 VOLODYMYR ZELENSKYY, UKRAINIAN PRESIDENT: Nice to meet you. Thank you for coming.\par \par \uc2 NANCY PELOSI\uc2 , (D-CA) HOUSE SPEAKER: Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Poor \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  can't walk straight, Laura, but she's going to strike fear in the hearts of the Russians? I don't think so. But I'm certain Put is going to pull back those tanks after seeing that Adam Schiff is also on the scene. Ukraine's inflation rate just rose by at least two points, and its borders are probably 50 percent more porous now.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think they should have switched costumes. Zelenskyy should have worn the pantsuit and Nancy should've warned the fatigues. That would have gotten my attention.\par \par \uc2 But what Nancy said to the Ukrainian president I think should give everybody some pause, Raymond.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 NANCY PELOSI\uc2 , (D-CA) HOUSE SPEAKER: Your fight is a fight for everyone, and so our commitment is to be there for you until the fight is done.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Until the fight is done?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, who is she to make that kind of commitment?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Is she the commander in chief? Have they voted on a war resolution, declared war in Congress? I think they haven't done that in what, 75, 78 years.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I guess. We're in until the end.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Raymond, so sad we missed the \uc2 White House Correspondents\uc2 ' dinner.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Not me. Irma Thomas was a lot better.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Irma and Jose Feliciano and The Who and everybody else.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Indeed.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Raymond, great to see you.\par \par \uc2 And while the left spent the last two weeks trashing a billionaire who threatens them, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , they spent the last two years building up one who doesn't even have America's best interest at heart. Up next, we play the revealing take from \uc2 Bill Gates\uc2  whirlwind book tour.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, if you've really been doing your homework over the last few weeks, you know that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is just an evil and destructive billionaire, correct? He's not one of the good guys, no way?\par \par \uc2 Well, "\uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " owner \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  for Democratic megadonor \uc2 George Soros\uc2 , what about them? He's certainly not the man who has risen to progressive sainthood quicker than anyone? The new swingled \uc2 Bill Gates\uc2 . Everyone from NBC to \uc2 PBS\uc2  to "The Daily Show," they've all rolled out the red carpet for Gates and his latest book. What's the topic? Preventing the next pandemic. I have some questions. Why should Americans trust a man who rejected, at times, basic science?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BILL GATES: The kind of polarization and conspiracy theories that are out there and of tearing that fabric of shared trust. Japan is an outlier, partly because of trust. I think their attitude towards mask wearing was kind of a form of politeness. If you're going to be near to someone, even before the pandemic, they had a lot of mask wearing.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And why should Americans trust someone who puts his faith in the CCP over all available evidence?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BILL GATES: Shouldn't we be careful of lab safety? It's quite clear in this case that it came across through animals. And almost all our diseases, Ebola came from bats. This also, with one step in between, came from bats. So it's going to keep happening, particularly with climate change.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That virus wasn't manipulated at all.\par \par \uc2 And finally, why should Americans trust someone who's worried about Musk's plan to increase speech and debate?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BILL GATES: His goals for what it ends up being doesn't match this idea of less extreme falsehood spreading so quickly, weird conspiracy theories, does he share that goal or not?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What goal, Bill? Total unanimity on issues that you and your gatekeepers demand? Musk might be the richest man in the world, but the left and the good billionaires are dead set on making sure he isn't the most powerful. And we should start asking why.\par \par \uc2 Here now is American Majority founder and CEO Ned Ryun. Ned, good to see you. Given all this icky behavior, how in the world has Gates remained in this rarefied air on all the networks?\par \par \uc2 NED RYUN, AMERICAN MAJORITY FOUNDER AND CEO: Because he is a useful billionaire for the left. You've \uc2 George Soros\uc2  who is useful for radical D.A.s being put in a power. \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 , he's useful because he can rig elections. And \uc2 Bill Gates\uc2  is useful on a whole variety of fronts, including some of the leftist goals on reducing world population, among other crazy ideas.\par \par \uc2 But they all seem to forget, as you just mentioned, he is a creep. He was good buddies with Jeffrey Epstein, was on the Lolita express. And he's quite frankly a freak with his eating of bugs and fake meats, and all the other things to in which he's trying to force everybody to get stuck with needles to get a therapeutic shot. And they are forgetting that because he's useful to them.\par \par \uc2 And the amazing part to me about \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is his whole sin, his fault is he had the temerity to stand up and go, you know what, I'm going to buy \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , and I'm going to make it a free speech platform. And all these leftist harpies lose their minds as start screeching about authoritarianism and that the world is ending. And the amazing part to me is Musk is saying I'm not forcing you to do anything I'm not forcing vaccine mandates, I'm not forcing any of this. I'm just proposing that we have free speech, which I think it's great, Laura. I'm all for it. I hope Elon succeeds. I hope he makes it a free speech platform.\par \par \uc2 But the scary part in all of this, I think, in a broader, bigger picture is, how did we get to this place as a country that we hope that a billionaire buys our rights back? And I think that's a really troubling place for us to be as a country.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Ned, speaking of Musk, "The Daily Mail" is reporting that Soros along with Clinton and Obama staffers, European governments, are all behind the anti-Musk campaign. Your response to that?\par \par \uc2 RYUN: What a shock. What a shock. The ruling class and the corporate propagandists and the hold that they want on the narrative to be able to drive the narrative would get blown up completely if Musk is successful in turning \uc2 Twitter\uc2  into a free-speech platform. They want to be able to control.\par \par \uc2 Quite frankly, Laura, the whole mindset of many on the left is the dirty little peasants don't know what's best for them, and we can't let him have the freedom of speech and the free flow of information for fear they might have the wrong idea. And that's why \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is a real threat to them, because of you have the concept of the free flow of information and freedom of speech and all these things, which, by the way, we are guaranteed as a freeborn American people, that's a very threatening idea to the left to these billionaires like Soros and others.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And by the way, every time he is asked, as the \uc2 BBC\uc2 , every time he's asked about are you in favor of tracking people with various technologies? \uc2 Bill Gates\uc2  always kind of laughs it off. He says that's another conspiracy.\par \par \uc2 Thank you, Ned, great to see you.\par \par \uc2 And our "Wit's End" segment is next. What group is the American government trying to attract with nude photos? Hurry up and tweet.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, what government -- what group, excuse me, is the American government trying to attract with nude photos? Tim Cleveland tweeted "\uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 ," how'd cheeky. Rick D. wrote, "The 39 percent that approve of Biden's administration." And Dr. Lisa Carroll guessed "ET and the Terminator."\par \par \uc2 All right, well, the answer is aliens. They're trying to attract aliens in space.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020220505ei5400001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden Attacks "MAGA Crowd"; Democrats Using Abortion To Demonize Republicans; Dave Chappelle Attacked On Stage During Show\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Pete Hegseth, Piers Morgan, Leo Terrell \par \uc2 7,975 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "HANNITY".\par \par \uc2 And tonight, comedian Dave Chappelle under attack. A deranged amateur rapper now charged with assault with a deadly weapon after storming the stage with a gun-shaped knife and lunging at the comedian during a stand-up routine.\par \par \uc2 Now, of course, the incredibly smart and stable ladies of "The View", they knew exactly who to blame. Who do you think? \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WHOOPI GOLDBERG, CO-HOST, "THE VIEW": What do you think is happening? I mean, it's happening on airplanes. It's happening on street corners people are just running. I mean, the Hollywood Bowl. I mean, just ran up on there.\par \par \uc2 JOY BEHAR, CO-HOST, "THE VIEW": Things that could contribute to what's going on, the pandemic, the opioid crisis, the fact that Trump was out there saying uh things like just knock the hell out of them, I promise you I'll pay for the legal fees when he had a heckler.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Okay, good. This is not a political thing. Come on, I know you want to wrap it all into policy, but this is really about security. Like I don't understand --\par \par \uc2 BEHAR: Why? It didn't happen before. It's happening --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Will Smith wasn't particularly right leaning and running up on the stage and smacking Chris Rock --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: No, but I do think that Trump unleashed some incivility at least in our country.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: The noise.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, sadly, Joyless Behar has yet to recover from her very severe case of Trump derangement syndrome. Thankfully, Dave Chappelle, who I think is hilariously funny is okay.\par \par \uc2 However, his attacker is not looking so good. The assailant suffered multiple injuries during the attack, including an arm that looks now totally mangled.\par \par \uc2 Simple lesson in life, if you attack someone, an innocent person, you might want to expect to get the living -- well, Adam Schiff kicked out of you. All right. Coming up, Piers Morgan, we'll get his reaction.\par \par \uc2 Also, DHS Secretary Mayorkas on Capitol Hill again today where he struggled yet again to explain why he hired a far-left activist to police your thoughts and Biden's brand new ministry of truth uh the full low lights, that's coming up straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 But, first, our top story tonight comes to us from the White House apparently our cognitively struggling commander-in-chief thinks that Trump supporters represent the most extreme political faction in American history. And because of them, well, gay kids will soon be banned from going to school. They just make this all up. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: This is about a lot more than abortion. What happens if you have a state change the law saying that that children who are LGBTQ can't be in classrooms with other children? Is that -- is that legit under the way the decision is written? What are the next things that are going to be attacked? Because this MAGA crowd is really the most extreme political organization that's existed in American history.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: In American history, okay, we'll deal with that in a minute. Obviously, that's a predictable Democratic lie.\par \par \uc2 We used to get it every two years, four years, Republicans, racist, sexist, misogynist, homophobic, xenophobic, transphobic, you know the routine. But remember, Obama said those people in Pennsylvania, the bitter ones that cling to their God, their guns, their bible, religion, or as Hillary called -- while half the country a basket of deplorables, or as \uc2 FBI\uc2  agent Peter Strzok once referred to conservatives as Trump supporting smelly \uc2 Walmart\uc2  shoppers.\par \par \uc2 Now, according to Biden, 76 million Americans are the most extreme political faction in history? Half the country, Joe?\par \par \uc2 Now, of course, everything Biden just said is a simple disgusting political scare tactic. No 