illions of property damage. These were violent demonstrations -- by the way, that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  publicly supported.\par \par \uc2 Like she supported the bail fund, like she supported defunding the LAPD. The message was clear give us what we want or we're just going to keep burning the neighborhood to the ground.\par \par \uc2 Here's a question by the way, where's that congressional committee looking into the 574 riots? I guess if a riot doesn't impact politicians, I guess they don't care about those rights. They only impact we, the people. Now, Democrats are yearning for a similar call to action ahead of the midterms.\par \par \uc2 Now, let me tell you what we're not going to do on this show. We are not going to take the bait. Most Americans have made up their mind as it relates to abortion. Sixty-seven percent of Americans, according to Gallup, they support restrictions on abortion. I know some radical Democrats they believe, in fact, that you can have an abortion up until the moment before birth. That obviously is infanticide.\par \par \uc2 And then, of course, you have Ralph Northam that says you can have an abortion even after birth. How insane was that statement?\par \par \uc2 Now, this week, a mob of far left agitators, they're answering the call once again taking to the streets with fresh new protests, including one in Los Angeles that in fact did turn violent.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, I have bad news for Democrats, you're going to try to distract the entire country and think that this is the one issue that will save you in 2022, it will not. Time will pass, reality will set in, and the American people will realize even if Roe v. Wade is overturned, abortion will be legal in America in most other places.\par \par \uc2 Now, by the way, if it is overturned, abortion will still be totally legal in most every state. Abortion access will exist for every American.\par \par \uc2 So the question is, why are they demagoguing the issue and lying to you, the American people? Because every one of their policies have failed. That's the distraction.\par \par \uc2 Now, is it an important issue? Yeah. Do people have strong passionate views on it? Yes. Will abortion still be legal in America? Yes. States like New York, California, they'll have the most liberal laws.\par \par \uc2 And while the American people are evenly divided on the issue of abortion, the vast majority of Americans are deeply worried about other things, you know, the economy, 40-year high of inflation, highest gas prices we've ever paid, high prices, the highest we paid for everything we buy in every store we go to, the disaster in Afghanistan, the war in Europe, the crisis at our southern border, poor leadership in D.C.\par \par \uc2 Now, these are issues that directly impact every American every single day. And, by the way, they know who to blame. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is an unmitigated disaster and every poll shows it.\par \par \uc2 So, all Democrats the media mob, they want to inflame your emotions. They want you to focus on only one topic. They don't want to talk about any of the failures of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . As a matter of fact, the mob and the media, they cover for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They'll tell you that the world is coming to an end, it's not true. They'll try to use abortion as a political wedge and lie to you, and then you'll realize -- oh, abortion is still legal. The states decide.\par \par \uc2 We will tell you the cold hard truths, separate fact from fiction. We'll bring you the facts and we will cover all of the issues that impact you the American people day in and day out.\par \par \uc2 The left has lost touch with reality. They have no good story to tell. Obama Hillary, you just need to tell your story. They don't have a story to tell, unless they make one up.\par \par \uc2 There's only one way to bring them back to earth and that's for you, the American people to show up at the polls, vote them out of office in six months. If you've not registered, I strongly suggest you do it now, because in these six months, we are now facing a very pivotal inflection point in this country, a pivotal election. A turning point election.\par \par \uc2 Now get this: right now, as of tonight, every single candidate that President Trump has endorsed in a primary -- oh, look at his record, 55-0. Wow.\par \par \uc2 Here with more, the founder of Outkick, we have Clay Travis with us. Along with the author of the big new book, "Battle for the American Mind: Uprooting a Century of Miseducation," "FOX and Friends Weekend" co-host Pete Hegseth.\par \par \uc2 Pete, first, congratulations on the book. \uc2 Amazon.com\uc2 , we'll throw it up, on hannity.com.\par \par \uc2 But if you look at this one issue, I understand why Democrats are doing what they're doing. There are all these other issues they don't want to talk about. So, Roe v. Wade, if it does go away, the states will decide what the laws will be and I doubt if any states will totally completely outlaw abortion. I don't think that's going to happen.\par \par \uc2 And if they did, people would have access in neighboring states, New York, California, or anywhere else they wanted to go. Is that correct?\par \par \uc2 PETE HEGSETH, CO-HOST OF "FOX & FRIENDS WEEKEND": Correct. This is -- the far left extremist ship is sinking, with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the helm. They know it. On every issue you just laid out, Sean, they believe that this criminal leak of a potential draft of a Supreme Court decision is their life raft, and they are clinging to it and screaming from the hilltops.\par \par \uc2 They just declared that you, me, I don't want to speak for Clay but I presume Clay, and everyone else who has supported the policies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or believed in America First is the most extreme movement in American history. They have pegged and maxed their rhetorical response.\par \par \uc2 And as you pointed out from the bitter clingers of \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , to the basket of deplorables to \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , that type of demagoguery doesn't work politically as well.\par \par \uc2 And to hear \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  say, how dare you, all I think that does is make voters say where's that passion on any other single issue? And it only reminds voters in the electorate that the only thing they care about is aborting babies or children as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  admitted, as opposed to addressing things that are crushing the American people right now.\par \par \uc2 So it shows the left for the extremists that they are and I don't think it will be effective, but it's tragic. Here we are demonizing the president one side of the political aisle effectively is terrorists.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I think what this is going to come down to -- look, I'm pro-life, Clay. I do make exceptions some of my friends disagree with me. Rape, incest, the mother's life. There are other people that I know in my life that I respect their opinion, they say they're pro-choice but they always will say that abortion should be rare and it should be first trimester.\par \par \uc2 What has happened with the Democratic Party in in many of these blue states I listed them last night, they actually allow abortion up to the moment of birth and then, of course, Ralph Northam's comments post-birth abortion, which is murder. And I think they've gone so hardcore radical on this issue, they're the ones out of touch because 67 percent of Americans think it should be legal but there should be restrictions like, for example, Mississippi saying 15 weeks max. What are your thoughts?\par \par \uc2 CLAY TRAVIS, OUTKICK FOUNDER: I agree with the vast majority of the American public and with a lot of what you just said, Sean, and notice what's going on here. The Democrat Party which has spent basically a year and a half, all of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's administration, arguing that democracy is under siege is now outraged that nine unelected justices are poised to