clashing with the \uc2 LAPD\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Police say a group there threw rocks and bottles at the officers and one cop was injured. Top Democrats echoing the fury coming from the base.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. ELIZABETH WARREN (D-MA): I am angry the (Inaudible) the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2  thinks that they can impose their extremist views on all of the women of this country and they are wrong. How dare they try to stop us from determining her own future?\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: How dare they, how dare they try to stop her from determining her own future. How dare they try to deny women their rights and their freedoms?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: President Biden adding fuel to the fire earlier and lobbying some serious attacks at Republicans.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: This is about a lot more than abortion. What happens if you have states change the laws saying that children who are LGBTQ camping classrooms with other children? Is that legit under the way that the decision is written? What are the next things that are going to be attacked? Because this MAGA crowd is really the most extreme political organization that has existed in American history.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Judge, I do want to start with that. Because there's this idea that the left is pushing less than 24 hours after this leak that the Supreme Court, next they are going to ban interracial marriage, which would be very strange for \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to do, I have to say.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: Yes, I agree with this. Look, according to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Dems the sky is falling. I mean, this is like for them the worst thing -- they can predict anything will happen and they will use this as a reason to fire up the base because they have nothing going for them in the midterms.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake, Griswold versus Connecticut, Loving versus Virginia, all of those other cases, Alito was very clear in the decision. Quote, "we emphasize that our decision concerns the constitutional right to abortion and no other right, nothing in this opinion should be understood to cast out on other precedents that do not concern abortion."\par \par \uc2 He makes it specific this is about abortion. And in addition, some of those other rights are based on equal protection. Civil rights, not necessarily on the right to privacy. So, that should all be removed from the discussion of this case.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Geraldo, we haven't had a chance to hear from you on this -- on the show this week, let's give you the floor.\par \par \uc2 GERALDO RIVERA, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: I think that first of all, Republicans make a mistake when they emphasized the crime of the leak itself over the impact of what the decision would entail for the women. And I think that emotion, however you think of those particular personalities, that is -- that is legitimate.\par \par \uc2 This is more problematic I think, and Judge, I think you would agree with me, what this shows because it goes both ways. What this shows is that the Senate confirmation process by which a nominee is interrogated by both parties and give their reasons why they are fit to be on the high court, is absolutely deeply flawed. Why? Because these nominees lied.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Whoa.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: They go before the \uc2 Senate of the United States\uc2 , they swear that they are going to be judicious and good, you know, shepherds of the court and its impartiality and the importance that it has in the American society, and that the stare decisis that the precedent of these cases well established.\par \par \uc2 Thirty years, 40 years, 49 years, that that is something that the Supreme Court honors. And then they turn around the minute they get in the high court they make a decision that is so dramatically opposed to what they said during the confirmation hearings, shame on them. Shame on Gorsuch, same on Coney Barrett, shame on Kavanaugh.\par \par \uc2 They knew when they were swearing to those senators or in the conversations in the Senate offices that they were going to vote to reverse, or overturn Roe v. Wade. They knew it and they lied about it. I don't know how you fix that. I don't know how you can repair when the most sacred office in the land, the high court of the United States, is peopled by politicians.\par \par \uc2 JOEY JONES, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: You know, if I was accused of being a serial rapist because I like beer at 16, I would probably say whatever I needed to get the hell out of that building.\par \par \uc2 I agree with that, Joey.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 JONES: Shame on --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Let me -- let me -- let me disagree. Because you said that I would agree with you. I absolutely do not agree with you. There was no lying to the -- to the Senate on -- to that judiciary committee. Because they talked about stare decisis. Stare decisis means that you follow precedent.\par \par \uc2 They were cleared to say this is not one of those super due process cases like Board versus -- Brown versus Board of Education that overturned Plessy versus Ferguson separate but equal.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK. They were very clear, especially Amy Coney Barrett. She was very clear to say stare decisis means that the courts under us have to respect our decision as a Supreme Court, the highest court in the land. And unless it's super due process, unless it's like Brown versus Board of Education where you cannot separate white and black children, then we can decide based upon what comes before us what we can do. They did not lie.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I have three boarders in the state of Ohio.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: It's the fetal heartbeat law that will now be in that place.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: That's a different issue.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: It will now be the law of the state of Ohio. And what am I going to tell my daughters now? That they don't have control over their body? That they can't make those choices for themselves? That's some old man scratching his belly and some other state is going to say that --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: That's not --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Amy Coney Barrett is not an old man scratching her belly.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes. I want to play --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: Seven old men did the Roe v. Wade decision in --\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes, yes. Let's listen to some media responses to all of this if we could please.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: The founding fathers didn't recognized abortion as a fundamental right because the founding fathers were racist misogynistic jerk faces. So that's the history that \uc2 Sam Alito\uc2  is accessing.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Honestly, at this point, I think we're all right to question the legitimacy of the court.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Mass criminalization event.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: No one is saying this overturning Roe will be a mass criminalization event.\par \par \uc2 JOY BEHAR, CO-HOST, ABC: So, don't think this is just a war on women. It could be a war on people of color, and gay people.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: What? All right, Greg, do you want to take that one?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes. I mean, we were talking about this, I think before the show yesterday at the break. But this is why pro-lifers win, because they can state their case so plainly.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You ask somebody why they are pro-life they will say because abortion takes a life and we believe life is sacred. You could disagree with that, but you cannot disagree with the simplicity of it. Right? But the problem with the pro-choicers is that they don't have the balls to state their case plainly.\par \par \uc2 Just say, like I prefer freedom over fetuses. Don't sit here and come up with all of these other things like it's going to be interracial marriage next.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: My body my choice, how much simpler can you get?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Let me finish. You already did your ad hominem. People we were talking --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Ad hominem? That was not.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: We were talking about this. Yes, you insulted a few people there. We talked about this. People are more concerned about what they lose than what they will gain because you don't have to imagine loss. All you got to do is talk to somebody who lost a child. But you can't -- it's -- you don't have to imagine it, and it's there forever.\par \par \uc2 A pro-choice mom can look at her adorable 2-year-old and think my life would be nothing without her in 2022. In 2017, when she was young and single didn't have a kid, she can only imagine the loss of her freedom, right? So that's the issue.\par \par \uc2 The issue here is that people need to imagine, right, they can't step back and see how pro-choice arguments are driven by refusal to imagine what that baby could be. But then when that baby bees, then suddenly it changes, right? And then they have to create reasons, they have to crate all of these reasons to be pro-choice. Rather than just be honest and say, yes, it kills an unborn kid but I prefer my freedom. That's all you have to say. You'll get so much more respect.\par \par \uc2 The other thing that drives me crazy now that I'm on my soapbox is it used to be, even the pro-choicers would admit that abortion was an ugly thing. But they felt like it had to be a necessary evil, something that would be safe and rare. That was the argument you always heard.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: But now when you go anywhere on social media it's something to celebrate, to cherish. The unborn --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: To shout.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: To shout.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: That's baloney.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: That's baloney.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I'll give you evidence.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Cherish the wire hangers stuck up their private --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Come on.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Trying to get what?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: The unborn child --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: What come on?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: The unborn child becomes --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: What come on? That's the -- the world made before Roe.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: This is exactly what I expected. Bring out the old coat hanger.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: You are arrogant.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Go for it, Geraldo. Come on, keep going.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: OK, Joey, on this --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You are making a fool of yourself.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Don't you -- you know something? You insulting punk?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: What am I, your new Bongino?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Joey, go. Joey, go.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: If you want that role.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Joey, you sat yourself patiently, Joey.\par \par \uc2 JONES: All right. Hey, listen, listen. I don't have anything important to say but I know it's more important (Inaudible) to sit right Geraldo.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK.\par \par \uc2 JONES: All right, listen, the original -- the original court case, what makes it -- what a lot of people don't understand is under the premise of privacy the Supreme Court went and not only did they say abortion is legal but they sent out all of these arbitrary boundaries of the first trimester always, the second trimester sometimes, the third trimester never.\par \par \uc2 Casey comes along and almost negates that entire decision but saying nope, it's about viability. Why? Because they try to bring some science into the equation that didn't -- maybe didn't exist or wasn't coming.\par \par \uc2 The point is the Supreme Court doesn't have the authority or even the understanding to create law and regulation because in doing all of this what are they saying? They are saying you should be able to have the privacy to make this decision with your doctor.\par \par \uc2 But that is a baby and we are supposed to protect it with constitutional rights at some point along the way, we just don't know what the some point along the way is. And you can sit here and not have to have a law degree or be an accomplished judge as an American citizen to say OK, yes, maybe that law back then really didn't do it right. Maybe we need something different. Or actually it wasn't a law, it was a Supreme Court decision that's the problem.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: They did that -- they did that with gay marriage.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I just want to say one thing, the Supreme Court came down in this decision. If it is ultimately a final decision and said it is not a constitutional right --\par \par \uc2 JONES: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: -- based on all the reasons I went to yesterday. They didn't say that it was illegal, they said we are going to give it to the people.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Yes. And they didn't say we are going to pass federal legislation - -\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You decide. You and Congress can decide, you and the states decide.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And the one thing we haven't brought up here and we're going to tease right after I make one small point here, is about the science. About all the things that we have learned about fetal pain, fetal heartbeats, --\par \par \uc2 JONES: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: -- and the things that are informing people's decisions. The sonogram that you see, the pictures that you put on the refrigerator, and that love that you have of the baby from the birthday.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Everyone is somewhere between conception and consciousness. Everybody on this issue believes there is a point on that line that I care to hear from. Because if you don't --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I agree there.\par \par \uc2 JONES: -- once you become -- once you become a parent, your -- what you want doesn't matter anymore.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Your job is to take care of the child. That I do believe.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Joey, you're the best. Our Georgia pitch.\par \par \uc2 All right. Ahead, President Biden boasting about the economy while trying to pin his bad poll numbers on Republicans.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: President Biden boasting about an economy most Americans are losing sleep-over and trying to blame everything that's gone to hell on Republicans. The president bombing on almost every issue in a new Fox poll. He's underwater on climate, Russia, the economy, guns, crime, immigration, and inflation.\par \par \uc2 And speaking of inflation, Biden didn't say much about it, only mentioning it a couple of times.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Let me tell you about this ultra MAGA agenda. It's extreme, as most MAGA things are. It will actually raise taxes on 75 million American families. Over 95 percent of whom makes less than $100,000 a year. There is no reason why a billionaire should be paying a lower tax rate than a teacher or a firefighter.\par \par \uc2 That's a sharp contrast to what today's Republican Party is offering. I don't want to hear Republicans talk about deficits and their ultra MAGA agenda. I want to hear about fairness, I want to hear about decency. I want to hear about --\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: All right. So, he's talking -- he believes his plan is rooted in fairness and decency, Dana. Has he gone outside? With everything that has come from this administration, from debt forgiveness to anti-cop mentalities, the pro-crime, it's unfair and indecent.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And every time he said the ultras MAGA agenda.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: You know, like that was like the poll tested phrase, he must've done very well in the focus group so you are going to hear it a lot. We'll see if they get better at delivering that message.\par \par \uc2 When Biden talks about the economy you can't help to think of the things that he inherited.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I mean, he inherited about getting a million vaccines out the door a week that was pretty good. You had the economy, it was a much better shape. You didn't need the build back or the American Rescue Plan, --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Right.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: -- which poured gasoline on the fire of inflation. And so, I think -- I think it's curious that he decided to go after the Republicans on this and not the Fed. Because you can actually go after the Fed and say they made bad decisions on inflation and I wish they would've done a better job. That is a punching bag that would make sense.\par \par \uc2 Now, what he's talking about there in terms of Republicans wanting to raise taxes, this was the whole dustup between Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  who put forth an agenda and Senator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  who said are you out of your mind. And, you know, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  and the rest of the conference was like what are you doing? \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  is stuck to his guns, and so this is exactly why.\par \par \uc2 However, I think most people out there are going to say OK, I've never heard of \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  and I don't hear any other Republican talking about this.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: What are you going to do about gas and groceries?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes. Exactly. Joey, so they used this phrase ultra MAGA, which I guess the new phrase for extreme. So, what is the extreme agenda if it's protecting your families from violent crime and being able to afford food and fuel while Joe has been embracing an extreme wokeism that allowed all this decline to take place?\par \par \uc2 JONES: Well, to people that partake in MAGA, MAGA means America first. But the people in the left it means white supremacy.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JONES: That's how far off they are from understanding. And also, if ultra MAGA was focus group that wasn't there to back a lobby because it doesn't sound like let me get a pack of those ultra MAGA 100s?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Different --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 JONES: Maybe that's a -- maybe that's a red neck to me that that's what I think about it, but that's all I hear. You know, but you're talking about a guy that stands there and he speaks with such conviction over an economy that this week all he wants to brag about is his ability to lower the deficit that was raised by $2.3 trillion because of COVID.\par \par \uc2 So, you know, here a trillion dollar that goes up to three and a half and it slowly come down the last two years. I mean, for God sakes, don't you think it should?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JONES: We spent what, 3 or $4 trillion in a year because of a pandemic that shut our economy down, but all he asked to brag about in the economy is the fact that he hasn't continued to spend as much as money as we spent in 2020, that's all he has to brag about this week. So of course, he's going to use words like ultra MAGA agenda, because if you use the numbers he'd be raked over the coals.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes. You know, Judge, my little conspiracy voice inside me says that this is why the Supreme Court story dropped at this time because they needed this amount -- this many weeks and months to kind of push the stuff away.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Because it's all bad news.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, I said yesterday there's no question.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I mean, the bloodbath that's predicted in November this gives them something to gin up the base and to raise a lot of money. But you know what's so incredible about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  talking about ultra MAGA, we've got the fastest phase inflation that this country has seen in over 40 years.\par \par \uc2 Eighty-seven percent of Americans are concerned about the future of this country and inflation. Biden has the lowest job rating as it relates to inflation and this country. And what's amazing is this is Biden's fault. Because on the one hand if he opened up drilling, and if he opened up North American energy between Canada, the United States, and Mexico we would be able to drill something like two million gallons a day for a hundred years. I got that from John Catsimatidis whose an oil gut. OK?\par \par \uc2 And now they are going to destroy the real estate market because they are now going to raise the interest rate, which is going to destroy the building of homes. Everything is going to hell in a handbasket with this guy. So, he's going to blame it on Republicans when Americans know it's him. He is a loser.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Geraldo, is he going to run in 2024? People are saying he probably won't.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Great question, I don't know the answer. I would imagine it depends on his health as we get closer to it. I just want to quickly say it's not all horrible news. The market was up over 900 points today. The deficit will go down by 1.5 trillion this quarter, that's good news.\par \par \uc2 But inflation there is no doubt, I have a very big family. You know, some are more needy than others. And everybody is feeling the squeeze right now. Everyone is feeling the pinch. Inflation is real and it is a cancer on the economy.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Up next, America first candidates racking up huge wins last night as the far-left crashes and it burns.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 P