a self-serving far left court employee who perhaps is attempting to coerce the court's decision or maybe make the case for court packing. Whatever the case may be, we'll find out, hopefully sooner than later.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice Roberts called the leak a, quote, a singular and egregious breach of that trust that is an affront to the court. He continued: To the extent this betrayal of the confidences of the court was intended to undermine the integrity of our operations. It will not succeed. The work of the court will not be affected in any way.\par \par \uc2 Good answer from him.\par \par \uc2 Now, an investigation is underway to identify the leaker and by the way bring this perpetrator to justice. But make no mistake: if Justice Alito's decision stands and Roe v. Wade is, in fact, overturned let me also separate again fact from fiction, abortion in America does not become illegal, instead, individual states state legislators they and the voters, of course, you will decide the rules and regulations regarding abortion.\par \par \uc2 And right now, by the way, views on abortion are split right down the middle. Look at this Gallup, 49 percent of Americans consider themselves pro-choice, 47 percent of Americans are pro-life. The same poll actually showed that only 32 percent believe abortion should be legal under any circumstance.\par \par \uc2 And meanwhile, an "AP" poll found a whopping 80 percent of Americans think that abortion should be illegal in the third trimester. As it now stands, 16 states and the District of Columbia have laws protecting or even codifying abortion, with many of these states even allowing a woman to terminate a pregnancy in the third trimester.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, at that late stage, you're talking about a viable fetus, especially if we're following science, a child that can live outside the womb of a mother. In California, New York, for example, many other states, abortion is allowed in almost every scenario so long as a liberal pro- abortion doctor signs off on it.\par \par \uc2 And meanwhile, Oregon, Vermont, New Jersey, Colorado, they guarantee abortion rights at any point during the pregnancy up until the very moment of birth. Now, that's called infanticide. That would be the killing of a child, an innocent child.\par \par \uc2 Now, it's insane how radical the left has now come that they would support such evil and brutality but they do. In fact some Democrats have become so radical that even, believe it or not, post birth abortion infanticide is apparently on the table. Now, you might remember this from former Virginia Governor Ralph Northam. Remember this, it went viral.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 FORMER GOV. RALPH NORTHAM (D-VA): Third trimester abortions, these are done with the consent of obviously the mother, with the consent of the physicians, more than one physician by the way, and it's done in cases where there may be severe deformities or may be a fetus is non-viable. So, in this particular example, if a mother is in labor, I can tell you exactly what would happen. The infant would be delivered. The infant would be kept comfortable. The infant would be resuscitated if that's what the mother and the family desired. And then a discussion would ensue between the physicians and the mother.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, that a discussion will ensue? No, I don't think so. That would be called murder, Ralph.\par \par \uc2 Now, of course, infanticide is illegal. But even if Roe versus Wade gets tossed out, abortion even later term abortion will still be legal in many states across the country. Now, how that practice is legal anywhere should shock the conscience of any human being, anybody with a soul.\par \par \uc2 According to Democrats, Hollywood, the media mob, all speak in one voice, this ruling spells the end of America as we know it. It does not. They are either completely dumb, ignorant or stupid, or they're just playing politics, probably a combination of both.\par \par \uc2 And after returning home from the Met Gala, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  proclaimed the court's ruling would kill and subjugate women, another complete lie. And one C-list actress referred to Supreme Court justices as drunk rapists and Nazis. Yeah, that's an obvious lie, too. Cher had a full-blown, all-caps meltdown and breakdown on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fang-Fang's boyfriend \uc2 Eric Swalwell\uc2  tweeted that the court's decision was really about Republicans wanting to ban interracial marriage. He's clearly not well. And, Eric, I think Clarence and Jenny Thomas would like a word about that.\par \par \uc2 And not to be outdone, Elizabeth Warren was spotted tromping all over town screaming at the top of her lungs. Take a look at this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. ELIZABETH WARREN (D-MA): This is what the Republicans have been working toward this day for decades. They have been out there plotting, carefully cultivating these Supreme Court justices so they could have a majority on the bench who would accomplish something that the majority of Americans do not want. We have a right. Extremists, we've heard enough from the extremists and we're going to --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And per usual, the insanity was even far worse from Chuckie Schumer and his friends on MSDNC, fake news CNN. Take a look, the predictable predictions of doom and gloom.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHUCK SCHUMER\uc2  (D-NY): The decision would be an abomination, an abomination, one of the worst ever in modern history.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Honestly, I want to cry. You know, I want to cry in so many different ways.\par \par \uc2 WARREN: Look, I feel really angry about this and what I feel angry about is that an extremist Supreme Court is going to impose their views on the rest of America.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEM