t babies. This is insanity.\par \par \uc2 Now as for the truth, as for this thing they want to set up the ministry of truth, we have a First Amendment they ought to abide by that. That's actually in the Constitution. We need ministry of truth against the government. It used to be called a free press.\par \par \uc2 We don't have a free press. They're utterly and completely corrupt. They're in the back pocket of the Democrat Party in this American Marxist movement. If we had a free press, that would be the ministry of truth, but they're all corrupt for the most part. That's it!\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're supposed to say that's it, I'm done. What happened to the "I'm done" part?\par \par \uc2 Anyway, that's why we call you the great one, the great one Mark Levin. All right. "Life, \uc2 Liberty\uc2  and Levin", Sunday night right here on Fox, don't miss it.\par \par \uc2 Newt Gingrich is next and if you haven't heard, JD Vance is the winner in the Senate primary Senate race. More details coming up.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And this is a FOX News alert, the "AP" is now projecting that JD Vance has won the Ohio GOP primary Senate race.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now with reaction, former speaker of the House, Newt Gingrich.\par \par \uc2 He was in the single digits, Mr. Speaker, and then somebody by the name of \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  endorsed him and here he is with a significant win tonight, along with I think 11 other candidates that look like endorsed by Trump that are going to win as well. What does that tell you?\par \par \uc2 NEWT GINGRICH, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, first of all, I want to watch the national media which had set this up as the big test. You know, did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  really have any stroke left or was he no longer capable of doing anything?\par \par \uc2 But I also think it's an important comment about JD Vance. This is a different Republican Party. JD Vance's background having written a book about his childhood, having grown up intimately aware of Appalachia, of the Ohio River Valley, of blue-collar workers, of local small farmers, this is a guy who is going to bring on the one hand a tremendous intellectual and artistic capability, on the other hand, a real down-home grassroots populism and he is going to I think be an enormous breath of fresh air in the Congress.\par \par \uc2 And I think combined with people like \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , you're going to see a very different Republican Senate next year. But it's certainly from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's standpoint, an enormously big win not just JD Vance, but as you point out, I think nine of the eleven people he's endorsed have already won. And the other two I think are still being counted.\par \par \uc2 To do that in Ohio --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It looks like they're going to win -- it looks like --\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: -- is enormous statement.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It looks like Trump will have a perfect night in Ohio tonight.\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Well, if that happens, look, I think we have a lot of great candidates. I personally think \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has a tremendous future as an example or somebody like \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , a number of governors around the country. But the truth is, if Trump retains his hold on the base of the Republican Party that he currently has and particularly if he starts shifting towards describing a better future, I think that he will consolidate and almost certainly end up as the nominee.\par \par \uc2 Tonight's a very big night in terms of 2024 as well as in terms of 2022, and it fits what we're saying. The fact is inflation matters, collapse at the border matters, crime matters, high prices for gasoline and food matters -- and in the middle of all this, the corruption of the Biden family matters.\par \par \uc2 And you know, I think the Democrats are going to discover that the January 6 Committee doesn't matter to most Americans and they're going to discover that a hard-line pro-abortion extremism doesn't appeal to most Americans, in fact will accelerate their loss of African-American and Latino voters who are culturally conservative.\par \par \uc2 So you're in the middle of a genuine revolution. Ohio is one of the places reminding us that in the real world, outside of Washington and the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and the big networks in the real world, that revolution is still underway.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Mr. Speaker, stay with us. Let's dip in this is JD Vance now who has just been declared the winner in the Ohio Republican Senate primary endorsed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , winning by a pretty significant margin based on our numbers. Let's step in and hear him.\par \par \uc2 JD VANCE (R-OH), U.S. SENATE CANDIDATE: -- loyalty, and this team has been loyal to me through good times and bad, when things were rough, when things were good we didn't have leaks in this campaign. We didn't have people stabbing each other in the back. We were a team and we will be a team all the way to November.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERS)\par \par \uc2 I have absolutely got to thank the 45th -- the president of the United States, \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 , ladies and gentlemen, one, for giving us example of what could be in this country, ladies and gentlemen. Remember in 2019 when wages were going up and not down, remember in 2019 when workers were doing well in this country, not struggling terribly, thanks to the president for everything, for endorsing me.\par \par \uc2 And I got to say, a lot of the fake news media out there and there are some good ones in the back there, there's some bad ones, too, let's be honest, but they wanted to write a story that this campaign would be the death of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's America First agenda. Ladies and gentlemen, it ain't the death of the America First agenda.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERS)\par \par \uc2 It wasn't just the president. Of course, we had a lot of endorsements, especially some of our early endorsements, I want to make sure I give some shout outs to Penny Nance, a great advocate for life and for people all across the country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, let me go back to Speaker of the House Newt Gingrich, former speaker, you know he said something there that I think is extremely relevant. I do believe the damage that has been caused in just a short period of time, everything from inflation, to high gas prices, to open borders, law and order, safety and security, even running out of COVID tests, Afghanistan, it's been a disaster.\par \par \uc2 I do believe that -- my feeling is the America First, Make America Great Again, now Save America Agenda is going to be what propels the Republicans to victory both in '22 and `24. It's a hope, it's a prayer because the country needs to change directions quickly.\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Look, I think that's right, and I just talked as recently as yesterday with Kevin McCarthy, who is really leading a remarkable effort in the House, to develop a very positive agenda, very much like the Contract of America, the kind of thing you and I have talked about.\par \par \uc2 I sense it in the Senate. Senator McConnell's much more favorable now than he was earlier to having some kind of a contract and that's motion in the right direction. I personally believe when you look at the disaster that big government socialism and woke liberalism has created, I think it's very likely that you're going to be somewhere between 25 and 70-seat gain in the House and at least I think at least a four-seat gain in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 So there's an opportunity in January for Republicans with people like JD Vance and people like \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , new people, new ideas, new approaches, there's a real opportunity that we could set a new pattern for America, force Biden every day to choose between the American people and his radical left and end up going into '24 as a party with big ideas, big solutions, offering a better American future.\par \par \uc2 If that happens, this will be the end of the Roosevelt era after almost 100 years, and you will see a really dramatically different America by 2026. I'm very optimistic that this can happen.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's very interesting because there's not a single success story that the -- I call them the climate alarmist religious cult or New Green Deal socialist. There's not a single success story. So they get this leaked opinion that's not even complete yet, and they rush to judgment -- oh, we'll run on abortion. Even if you consider yourself pro-choice, you don't support abortion up until the moment of birth.\par \par \uc2 We have about a minute left, sir.\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Well, that's right. I mean, if you look at the extremism of the radicals who would literally allow abortion on the day of the birth, would allow the baby to be killed after it's born, basically infanticide. I think it's crazy.\par \par \uc2 And remember, this is a Democratic Party which is on the verge of replacing Mother's Day with birthing persons day. My newsletter at Gingrich 360 this weekend is going to be on, which do you identify with.\par \par \uc2 If you think it ought to be birthing person's day you ought to be a Democrat. If you think it's ought to be mother's day, you ought to be a Republican. It's that simple, and that's why they're going to lose and I think lose for two generations because they're just nuts.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. Well, I mean, look, if Kevin McCarthy if you're right and apparently the president was not angry at the tapes released and they have made amends, that's between them. I'm not getting in the middle of that. But if they follow your lead that you laid out an agenda, positive agenda to save the country like you did in '94, it will be '94, 2010 and maybe even bigger.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, Mr. Speaker, thanks for being with us.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, that's all the time we have left. Please set your DVR, never miss an episode. Thank you for making this possible.\par \par \uc2 Let not your heart be troubled. Laura Ingraham is next. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020220504ei5300001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Leak Of Supreme Court Opinion Draft Unprecedented; Left Urges Violence, Disorder Over Abortion Rights; Abortion Impact On Black Americans; Interview With Sen. \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  (R-MO); Polls Are Closed In Ohio State Primary\b0\par\par\uc2 Tucker Carlson, Laura Ingraham, Bill Hemmer \par \uc2 8,545 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: Tucker Carlson Tonight\par \uc2 TCARL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 BRIAN KILMEADE, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Meanwhile, we're going to continue to follow the Ohio race on the Republican side, a lot of drama, and we're also going to continue to follow the speech by Kamala Harris. She is speaking, and it turns out she is using this as a political opportunity. Who would have thought?\par \par \uc2 Now, it's time for the \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  show, listening for the snare drum.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Good evening, and welcome to TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT.\par \par \uc2 First up, polls have just closed in the Ohio Senate primary, one state, one primary early in the season, yet the results could determine what the Republican Party looks like going forward. So we're going to follow this for you and bring you any updates we have.\par \par \uc2 But first tonight, if you listen carefully to the leaders of the Democratic Party -- and we do -- you would think America was built on a single Court decision from 1973.\par \par \uc2 The very same people who consider the Bill of Rights a racist relic, and quickly dismissed it out of hand, those same people have quickly become emotional as they describe the sublime beauty of Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, when a Democratic officeholder described the Roe decision as quote, "sacred" and it's not an overstatement, for many Democrats, it is sacred. They will tell you and they mean it, that this country cannot continue without Roe. Without Roe darkness will descend. America will revert to slavery and cannibalism and other varieties of Hobbesian misery so gruesome they're best left undescribed.\par \par \uc2 Between a bright new tomorrow and the hell of "The Handmaid's Tale," stands only Roe v. Wade. They're telling you that on channels right now across the spectrum.\par \par \uc2 It's all pretty bewildering if you consider what Roe v. Wade actually is and that is true no matter what you think of abortion itself, whether you're strongly for legal abortion. The decision, as a decision, Roe v. Wade is a widely acknowledged joke. Moral questions aside, Roe is the most embarrassing Court decision handed down in the last century.\par \par \uc2 Every part of it, from its invented constitutional justification to its meaningless parameters, mocks the idea of sober jurisprudence. The point of the Supreme Court is to interpret the Constitution. Abortion is not mentioned or alluded to in the Constitution. Roe is invented whole cloth, and if you don't believe it, reread it 49 years later. Go ahead and try it. It'll make you blush.\par \par \uc2 The Roe decision turns out to be a period piece from the early 70s, like sideburns or the AMC Gremlin. It's the triumph of faddish political trends over the law.\par \par \uc2 So the fact that the Roe decision was in fact shoddy and shameful is hardly a partisan opinion. In fact, plenty of Democrats, including a lot of ardent pro-choicers, have acknowledged that over the years because it's true and that would include, by the way, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has always supported legal abortion, but nine years after the Roe decision was handed down, he was still willing to admit it was indefensible as a legal decision. Pregnant women, Biden explained in 1982 as a Member of the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2 , should not have quote: "The sole right to say what should happen" to their unborn children, because, after all, no one creates children alone. It takes two people. That's obvious.\par \par \uc2 In fact, Biden concluded, Roe had gone quote, "too far." And of course, it had gone too far. That was obvious then, it is obvious now. Then, as now, many Americans believe that abortion is murder. Many other Americans consider abortion a prerequisite to happiness.\par \par \uc2 Now, those are unreconciled positions, but thankfully, in a democracy, we have a solution to quandaries like this, and it's called voting. If we don't like something in America, if we want to change it, we elect representatives to act on our behalf. If they do what we ask them to do, we re-elect them. That's the reward. If they don't, we vote them out. That's the punishment. That's how our system works.\par \par \uc2 For hundreds of years, we have used that system to resolve plenty of complex and thorny moral issues, not just abortion, many others, and it has worked well and that's why this has always been a stable country, because we get to rule ourselves.\par \par \uc2 Roe versus Wade took that right away. In a single 1973 decision, the High Court banned democracy from the debate over abortion. Justices prohibited the states from enacting abortion restrictions that their own citizens strongly preferred.\par \par \uc2 That meant that going forward, Alabama would be required to have the same abortion laws as Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 Now, some people loved this. Of course, people in Massachusetts loved it. People in Alabama hated it, but there was nothing anybody could do about it because the Supreme Court had cut voters out of the equation. And as a result of that, the issue of abortion was never resolved. Things are not resolved by fiat. They're only resolved by consent. That's the core idea in democracy, and it's true.\par \par \uc2 So as a result of this short-circuiting of democracy, demands from the left forced it. As a result of that, for nearly 50 years, this issue has festered. It has given Americans yet another reason to dislike each other. It has divided the country and now, finally, after 49 years, voters might have their rightful say over what to do about abortion, as is their right.\par \par \uc2 According to a piece last night in the blog, POLITICO, the majority of Justices on the Supreme Court are ready to overturn Roe. Justice Alito said so very clearly in a draft opinion you can read yourself because it's circulating on the internet.\par \par \uc2 Now, we shouldn't be able to read that draft opinion. It's not for public consumption. A final official decision on Roe is supposed to be months away and yet an unnamed liberal operative short-circuited this ancient process, which has worked well for hundreds of years. This person leaked the opinion and not by accident.\par \par \uc2 The point of leaking the opinion was to intimidate conservative Justices into reversing course. Mob justice.\par \par \uc2 Now, if you're shocked by that, you shouldn't be. Remember that it's not so different from what we saw this January when another unnamed liberal operative leaked the news that Justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  was planning on retiring, and that news forced \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  to retire, which liberal operatives wanted him to do because he was a White man.\par \par \uc2 So that was, in other words, another op, one of many we're now seeing in our country and as if to prove that, within moments of this story breaking last night, a mob formed -- a flash mob -- at the Supreme Court. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CROWD CHANTING: Hey, hey, ho, ho, fascist scum has got to go. Hey, hey, ho, ho, fascist scum has got to go. Hey, hey, ho, ho, fascist scum has got to go. Hey, hey, ho, ho fascist scum has got to go.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, the upside is they're not telling you "It's your body, your choice." Even these people couldn't pull that off with a straight face after forcing millions of Americans to inject an experimental drug against their will or be fired. Do you remember that? So, they can't claim you have bodily autonomy anymore because you demonstrably don't. So, instead, they move to name-calling.\par \par \uc2 You're a fascist if you disagree with them and they've been honing those talking points because they've been preparing for this moment for quite some time.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court, everyone knows, is currently debating the constitutionality of a Mississippi law that bans abortion after 15 weeks. Now, during oral arguments in this case in December, Justice Alito noted that, quote: "The fetus has an interest in having a life." Now, that's true. But when he said that, plans for retaliation began. No one wanted \uc2 Sam Alito\uc2  to vote the wrong way and now those plans are underway.\par \par \uc2 And it's no exaggeration to say that once this stuff gets going, you don't know where it winds up. People could get hurt because of this leak. You'd hate to think that could happen and you'd hate even more to think anyone wanted that to happen, but people do and here they are.\par \par \uc2 Aida Chavez works for "The Nation." She's some kind of reporter. She just tweeted that it is quote, "good" that conservative Justices and their families will quote, "have their lives threatened." She's in favor of that.\par \par \uc2 Over at vox.com, Ian Millhiser added, quote: "Seriously, shout out to whoever the hero was within the Supreme Court who said, 'F-it! Let's burn this place down.'" Oh, we don't get what we want, we'll just burn it down. Government by tantrum. You've seen that before.\par \par \uc2 Brian Fallon, the executive director of the thoroughly thuggish activist group Demand Justice (or Else), which is implied, said this quote: "Is a brave clerk taking this unprecedented step of leaking a draft opinion to warn the country what's coming in a last-ditch Hail Mary to see if the public response might cause the Court to reconsider?"\par \par \uc2 Oh, the public response, like do what we want or will hurt you. Again, we've seen that before. Let's stop pretending. These are threats of violence, obviously.\par \par \uc2 The CEO of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  is now calling on activists to storm State Capitol buildings. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS MCGILL JOHNSON\uc2 , PRESIDENT AND CEO OF PLANNED PARENTHOOD FEDERATION OF AMERICA AND THE PLANNED PARENTHOOD ACTION FUND: We know that this decision is going to enrage people. We know. We've already seen what's happened when people find out that -- when they found out what was happening in Texas, they started filling State Houses. In Florida, they started filling State Houses and other places because they know that the fight right now is on the ground in these states and so we are going to continue to capture that rage.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Oh, we're going to capture that rage? "People get angry, and you wouldn't like us when we're angry." What? Didn't we have a system? Didn't we have democratic norms we were supposed to observe? If you don't like something, isn't there a process for resolving that? Don't you elect people to see your will put into law? Not anymore. You just storm Capitols.\par \par \uc2 "But wait a second," says the attuned television viewer, "Isn't storming Capitols to thwart democracy an insurrection?" Oh, no, only under certain circumstances. Not when the abortion people do it, not when they announced their plans on CNN. When that happens, that's a good thing.\par \par \uc2 Already the leaders of the Democratic Party are vowing to use this draft decision as a pretext to eliminate the filibuster and pack the Supreme Court. Now, here's the best part: All of this is happening in the name of democracy, so that you will never have a chance to vote on something that matters to you like abortion. And by the way, it matters to you whether you're for it or against it, but so that you won't have a chance to ever vote on something like that, they're going to for democracy.\par \par \uc2 Here's a former U.S. Attorney explaining to the conservative Justices on the Supreme Court are, in fact, insurrectionists.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PREET BHARARA, CNN SENIOR LEGAL ANALYST: I think it's not too great a stretch to say there is some connection between an effort to overturn an election and an effort to overturn Roe and it's this, as I've been thinking about it. There is a segment of the ideological spectrum now who thinks it has certain kinds of powers and wants to engage in radical efforts to overturn things that they don't like.\par \par \uc2 There's no more incrementalism. There's no more compromise. You don't like the results of an election, you storm the Capitol and you talk about hanging the Vice President of the United States and you get the presidency back.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, it's like overturning an election. I mean, you listen to something like that and there are like nine points you could make in response. Then you have to ask: Either the person saying that is so stupid that he doesn't understand what he is saying or he is willing to say absolutely anything to stop the other side and that's, of course, what you're watching.\par \par \uc2 These people aren't stupid. They're just dishonest.\par \par \uc2 Now, the thread, the consistent note in all of