r \par \uc2 State Senator \uc2 Matt Dolan\uc2  saw a late surge in support after rejecting Trump's claims that the 2020 election was stolen. Dolan tells Fox, Ohio voters care more about the future than the pat.\par \par \uc2 DOLAN: There is one candidate, me, that has been talking all about Ohio, going to Washington, fight for Ohioans, and that's why I think momentum is great.\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH: Businessman Matt Gibbons, who lost a Senate primary bid in 2018, says he's hopeful he'll have better luck tonight.\par \par \uc2 MIKE GIBBONS (R), SENATORIAL CANDIDATE, OHIO: It's kind of an end of a 13 months of hard work ended today. And hopefully it will begin again tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH: Today, Democrats are also going to the polls to pick their Senate primary candidate. The DNC is expected to spend a lot of money between now and November to try to flip the Senate seat blue.\par \par \uc2 We're also hearing from outgoing Republican Senator Rob Portman, who says this really has been a contentious primary, but that he believes no matter what happens tonight, we will see a united Republican Party by the fall, and we should know who that nominee is going to be within the next couple of hours. Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (on camera): See those results here on Fox. Mark, thanks.\par \par \uc2 BAIER (voice-over): "BREAKING TONIGHT", more on those new Fox polls we told you about. One shows Republicans with a seven point lead over Democrats for the generic congressional vote. That is flipped from the last time Midterm Elections were held in 2018, when Democrats held the edge.\par \par \uc2 If that margin holds through the midterms, Fox News models suggest it would be a wave election for Republicans. And this is the number that sits today: 44 seats swing in the House and 11 seats swing in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Again, as of today, approval of President Biden's job performance remains low, stands at nine points less than it was spring 