 all this time, they're all but applauding the homeland security secretary in his announcement or pronouncement of a creepy new disinformation governance board or as we call it on this show, the socialist Democrats minister of leftist truth. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BRIAN STELTER, CNN HOST: Here in the U.S., there's been an uproar in recent days about the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  setting up what they call a disinformation governance board. This has been mostly a Fox world story. It could come up earlier today on CNN `State of the Union". But I don't think people know what it is and what it isn't, and there's just been a lot of right-wing uproar without knowing what it is. So --\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, keep in mind, the DHS, they were founded after 9/11.\par \par \uc2 We lost nearly of our fellow Americans. They were designed to prevent another 9/11, another attack on the homeland. But under Secretary Mayorkas, what, the department has now turned their focus inward, a complete dereliction of duty, a complete retreat from a post-9/11 world and policies, to keep every American and this country safe from terrorists?\par \par \uc2 By the way, how many terrorist encounters did they have at the border? Forty-one? We don't even know. How many people might have snuck in that we don't know about?\par \par \uc2 And according to Mayorkas, disinformation and climate change, they are the crises of the day and apparently, we have no one to blame but ourselves. In other words, the administration actually believes the greatest threat to this great country are, we, the American people. We've got to look into domestic terrorism, those scary mommies and daddies at school board meetings that will be investigated for domestic terrorism if they dare to raise their voice against CRT or age inappropriate education.\par \par \uc2 And counter to this grave threat, Mayorkas announced a new ministry of truth to be led by a far-left lunatic who ironically spreads a ton of disinformation all the time. For example, in April 2020, Nina Jankowicz referred to the COVID lab leak theory as a baseless rumor spread by Trump supporters -- false. Chinese state-run media frequently cited her fictitious claims using them in their own disinformation campaign.\par \par \uc2 And Jankowicz also spread misinformation, playing down the Hunter Biden laptop. She called that a Trump campaign product, another disinformation lie.\par \par \uc2 She praised this information dossier author \uc2 Christopher Steele\uc2  and on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , she enthusiastically voiced her support for \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  and echoed Hillary's insane claim that Trump would embolden ISIS. No, Trump actually wiped them off the planet and sent them straight to hell where they belong.\par \par \uc2 But don't worry, let not your heart be troubled, according to Mayorkas, our new disinformation minister is totally neutral with no bias at all, who will only act in the best interest of Americans, on a government disinformation board, that will never abuse its power. That's what he's saying.\par \par \uc2 Didn't they tell us that with FISA warrants? Yeah, I think they did.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DANA BASH, CNN HOST: Will American citizens be monitored?\par \par \uc2 ALEJANDRO MAYORKAS, DHS SECRETARY: No.\par \par \uc2 BASH: Guarantee that?\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: Well, so what we do, we in the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  don't monitor American citizens.\par \par \uc2 BASH: You don't, but will this board change that?\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: No, no, the board does not have any operational authority or capability. What it will do is gather together best practices in addressing the threat of disinformation from foreign state adversaries, from the cartels, and disseminate those best practices to the operators that have been executing in addressing this threat for years.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, so we're supposed to take his word for it. Didn't the federal government also tell us that the FISA program, that's right, it would never be used against Americans? Tell that to \uc2 Carter Page\uc2  and Donald J. Trump.\par \par \uc2 And what about this shocking report from late last week detailing how the \uc2 FBI\uc2  actually was caught searching millions of emails and texts and other electronic communications of Americans without any warrant whatsoever.\par \par \uc2 Now, the last thing this country needs is yet another government program that gets used and abused to monitor Americans' communication. I live this life every day. It's a great joy. You should try it one day.\par \par \uc2 Now, first back to tonight's big breaking news from the Supreme Court, here is what we know and that is the host here with -- what she knows, the host of "FOX News @ Night," Shannon Bream, along with "Outnumbered" co-host \uc2 Kayleigh McEnany\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You know, Shannon, because it's "Politico", they do have a degree of credibility and I read through all of this and it was breaking literally 10 minutes before we came on the air.\par \par \uc2 Shannon, I -- and you used to cover the Supreme Court for Fox, so you know the Supreme Court well. I cannot think of a single instance that I recall where there's ever been a leak at the court. So part of me is suspicious but the specificity of it makes me think it would not at all surprise me if this is real.\par \par \uc2 SHANNON BREAM, FOX NEWS ANCHOR, "FOX NEWS @ NIGHT": Yeah, and I have been -- I will say this very carefully -- I have been not waved off that this is actually real. Now, remember, this is a draft dated in February. These drafts go back and forth, they can change, votes can change, until it actually is signed off by the nine justices or you know whoever if there are people recused all the justices here in the case until it's signed off and it's