vation for having abortion up until basically the baby is out of the womb. They stood and gave the standing ovation for the most liberal abortion law, I believe, in the United States is in New York. They gave it a standing ovation. OK, that's what the people in New York want. The people in Mississippi, they want something different. That's how our framers understood our country. It wasn't one-size-fits-all. So that's how it's going to work.\par \par \uc2 Tonight on MSNBC, \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  parroted the Democrats favorite line on this issue.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 JAMIE RASKIN\uc2 , (D-MD) JANUARY 6TH INVESTIGATION MEMBER: I found it astonishing and appalling about the basic legal claim here is that the word "abortion" doesn't appear in the Constitution, and of course it doesn't. This would appear to be an invitation to have "Handmaid's Tale" type antifeminist regulation and legislation all over the country.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Oh, my gosh.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Is he not speaking as a former embryo? That's my question.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Here's my question. When it doubt, when you have no constitutional argument to stand upon, cite Margaret Atwood. I guess that's the "Handmaid's Tale."\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They tried that with Kavanaugh dressing up in the red capes.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Right, they were all out in the outfits marching around.\par \par \uc2 Look, this is performative theater. And I have to say, the leak is part of that. What you are seeing on the streets tonight, this is performative theater. Step back, everybody has to take a big breath. Let the court finally issue its formal opinion. Then we as a country can digest it. I don't like that this leaked out. This is a bad day for --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Horrific, horrific.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: You talk about democracy, damaging democracy? This is one of the most damaging moments to our democracy right here when a major institution has been breached and undermined. I hope there is a congressional investigation into this.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, right. No, no, they are too busy -- oh, no, this is my question. Where is \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  tonight? She is supposedly a strong conservative. Maybe she is out and she said something, and maybe I missed it. But again, if you truly care about these institutions that the rioters, which we condemned, who took down those barricades and injured those police officers, we were against that and we said so, and I tweeted it and texted it, and all of you have seen my texts. But what about this? All of you guardians of democracy -- maybe there should be a new superhero, the guardians of democracy.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: The guardians of democracy.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Maybe they should show up. Maybe they could come up tonight.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: The barricades are up. The barricades are up around the Supreme Court. The moment it leaked in "Politico" the barricades came up. \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  knew what it was up here. He knew what would happen next. And we are watching it unfold.\par \par \uc2 Let's hope this doesn't create pressure that changes the vote improperly and against constitutional law of the construct of the Constitution.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'm telling you, again, I say this, and people say you're trying to tell everyone you clerked at the Supreme Court. No, that was ancient history. What I'm trying to say, that was the first thing we were told when we walk through those doors, that was the first thing Justice Rehnquist told us. You leak something out of here, and you're gone. Your career is over. And a bunch of us were texting each other tonight. And I had forgotten that until they reminded me. I said, oh, my gosh, I remember. And it sent a chill. But it wasn't even a question.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: This is the rabid politization of the court and a major decision. They shouldn't be allowed.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They politicized with Roe, and now they are doing it all over again. Raymond, thank you. Great to see you. And we'll do your other segment later in the week.\par \par \uc2 Up next, the executive director of Demand Justice, Brian Fallon, he put out a tweet. A lot more coverage coming up.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020220503ei5200001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Meet Your New Disinfo Overlord: Nina Jankowicz; Biden's Disinfo Czar Has Propagated Lies For Years; Elites Seek Any Pretense To Stifle Freedom; NYT Suddenly Concerned About China's Influence; Study Indicates 50 percent of Parents Buy their Adult Offspring Food, Cell Phone Plans, Insurance; U.S. Economy Shrank in First Quarter of 2022\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham, Charlie Hurt, Jackie Ibanez, Raymond Arroyo \par \uc2 6,967 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 April 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: They're just purveyor of disinformation and misinformation. You never thought it could happen.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, have a great weekend. Thank you for making this show possible. Set your DVR, so you never miss an episode. In the meantime, let not your hearts be troubled. Laura Ingraham, the 'Ingraham Angle' is next. Have a great weekend. See you Monday.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Everybody, thanks for being with us tonight. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is the 'Ingraham Angle'.\par \par \uc2 Fearing your own people. That's the focus of tonight's 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Nina Jankowicz, Biden's new disinformation czar over at Homeland Security. She's off key and a really bad Julie Andrews impersonation, but it's off key in more ways than one.\par \par \uc2 If we all didn't know that this was really happening, if you didn't just witness that, we'd think this was all some kind of Orwellian spoof of what paranoid conservatives think the establishment on the left is planning.\par \par \uc2 Part angry feminist, part frustrated karaoke singer, Jankowicz, is the last person who should be trusted with distinguishing between fact and fiction. She's a graduate of \uc2 Bryn Mawr College\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It's kind of a caricature of the modern left university. She worked at the liberal Wilson Center, a think tank, globalist, of course, has a collection there of all the worst ideas on foreign policy. And as an expert in Eurasian Affairs, you would think that Ms. Jankowicz would have authored articles maybe on the importance of preserving free expression in repressive regimes, right?\par \par \uc2 Well, not quite. But she did publish this gem. "Malign creativity: How, gender, sex and lies are weaponized against women online." Oh, can't wait to read that.\par \par \uc2 She even worked as an adviser to the Ukraine Foreign Minister. What? And most importantly, for the current day, she is a Hunter Biden scandal denier?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. JIM JORDAN (R-OH): Is this the same individual who said the dossier was real and the Hunter Biden laptop story was false? Is that the individual who's now running the disinformation governance board?\par \par \uc2 ALEJANDRO MAYORKAS, U.S. SECRETARY OF HOMELAND SECURITY: I'm not familiar with those statements.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Then reported widely.\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: I'm not familiar with those.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'm not familiar with that. Well, let me enlighten you, Mr. Secretary. What the new disinfo czar really said about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop was that, we should view it as a Trump campaign product. She obviously wants us to, like, I don't know, emulate a European style model of heavy regulation of Internet content deemed harmful and dangerous.\par \par \uc2 Of course, that just means content that conflicts with whatever the left believes about issues like climate, elections, race and gender identity.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 NINA JANKOWICZ, AMERICAN AUTHOR: The First Amendment does not apply to private platforms. And \uc2 Facebook\uc2  could very easily decide that climate denial or other harmful hate speech and misinformation is not allowed on their platform.\par \par \uc2 But they have decided instead to allow this kind of free speech fairy dust to reign over the platform. And I think that's where we need to see regulation come in.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You see how she had that laugh like just got free speech.\par \par \uc2 Now, someone should give her a lesson in basic administrative law, because if it were Constitution as a delegation of authority for the executive branch to effectively outlaw certain types of speech it doesn't like or doesn't agree with. I kind of have a feeling that, President Obama, who actually is a Harvard law graduate would have figured that out before this Biden Bryn Mawr crowd.\par \par \uc2 But the real story here is a lot bigger than Ms. TikTok meets America's got no talent. The problem is the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  itself, set up by President Bush after 9/11 it's a complete disaster. I've been saying this for probably 15 years. And now, it's run by a man I wouldn't hire to work security at a preschool.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Have of the 42 illegal migrants on the terrorist watch list or no- fly list encountered on our Southwest border been released into the United States?\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: I do not know the answer to your question.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So look, if you think that DHS exists to protect the homeland, you heard him. You're sorely mistaken. Its entire mission now, this disinformation board, is to protect the elites from the homeland. In other words, to subdue and surveil the people who actually pay their salaries.\par \par \uc2 Now, last time I checked, 221,000 illegal immigrants crossed our southern border. They were encountered by our border patrol. This was in the month of March alone. That's a record, I believe. Congratulations, Mr. Secretary. No threat to the homeland there. No worries at all.\par \par \uc2 Well, this only fuels our drug epidemic and puts the cartels in charge, kills tens of thousands of Americans every year in fentanyl overdoses. But the only thing that DHS is really worried about, is you. Because they want to shut down conservative speech, ban anything negative said about Biden to the Democrats, and punish you, if they think you get out of line.\par \par \uc2 They call that, by the way, domestic terrorism. If you post something that they don't like, believe me, that's what they think.\par \par \uc2 So I'm telling you. Someone like \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  should have the Senate lawyers write a letter to put the administration on notice, that Republicans believe the office of disinformation has been set up to harass and intimidate law-abiding Americans, who are simply peacefully exercising their constitutional rights. That they believe that it's being headed by a rank ideologue and a gender activist.\par \par \uc2 And that the Republicans also should announce, that if any American feels threatened, or in any way targeted by the DHS, Republicans will fight tooth and nail to defend their rights.\par \par \uc2 Remember, now, the government used 9/11 to justify the creation of DHS, which just turns into this huge surveillance apparatus in the United States. The government then used COVID to lock us down, mandate vaccines, and close schools and even churches. And now many of these same people are using January 6 in a similarly nefarious way, as a way to limit freedom.\par \par \uc2 Attend a conservative event, a Trump rally, you better watch out, even post about it. Or maybe some criticism of the Biden administration, maybe you're really angry about the Biden administration. On the internet, doing so could end you up on some type of watch list. Maybe you'll lose your job, maybe you'll even be put in jail.\par \par \uc2 Now, the more this goes on, the more obvious it is that these people do not know how to govern America. Look at the economic news this week. The more desperate Democrats will become to silence the opposition, to punish their domestic enemies. This is why, for instance, they're freaking out about \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , it was an idea whose time has long since expired. Should have been broken up many, many years ago. They could have streamlined intelligence without creating a new superstate style control of the American people.\par \par \uc2 It's too big. It's too unwieldy. It wastes too much money, and it's too ineffective. And by the way, it's now actually vindictive. And that's the 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now and I'm delighted she's with us, Colorado Congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 , who sits on the House Budget Committee. Congressman, this new misinformation board is prompting action from House Republicans, I understand. This happened today and is bubbling all week. What can you tell us?\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 LAUREN BOEBERT\uc2  (R-CO): Laura, first of all, who the hell does Mayorkas think he is? He's lied to the American people about the border being closed; he's lied about how many Haitians were crossing our border; he's lied about our great Border Patrol agents. And now, he's the one starting this Orwellian Ministry of Truth.\par \par \uc2 I will be introducing the protecting free speech act, which will defund this proposed department and prohibit any spin off that these scoundrels may try to create. Congress has the power of the purse, and it is our duty to shut down this department.\par \par \uc2 No taxpayer dollars should be used so that Biden can commit what he calls the greatest send and abuse the power of the federal government to silence truthful stories like Big Tech did, when the Hunter Biden laptop from hell story broke. My bill puts in into this department of propaganda.\par \par \uc2 Laura, this is sick. It's unconstitutional and it's un-American. And every person, Republican, Democrat and independent throughout this great nation should be outraged.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I mean, not a single penny of U.S. taxpayer dollars should be going to this board. And I - \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  tried to spin this today and speaking specifically about this ministry of disinformation. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JEN PSAKI\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: The first bullet was about protecting privacy, civil rights and civil liberties, and the First Amendment. They said, the primary mission is to establish best practices to ensure that efforts to understand and respond to disinformation are done in ways that protect privacies. To address how - and understand how misinformation's spread by human smugglers.\par \par \uc2 There's no question. Everybody that has bipartisan support for that to address disinformation that's going - that's helping smugglers.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. Congresswoman, I mean, I laughed out loud. OK. When I first heard that with a bunch of the producers here, we were screaming, laughing.\par \par \uc2 So they're starting this to really crack down on the smugglers that they're allowing to just cross enmasse into the United States with a millions of illegal immigrants.\par \par \uc2 BOEBERT: Right. We're up to almost 3 million illegal immigrants who have come into our country and they're doing nothing to slow them down. But, Laura, we know that Biden in his regime lie constantly. So the hypocrisy isn't anything new. And we can't just shame these tyrants. They must be held accountable.\par \par \uc2 What the American people want is for those trying to take our rights away, trying to trample the Constitution and silence our voices, to pay the price. This cannot go unaddressed. And that's why I'm calling on House leadership Kevin McCarthy, Steve Scalise and others to not only join me in efforts to defund this program or any program that would seek to police and speech. But they should join--\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. Congresswoman--\par \par \uc2 BOEBERT: --my talk to impeach Secretary Mayorkas.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, we got to go. But thank you so much. And we'll be following up on your call for this legislative action.\par \par \uc2 All right. Our next guest couldn't help but notice the parallels between this dystopian vision of the Ministry of Truth like board at DHS, and other governmental instruments used by the CCP. He joins me now, Steven Mosher, president of the Population Research Institute, author of Bully of Asia.\par \par \uc2 Steven, so I believe you go as far as to say that this one act at the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , that they say, Oh, Trump had something like this, and this is not a big idea - big deal. But you fear for the future of our country because of this. Explain?\par \par \uc2 STEVEN MOSHER, PRESIDENT, POPULATION RESEARCH INSTITUTE: Well, I do because this is what happens in communist China. My goodness. Communist China not just takes down the posts of dissidents and blocks them on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . A thought crime in China is punishable by law. It is punishable by imprisonment. And it happens all the time.\par \par \uc2 And I'm afraid that people on our side of the Pacific are now looking to China for guidance in how to control their population. Because China, as we see from Shanghai, as we see from the gulags in the far west, China does it so well.\par \par \uc2 And I listen to the people on the left side of the equation saying things like, we now are able to hack into human brains. We now are able to control your very thoughts and to program you. We now are able to set up alternative realities and decide for you, how you should think about different issues.\par \par \uc2 This new office strikes me as going precisely down that road. And it terrifies me, Laura, because at the end of that road is a total lack of freedom. Once you allow an office to define truth, then you've allowed them to define what is falsehood in their view, and from there it's a very short step to thought crimes and imprisonment.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, you're - I mean, people are already editing themselves, right, Steven? I mean, they do it on a college campus all the time. High school, junior high kids are afraid to say what they believe. But now people everywhere editing themselves That that in and of itself is scary.\par \par \uc2 But I'm going to get back to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , because the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  issue with Musk, because the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  is finally expressing concern over China because of Musk. And I want to quote something. OK.\par \par \uc2 "As \uc2 Twitter\uc2 's new owner, Mr. Musk may well face Chinese pressure", they wrote today. "Not only demands from the authorities to censor information online, even outside China's Great Firewall descriptions of Taiwan is anything but a province of China, for example, but also the arrest of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  users in China. In China, Mr. Musk's takeover has raised fears that officials will have even more levers to censor their critics."\par \par \uc2 Steven, it took \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  buying \uc2 Twitter\uc2  for the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  to get a light bulb over how repressive this regime is.\par \par \uc2 MOSHER: Yes, I mean, Chinese influence operations in the U.S. go back 40 years. They include the pages of the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MOSHER: The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , other major publications. They pay them by the page. They freely place propaganda pieces and have for years.\par \par \uc2 And now - I mean, look, The Times' real concern is not \uc2 Twitter\uc2  censoring content critical of China's human rights abuses. That happens in the past. The real concern, of course, is that \uc2 Twitter\uc2  will no longer protect the failed Biden administration and the progressive policies, in general, by censoring and de-platforming its critics. That's what they're concerned about.\par \par \uc2 What's going to happen to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  users in China, I don't know. There aren't very many. Chinese Communist Party tried to ban all \uc2 Twitter\uc2  users from China back in 2011. So the newest company owned by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is not directly susceptible.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. Steven, you're the best guest on this topic. We really, really appreciate it. But I howled at the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , we're worried about Chinese influence. Come on, give me a break. Thanks, Steven.\par \par \uc2 And remember, if you cannot watch us live, tsk, tsk, make sure you set your DVR to record the series record. It'd be great. You don't want to miss us every weeknight at 10pm Eastern.\par \par \uc2 But up next, we have a job for Biden's new disinfo czar, but involves looking into her new boss. What are we talking about? I'm going to explain it in moments. So stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It sounds like Joe's Disinformation Governance Board's first task should be examining a new piece from CNN headlined, "A frustrated \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will go on the attack against Republicans in the midterms and into 2024."\par \par \uc2 Now, the piece goes on to describe President Biden as "letting loose in private conversations in recent weeks, railing about the factors bogging down his approval ratings, and the people he thinks aren't helping."\par \par \uc2 Find a mirror, Joe. But on the piece. It continues to go on and say, "He's gearing up for intense midterm campaigning built around hammering Republicans, as he tries to save Democrats in the House and Senate, but also to tee up a reelection campaign." I'm sorry, my stomach hurts.\par \par \uc2 Now, leave the political wisdom of this strategy aside for a moment. He's in, what, 36 percent approval in some polls. Does anyone believe any of this? That \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the man who needs a little blue dot sticker on the floor to know where he's supposed to stand, a guy who needs the Easter Bunny to tell him where to go in a rope line?\par \par \uc2 He's helming some type of impassioned strategy meetings. The man who couldn't command his own dogs to behave; the man who doesn't have command over his Cabinet members' names is supposedly commanding war room sessions. I love how they use the word, hammering.\par \par \uc2 Here now is Fox News contributor, Washington Times opinion editor, Charlie Hurt; and Ohio Senate candidate J.D. Vance, who is way up in the polls in Ohio after being endorsed by President Trump. As these Biden broad sides are apparently J.D. going to intensify against people like you. Are you scared?\par \par \uc2 J.D. VANCE, OHIO SENATE CANDIDATE: Yes. I'm really shaking in my boots, Laura. The \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  who doesn't know where he is half the time is going to come after me. But it is extraordinary what's happening in the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 It's weird too, but I can't tell whether to be angry at it or sad for what - guy clearly doesn't seem to be totally with it. But his administration is filled with radicals.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. And, Charlie, we have this segment called positively boosted, which we always want everyone to be healthy. But it's just a kind of a checklist right of who has been boosted, fully vaxxed, yet they keep getting COVID.\par \par \uc2 So the White House Communications Director \uc2 Kate Bedingfield\uc2  is another positively boosted person. The latest in this long line of these White House officials who test positive, but like others, apparently, she's not to be considered someone who ever had close contact with the President recently.\par \par \uc2 Now, Charlie, this gets to the point, right, that it's impossible to believe Biden is running strategy meetings when he hasn't had close contact with Pelosi, who had COVID; \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who had COVID; the attorney general, who had COVID. And I forgot all the other names, but there's lots of them.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE HURT, WASHINGTON TIMES OPINION EDITOR: Yes. So we keep eliminating all of these people. And we're wondering who's running the government? Because clearly, it's not \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and it's not any of these people. So the question remains, who is it?\par \par \uc2 But I love that the White House is suggesting that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is going to go out there on the campaign trail to save Democrats. It will be really interesting to see how many Democrats running for reelection, running for their lives, actually call on President Biden to come and save them. I think that they're going to be - he's like kryptonite for Democrats running for re-election. They're going to be - not going to want to be anywhere near the guy.\par \par \uc2 But it's really interesting, because as bad as he has been on policy, as much as he has destroyed so much of the country, he's even worse when he goes out there and just tries to wing it. He freezes up, he flags out. You have no idea what he's talking about. He has no idea where he is. As you point out, he has to be rescued by the Easter Bunny.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: When I - Charlie, when I get to the point where I need blue dots on the floor to tell me where to go, you have to physically come to the studio and pull me off the camera. OK.\par \par \uc2 HURT: We will do an intervention.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Thank you. Thank you. Easter Bunny, Santa Claus, any of them ordering me around, just take me off, J.D.\par \par \uc2 All right. In a new NPR/Marist poll just came out. Republicans, J.D., are leading Democrats in this generic congressional ballot of parents with children under 18, 60 percent are choosing the GOP; and 39 percent only are choosing Democrats among Latino voters.\par \par \uc2 This is critical. 52 percent are choosing the GOP over 39 percent on the Democrat side. J.D., I don't think I've seen numbers like this. I don't know when - I don't know if I've ever seen numbers like this. Your reaction?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: No, we're in store for a really good year as Republicans, which by the way, Laura, is why Republican primaries like mine are so important, because are we going to send establishment to any Republicans, are we going to send people who are actually going to push for stronger trade policies? And for a reasonable foreign policy. That really is the question, I think.\par \par \uc2 We're going to get a Republican Congress, Laura. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's mismanagement, his terrible governance has ensured that. But I really think a big question is, what kind of a Republican government are we going to get in 2022? And America First government and American First Republican Congress, or the same old thing that just sits on its hands and doesn't do anything to fight back against the radicalism of the left. That to me is the big question.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. Be a punching bag and start things like \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  that end up spying on the people.\par \par \uc2 Charlie, today, Politico published an article called "The rise and fall of the star White House reporter". Now, where one reporter says, "\uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is very good at her job, which is unfortunate. And the work is a lot less rewarding, but because you're no longer saving democracy from \uc2 Sean Spicer\uc2  and his \uc2 Men's Wearhouse\uc2  suit, jawing with Jen just makes you looks like an a**hole".\par \par \uc2 Why did this person actually get a grant? Why is this reporter granted anonymity for that revealing comment about his or her bias?\par \par \uc2 HURT: I have no idea. But I do think it's kind of interesting. I don't think that the press is ever going to get on the side of Republicans, or do that much to--\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Or be fair.\par \par \uc2 HURT: --undermine a democratic and be fair. But I do think that you're going to start seeing more and more questions about the Biden administration. And so what - as bad as it's been so far, I think that we're looking at probably things getting much worse for the Biden administration when more and more reporters start asking actual questions.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Just back to J.D.'s point very quickly. What type of Republican are people rallying to America First, or the old dinosaur establishment pro-China, pro-open borders? J.D., that was an excellent point. I hope that resonates with people all across America throughout the weekend and this midterm election cycle. Thank you both.\par \par \uc2 And we have something really exciting for you coming up next in the next segment. Instead of Friday Follies, Raymond and I are going to be joined by a live audience of Floridians. We have a raucous focus group coming up. It's a new segment and it is next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 JACKIE IBANEZ, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Good evening and welcome to FOX News live. I'm Jackie Ibanez in New York.\par \par \uc2 A Democrat hoping to run against Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  saying he's open to a statewide mast mandate. Congressman \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  telling attendees at a campaign event, quote, "I would be open to doing what scientists advise." Earlier this month a Florida judge tossed out the Biden administration's mask mandate for passengers on public transportation. Crist's primary opponent Nikki Fried supports ending the mask mandate.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a sinking feeling on Wall Street. The Dow tumbling more than 900 points and the Nasdaq fell 13 percent in April, its worst monthly performance since the Great Depression. Traders are concerned about poor performance by major tech firms like \uc2 Apple\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , and news this week the U.S. economy shrank during the first quarter.\par \par \uc2 I'm Jackie Ibanez. Now back to THE INGRAHAM ANGLE.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Tonight we're doing something a little bit different. It's not Friday Follies, but Friday forum. I'm joined by FOX News contributor, duh, Raymond Arroyo. This incredible crowd in Orlando is with us.\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: And Laura, we thought it would be fun to turn these guys into our THE INGRAHAM ANGLE focus group. Is that OK, gang?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, well, I don't know. This crowd is a little unsavory. But Raymond, did you see the story where half of all parents say that they continue to financially support their adult children? What?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I did see that. According to a new report, it's a study by \uc2 Savings.com\uc2 , get this, 50 percent of parents buy their adult offspring food, cell phone plans, and insurance.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You've got to be kidding.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: A show of hands, ladies and gentlemen, how many of you financially support your adult