GRAHAM: What? He would never do that.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I would just like to see Biden name all 50 states, I think that would be fun. Don't you?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No, not going to happen.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Minne -- Minneap -- Minne-flori --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How many of you think Biden is going to go to all 50 states, raise your hand? How many of you think he's going to go to any state beyond Delaware, Maryland, Virginia, and D.C.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, how will it play when he visits Florida?\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Everyone over there?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I see crowd.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Or maybe Tennessee. Would they like him a little bit better there?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How about Wyoming?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Can I take a personal -- do you mind if I take a little moment of personal privilege here to interrupt the proceedings?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Please.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: How many Frank Sinatra fans here in the audience?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, God.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: OK, good. Look at you everywhere. I'm going somewhere with this, I promise. The state of New Jersey just honored Sinatra by naming a Garden State parkway after the voice. In my estimation -- and it's a rest area. It's a rest area. In my estimation, Jersey has turned to the chairman of the board into the chairman of the toilets and the truck stops. Is it disrespectful to name a rest area after him? They couldn't give him a road or a bridge, for goodness' sake? Anybody? Yes, what do you want to say. What should they name after Frank Sinatra?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I'd like to see them name a building after Frank Sinatra, to be frank.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: To be frank.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But so, Raymond, maybe when he's saying "my way," that's an a little insight into some on the toiletry proceeding. My way -- which