said we are in a period of enormous growth when we've had a contraction of the U.S. economy. And, and he said the recession is not here now, but it could be in 2023. This is just coming off the top of his head. How many of you believe that we are in a period of economic growth, raise your hands?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Growth.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Growth.\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How many of you believe that, without Congress declaring actually a declaration of war, we should be sending $33 billion more to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 CROWD: No.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Build the wall? Where, in Ukraine?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: No, I think we need to secure our southern border. that's what we need to do.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, guys, we've got to go. This has been great. I love our focus group. Let's do it next week, OK, everybody? Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Come on back.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Come back.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 In moments, I think one of my most powerful segments that I have done in my entire career, next. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. RON DESANTIS (R-FL): We are here today to protect life.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS: We are here today to defend those who can't defend themselves.\par \par \uc2 This will represent the most significant protections for life that had been enacted in this state in a generation.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That was Governor DeSantis just two weeks ago signing into law a bill that prohibits abortion after 15 weeks unless the mother's life is at risk, or the baby will suffer from a fatal abnormality. And that legislation was very important to my next guest. After suffering a stroke when pregnant with her older sister, doctors and her family recommended Congresswoman Kat Cammack's mom have an abortion when she was pregnant with her. The advice didn't sit right with her mom, and she made the courageous division to go through with a very difficult pregnancy. That decision informed Congresswoman Cammack's position on life, and she is now the leader of the House pro-life caucus. God is good.\par \par \uc2 Also with us is Terri Kellogg, a Florida mom who adopted a little girl named Hope after she survived an attempted abortion at just ten-and-a-half- weeks gestation. Unbelievable story. Welcome to both of you.\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman, something that the abortion fight is losing, they think it's losing one for the Republicans. Your response to young voters, especially young women who have been fed so many lies about this issue?\par \par \uc2 REP. KAT CAMMACK (R-FL): Well, first and foremost, I have to think about the fact that, as the youngest Republican women in Congress today, I stand here basically an abortion survivor, and on the cusp of being amongst the generation that is post Roe v. Wade. Millennials are the pro-life generation. And so that is incredibly important to me.\par \par \uc2 And when I think about how the left has really cornered the market, effectively shadow-banning the pro-life movement through big tech, through media, they have had every opportunity to tell the facts and to tell the truth. But they don't have the facts and they don't have the truth. Those of us in the pro-life movement do. We have got science on our side. We've got God on our side. And we will be victorious and end Roe v. Wade in this time.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Terri, your story, Terri, is such a powerful one. When I first read about you and your daughter, I'm a mom of an adopted daughter and two adopted sons. Your story was so moving, I get teared up just thinking about it. Briefly recap why you made the decision you did, and why people should pay attention to this issue now.\par \par \uc2 TERRI KELLOGG, MOTHER OF ABORTION SURVIVOR: When we decided that we wanted to adopt, and I was going to be a special education teacher, so I was open to special needs children. And I knew they were hard to place. And that's I was open to, when I heard about Hope and her special needs through this Christian adoption agency.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You were called to do this.\par \par \uc2 KELLOGG: Yes, it had been placed on my heart. And she's been a blessing. It's been what we know. And it has been difficult, but being a mother is difficult, period. But the blessings have far outweighed it. And God, he has just opened doors for us to share our story, which it takes a lot for someone to understand exactly what happened. And when we share it -- what happened to her head? We tell people when she was 10 weeks gestation, like you had said, which would have been the size of this baby, first trimester, and that's when her birth mom went and had an abortion and thought it had worked. And it didn't. And she left not knowing she was still pregnant. And then she felt movement at five-and-a-half months. And then she chose life, she chose adoption, and didn't know anything was wrong with her. And then she delivered early, and then they knew they were going to have to place her with a special-needs adoption agency.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: There are angels on earth walking among us, and I think you are one of them. And Hope is here tonight. Hope, I'm so glad you are here. You are a witness, and a living witness, to the evils that we can avoid by choosing the right thing. Why is this so important, and why do people need to pay attention to this?\par \par \uc2 HOPE HOFFMAN, ABORTION SURVIVOR: I think because they need to choose life for their child. And even though it may not be easy, they should not choose life abortion. They should choose life for their child, because even for me, I don't know what I was going through until God sent a very special person in my life, and that special person is my mother.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congresswoman, here's what one Planned Parenthood doctor said about laws such as what Governor DeSantis passed yesterday, in Oklahoma, passed a six-week abortion ban modeled on what Texas did. This is what Planned Parenthood is trying to sell.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DR. IMAN ALSADEN, PLANNED PARENTHOOD DOCTOR: And so you are making it so that people of low incomes cannot obtain abortions. And so you are disproportionately controlling people that are black and brown, like I said, low income. And so a law that disproportionately affects that group of people is a white supremacist law.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So for more black and brown babies to be born is now by that logic racist, Congresswoman?\par \par \uc2 CAMMACK: It's amazing how the left can seemingly spin anything. They perpetuate a culture of victimhood. But we in this room, people across America, know that victimhood is not a virtue. It is a condition. And if they were smart, in particular that doctor who we just heard, they were recognize that Planned Parenthood was founded by someone who championed eugenics. The number one race that is terminated in this country are black babies. And the pro-life movement is about empowerment. It's about empowering women. It's about giving a voice to those little girls that are going to be aborted.\par \par \uc2 And that goes for the white little girls, the black little girls, brown little girls. We don't see color in the pro-life movement. And so it's a real slap in the face to every single person, man and woman, who has championed and advocated the voice of preborn children. It is really a shame. And again, the left knows this is a losing issue because the pro- life movement, we're winning.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And I would say the left would say that Hope was not human when they attempted to abort Hope. She wasn't human? Human, heart, voice, love. Mother's Day is coming up. I can't think of a better segment that we could have done, and I'm going to start bawling, so we have to get out. Thank you, Terri, thank you, Hope, for speaking out. Thank you, Congresswoman. You are the future of this party, and we really, really appreciate you. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The Democrats latest disgusting attempt to smear Justice Thomas blows up in their faces. The Last Bite explains.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: For three decades or so, the activists on the left have made it their mission to slander and defame my old boss, Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . But at a recent hearing on Supreme Court ethics, attorney Mark Paoletta caught Democrat \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  with his pants down.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. HAKEEM JEFFRIES (D-NY): I think the quote is many on the left hate Justice Thomas because he is a black conservative who has never bowed to those who demand that he must think a certain way because of the color of his skin. What evidence do you have to support that?\par \par \uc2 MARK PAOLETTA, ATTORNEY: When Chairman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  calls him an uncle tom.\par \par \uc2 JEFFRIES: He's entitled to free speech.\par \par \uc2 PAOLETTA: Can I give you another example.\par \par \uc2 JEFFRIES: No.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Good job, Mark. What a perfect tie-in to the top of the show. Only speech that they agree with is the speech they will protect and defend. All the inconvenient speech, they either want to forget about it if they've said it, or they want to ban it if we say it.\par \par \uc2 That's it for us tonight. Remember, fly your flag, be with your family. Remember, get your USA made Freedom Matters gear and your Mandate Freedom gear at LauraIngraham.com. It's great stuff for the summer, great for Mother's Day, Father's Day. All proceeds of Freedom Matters goes for the month of April to the Special Operations Warrior Foundation.\par \par \uc2 Remember, it is America now and forever. Gutfeld is next.\par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020220430ei4t00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Head Exploding over Musk Buying \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ; Jack Brewer Threatens to Sue Joy Reid over Tweet; Leaked Video Reveals \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Struggle Session; Psaki Shrugs off Question over Visitor Logs; Double Boosted \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Tests Positive for COVID\b0\par\par\uc2 Tucker Carlson, Miranda Devine, Jimmy Failla \par \uc2 7,794 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 April 2022\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: Tucker Carlson Tonight\par \uc2 TCARL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST, "JESSE WATTERS PRIMETIME": ... everywhere and then Vineyard Vines, super classy. And as always, you guys know I rock the Rhoback, all summer long. Stop laughing.\par \par \uc2 That's all for tonight. \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  is up next and always remember, I'm Watters and this is my world.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST, TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT: Good evening and welcome to TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  bought \uc2 Twitter\uc2  yesterday with the promise to restore free speech to America and a lot of people were thrilled by that news. To them, it felt like liberation. Finally, they can say what they think out loud, they can participate in the life of their own country, they can be full citizens again -- that's how they felt.\par \par \uc2 But at the same time, a lot of other far more powerful people were not thrilled by this news. They were highly upset that \uc2 Twitter\uc2  will be lifting its speech restrictions. The \uc2 ACLU\uc2  warned that this was just way too much free speech, and the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  strongly agreed with that. "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " concurred of course, but it took a different angle.\par \par \uc2 "It is terrifying," explained \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 ' personal newspaper, "When billionaires start buying media outlets."\par \par \uc2 MSNBC and CNN did not laugh at that claim, they amplified it and added some. It turns out that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is a hardcore White supremacist. Who knew?\par \par \uc2 Technically, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is an African-American, but 2022 has been like that. You're always being surprised. So, how do you make sense of all this watching from home? Here you have one news story, but two diametrically opposed interpretations of the same story.\par \par \uc2 So how do you determine who is right? Who are the good guys and who are the villains?\par \par \uc2 We've been brooding about this all day, and we have devised a simple test to answer that question.\par \par \uc2 We're about to show you two images. Both of them are famous. You've seen both of them before many times. They're both from the 1980s. Here is the first one. Now, to get a pen and paper and record your reaction to it and remember, there are no right or wrong answers. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE (voice over): Overnight, the wall went up, and overnight, family members were cut off from each other, a city and a country divided.\par \par \uc2 There was a scramble to get out, people jumping from buildings even as their windows were being bricked up.\par \par \uc2 Over the years, there were numerous escape attempts by the checkpoints through tunnels, even in hot air balloons.\par \par \uc2 Three decades later, communism began to crumble across the Soviet Union, the cracks appeared and eventually the wall came tumbling down.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So those last pictures, as you know, were from Berlin in the fall of 1989. Ask yourself, what did you just see? Did you witness the triumph of the irrepressible human spirit over forces of totalitarian control? Or did you find yourself annoyed by the senseless vandalism of government infrastructure?\par \par \uc2 Who did you sympathize with as you watched that video? Was it the protesters breaking down that hated wall? Or did you find yourself feeling for the prison guards in the background who are going to have a whole lot more trouble keeping track of people once the sensible barrier is removed?\par \par \uc2 Be honest. Write down your answers.\par \par \uc2 Now, we're on to the second image. This one is from Beijing, China. Same year, a few months earlier. So what do you see here?\par \par \uc2 There is a man standing alone in front of a tank. Is that man a hero risking his life for human rights? Or is he a hooligan impeding the process progress of a government vehicle? Who do you sympathize with? The man or the tank?\par \par \uc2 These may seem like easy questions, but that is only because those images are more than 30 years old. Everyone today supports the fall of the Berlin Wall and the freedom fighters in Tiananmen Square.\par \par \uc2 But back in 1989, it was a mixed bag. Actually, a lot of highly respected people thought the Berlin wall should stay up, that would include \uc2 Margaret Thatcher\uc2 , the President of France, and a lot of others.\par \par \uc2 Now, that may sound shocking to you, but really, it's not so different from what we're witnessing now. Now, today, we are witnessing a lot of well- respected people who are arguing with the straight face that \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , one of our main avenues for solving political differences should remain censored.\par \par \uc2 They're telling you again, with a straight face, that you can't have a democracy where everyone is allowed to participate in the conversation. No.\par \par \uc2 In order to represent the public, the public must be forced to shut up. That's what they're saying.\par \par \uc2 So whose side are you on? The man or the tank? Keep in mind that if you chose the tank, you are by definition, a Stalinist. We're not judging, but we thought you should know that. The good news is you've got a lot of company. Here's MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ANAND GIRIDHARADAS, PUBLISHER, THE.INK: There's studies that have been shown that this power can be used to tilt elections if someone were to want to use it that way.\par \par \uc2 It's not enough to just rig law and policy, you want to rig the discourse. You want to make sure you control the terms.\par \par \uc2 ARI MELBER, MSNBC HOST: If you own all of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  or \uc2 Facebook\uc2  or what have you, you don't have to explain yourself. You don't even have to be transparent, you could secretly ban one party's candidate or all of its candidates, all of its nominees or you could just secretly turn down the reach of their stuff and turn up the reach of something else and the rest of us might not even find out about it until after the election.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Oh, see, if a billionaire controlled \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , you could rig the discourse. That's a fair point. See the thing about owning a social media company is you could, quote, "Secretly ban one party's candidate." Or even scarier than that, you could, quote "secretly turned down the reach of their stuff or turn up the reach of something else, and the rest of us might not find out about it until after the election."\par \par \uc2 Yes, that's a terrifying prospect. Democracy could not withstand that. Let's hope it never happens.\par \par \uc2 What is it about cable television that completely eliminates people's self- awareness? Maybe N.I.H. should do a study on that, it seems like a legitimate health crisis.\par \par \uc2 We're being slightly unfair in that analysis. We do not mean certainly to suggest that it's only Democrats who favors censorship for political ends, Republican leaders support it, too.\par \par \uc2 In a phone call reported today by "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 ," for example, Congressman Kevin McCarthy of California told his close friend \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , that he hoped the social media companies would censor more conservative Republicans in Congress.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the sitting President who had already been silenced by those companies, but McCarthy wanted the tech oligarchs to do more, to force disobedient lawmakers off the internet, quote: "Can't they take their \uc2 Twitter\uc2  accounts away, too?"\par \par \uc2 Those are the taped recorded words of Congressman Kevin McCarthy, a man who in private turns out sounds like an MSNBC contributor, and yet, unless conservatives get their act together right away, Kevin McCarthy, or one of his highly liberal allies like \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , is very likely to be Speaker of the House in January.\par \par \uc2 That would mean we will have a Republican Congress led by a puppet of the Democratic Party. So you wouldn't know any of this unless it was leaked, and you can start to see why the people in charge oppose transparency and fervently support censorship on both sides. Why? Because the more you know about them, the less satisfied you're likely to become with their leadership.\par \par \uc2 Here is eunuch general of CNN's Praetorian Guard warning, the peasants cannot have too much liberty.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BRIAN STELTER, CNN CHIEF MEDIA CORRESPONDENT: If you get invited to something where there are no rules, where there is total freedom for everybody. Do you actually want to go to that party? Or are you going to decide to stay home?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: "Or you're going to stay home." Actually, if you let people choose, you never know what they're going to do.\par \par \uc2 For example, CNN just spent more than a quarter of a billion dollars on a streaming service that in the end attracted 10,000 viewers, right, because people had a choice, and that's not what they chose.\par \par \uc2 So if you're part of a company that made a decision like that, you'd be very much in favor of squelching the competition with censorship. Because if you didn't have a monopoly, you would wither and die.\par \par \uc2 People would start asking questions like, why is equity so important again? Why do we care what TV personalities look like? Shouldn't we care about what they do, what they believe about their characters?\par \par \uc2 Over on "The View," host, Sunny Hostin is desperately hoping you will never be allowed to ask that question.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SUNNY HOSTIN, COHOST, "THE VIEW": On \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , it is predominantly straight White men. So when \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  says, wow, this is about free speech, it seems to me that it's about free speech of straight White men.\par \par \uc2 GIRIDHARADAS: \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  lives in a world in which the only kind of free speech is White men feeling free to say whatever the hell they want.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Oh. Now, we could rebut those points and these people are obviously racist, and nobody says anything about it for some reason, but that's not really the big point. The big point -- and we're going to restate it, because it's the whole point -- is this: Anyone who was angered by the prospect of American citizens expressing their opinions is a Stalinist, and should be feared.\par \par \uc2 We no longer need to guess who those people are. They have conveniently self-identified. It's a clarifying moment, but it is also a little scary, because at this point, there is no going back. Once the kidnapper shows you his face, he can't release you. God knows what happens next.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has jumped with all four paws into this, signaling it is going to use the weight of the Federal government to crush \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  because he wants you to speak freely.\par \par \uc2 The day that Musk announced his intention to by \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , the Feds opened a probe into \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , that would be his electric car company and the source of the wealth that made it possible for him to by \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , and at the same time the Biden administration's allies in the media are uniting to defame \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and destroy him as a man, because that's what they do. "He's a racist."\par \par \uc2 They're about to do that to us, again. "The New York Times" Editorial Board has published a stirring defense of censorship in a newspaper. On \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , "The Times" complained, Musk will be free to quote, "Body shamed people." He could also quote: "Pooh-pooh sound health regulations and shout down critics," and that can't be allowed. Thou shalt not body shame, \uc2 Tony Fauci\uc2 . \uc2 Tony Fauci\uc2  is a very tall man. By the way, the vaccines work flawlessly. Not very subtle.\par \par \uc2 CNBC was even less subtle by the way in its character assassinations. That channel granted anonymity to a source identified as quote "close to some of the Democratic Party's biggest Silicon Valley mega donors." What did this source come over to CNBC to say, quote: "Musk is a great engineer and businessman, but I would not trust him with my daughter."\par \par \uc2 Oh, so he is a rapist now. Got it. Okay. No evidence whatsoever, but you should be afraid for your daughters because \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  wants free speech, and "NBC Nightly News" in between prostate health segments, strongly agrees with that.\par \par \uc2 Watch them tell you that free speech in dangerous women weigh more than abortion clinics, TikTok and "Teen Vogue." Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE (voice over): And some critics are concerned that Musk's pursuit of free speech will collide with growing safety problems on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , especially for women and minorities.\par \par \uc2 Do you trust \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  to make \uc2 Twitter\uc2  better for women?\par \par \uc2 BRIANNA WU, EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR, REBELLION PAC: No, I don't trust \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  to make \uc2 Twitter\uc2  better for women at all.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Oh, it's bad for women. It's pretty funny. All the rich and title ladies won't have a voice, okay. But of course they will. Everyone will have a voice and that's what they're mad about.\par \par \uc2 What they don't want us to coming of diversity, the one thing they say they love. There's no diversity at \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As it stands, 99 percent of recent political donations from \uc2 Twitter\uc2  employees have gone to Democrats, 99 percent -- at 98.7 to be precise.\par \par \uc2 Now, how much is that? Well for perspective, Kim Jong-un got a much smaller level of support from workers at the Central Pyongyang steel plant recently. So 99 percent of anything is a bad sign. It's a terrifying level of conformity. It suggests brain death. But brain death is what they are demanding, and that tells you everything.\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  himself wrote today, quote, "The extreme antibody reaction from those who fear free speech says it all," and it certainly does.\par \par \uc2 Jason Whitlock is here to say more. He's the host of "Fearless," and we're always happy to have him on this show. Jason, thanks so much for coming on tonight. So you've watched all of this. You've been reading about it? What's your reaction?\par \par \uc2 WHITLOCK: At first, I just want to salute you hats off, one of your best monologues and that is saying a lot. I hope that I can meet your standard.\par \par \uc2 Tucker, I want to analogize this to the movie, "Don't Look Up." Leonardo DiCaprio's last movie on \uc2 Netflix\uc2 . It was an analogy about climate change, about a meteor coming to hit, a comet coming to hit Earth and destroy everything. It was a spoof on climate change.\par \par \uc2 We're looking at political climate change, and the left is losing its mind. They ignored the warnings from the Tea Party. They ignored the warnings from the MAGA Movement. They ignored the warnings delivered in a big powerful way on January the 6th, and now they have to deal with the ramifications of that.\par \par \uc2 People like \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , hats off to him. Man with the money is fed up with their censorship and their tactics, and the whole climate around media, the woke media -- CNN+ collapsed, Rachel Maddow running away from her TV show, \uc2 Netflix\uc2  collapsing and losing subscribers.\par \par \uc2 We're in the middle of the climate change that America needs, and the left is losing its mind. Don't look up, they are all scared.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So this -- I love that analogy. We're not overstating it. This really is the beginning of actual change.\par \par \uc2 WHITLOCK: Listen, the meteor will be here come November, these midterm elections. They're all running around like: "Oh my God, we've lost control of public discourse with \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ." This comet that's coming for us and these midterm elections could be even worse now that we don't control public discourse through \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . Now that we don't have our hitman to assassinate the character of anybody that challenges our authority.\par \par \uc2 I'm just very hopeful that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  stays the course. I'm prayerful that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is protected because what he has done, again, with this climate change, changing the climate of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  is incredibly threatening to this Democratic authoritarian style government, this move of Marxism and trying to mimic the behaviors of China, he has disrupted everything. I don't know, in my career in 30 years in journalism, 35 maybe, I don't think I've seen anything this disruptive as what he has pulled off here.\par \par \uc2 And I just delight in the fear that it has caused, and the panic that it has caused among the left, that he is over the target. This is incredible. This is an incredible time to live and the witnesses, they've ignored all the warnings.\par \par \uc2 The warning signs that this was coming, that people were eventually going to rise up and say, "You can't feed me lies forever." You can't intimidate me and send out your Antifa thugs and \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2  thugs and terrorize our cities and get away with it forever. The storm is coming. I'm just happy to be a witness to it.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Amazing. They're rooting for the tank over the man, and the rest of us know it. Jason, we like it is so great to see you tonight. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 So here's one potential vulnerability for \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . Two of his companies, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  have close relationships with the Federal government. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is dependent on Chinese factories. That's where the batteries come from.\par \par \uc2 Now, he is promising to take \uc2 Twitter\uc2  into an uncensored social media platform. So, that is a huge threat to the governments of both the U.S. and China. What does that mean?\par \par \uc2 Glenn Greenwald has been following this story, knows a lot of the players in it, has been fighting for free speech for a long time. We spoke to Greenwald a couple of hours ago for an episode of "\uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  Today" coming up tomorrow morning at FOX Nation at seven and here's part of it, really interesting. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: What do you make of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 ? Do you think he is sincere?\par \par \uc2 GLENN GREENWALD, JOURNALIST: You know, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is somebody who has grown up in incredible privilege. So, he was part of an extremely wealthy family from South Africa. His father was, you know, a very rich entrepreneur.\par \par \uc2 He came to the United States, and he,