t we have. It will be an extraordinary reversal of this trend toward tyranny. That's one possibility.\par \par \uc2 The other possibility is that he either isn't sincere, or he is sincere and will try it, but will fail because of the backlash and the forces amassed against him, which will be extremely significant.\par \par \uc2 In which case for me, we'll just have the status quo. The status quo is billionaires censoring the internet. So if he fails, we'll just have billionaires censoring the internet, nothing will have been lost.\par \par \uc2 So for me, I only see upside.\par \par \uc2 He takes over \uc2 Twitter\uc2  with all of this fanfare and all of this talk and threaten about bringing back free speech and then fails to do so, he is going to look like a fraud and a failure. So, I'm not so worried that he won't -- that he doesn't really harbor that intention as just pretending to.\par \par \uc2 What I question is whether he is going to be able to, because you can be the richest person on the planet. But if you're trying to take away a weapon, from the most powerful institutions on the planet which is what he is doing, he is trying to remove and take out of the hands of the Pentagon, the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 , Democratic Party, Wall Street, all of these -- \uc2 NATO\uc2  -- all of these institutions of power and extremely powerful, the probably their most powerful weapon to censor the internet and therefore, propagandize huge populations. He is threatening to take that away from them, to allow the center for-ish, to ideas to be challenged.\par \par \uc2 You think they're going to just let him waltz in and take that from them without one of the most vicious fights you've ever seen? They're going to try and destroy him.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: He's taking away their most powerful weapon, they're going to try and destroy him. Tomorrow morning, you can stream our entire conversation with Glenn Greenwald, which is worth it. It's now 