em, it is one hell of a problem.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It's bad faith. It's basically abuse of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  systems. And they're -- they are intentionally like -- when I say "they" I mean like Matt Walsh and his publishing company, and other people like him are taking advantage of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and how the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  algorithms work to promote their particular brand of hate and harm on the community.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The final thing we're going to show is a 30-second clip.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Brace yourself.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Of Matt Walsh and I want to say, I want you to brace yourselves.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Okay, so just a primer how this works, anyone who uses the term - - these are academic terms, by the way -- "problematic," "hate" right, is probably an enemy of free expression, a proponent of censorship, and therefore an opponent of civilization.\par \par \uc2 Those people Matt Walsh is up against, he is the host of "The Matt Walsh Show" and of course, an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  bestseller. He joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 This book is deemed problematic by \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , I noticed. It's been bad faith. That's the phrase. What do you make of it?\par \par \uc2 MATT WALSH, HOST, "THE MATT WALSH SHOW": I'm an abuser of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  system, apparently, as well. Look when I listen to them, they're describing my book, "Johnny, the Walrus" as traumatic, hateful, triggering. At one point in the "Eclipse" which I really enjoyed watching. One of the guys breaks down in tears, and I'm thinking to myself, first of all, I'm just a humble children's author in a cardigan.\par \par \uc2 And frankly, I think their behavior towards me is marginalizing me and invalidating my lived experience as a children's author. But also, the book is just -- it's about true self-acceptance, okay. It's about a boy who identifies as a walrus and his mother goes along with it. But then they both learn at the end, that you should accept yourself for who you truly are, who you biologically are.\par \par \uc2 And the thing is, a message of self-acceptance, that was -- when I was a kid that was the most common message in books that we read. It's just that now on the left, what they foist on kids is this false self-acceptance of actually rejecting who you really are in favor of a delusion, and so that's what they're upset about at best.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: But it is a little weird, if you run the world's biggest book company, you probably wouldn't want to hire book burners. I mean, how did Bezos end up with employees like this?\par \par \uc2 WALSH: Well, because this is what the left is all about. We see the same thing with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . That's why I thought it was really interesting when they accused me of gaming the system and manipulating the system. All I did was just write a book and put it on \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the fact that they accuse me of gaming the system only proves that the system is set up to make sure that people like me fail, you know, the conservatives fail and that's what they're upset about \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  about, is that he is going to go look -- no, that system isn't designed for people like him, it's designed to keep us out, and every once awhile, you get these mask off moments where they just basically come out and admit it and I think it's pretty interesting, and also pretty hilarious as well.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: But \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is also like, as noted the biggest bookseller in the world. So, it is the repository of the West's collective knowledge and history. So, if you have censors running it, shouldn't you be really worried that they might disappear this information?\par \par \uc2 WALSH\uc2 : I would be worried about that. I would also point out just what they choose to censor and what they choose not to. I mean, one of the other bestselling children's books on \uc2 Amazon\uc2  right now is a book by the \uc2 American Academy of Pediatrics\uc2 , and it is a book that's one of the top selling children's books and it and it promotes chemical castration and sterilization for kids ages nine through 12.\par \par \uc2 You know, that's the kind of book that they're okay with not my book "Johnny, the Walrus," which is just a tale of a boy who identifies as a walrus. No, they want your nine-year-old to read a book that encourages him to sterilize and castrate himself.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, sterilize your children, because it's not a pagan death cult or anything. Don't worry. Just relax, Matt Walsh.\par \par \uc2 Great to see you tonight. Congrats on the book, which is great.\par \par \uc2 WALSH\uc2 : Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So speaking of history, all of our history now resides in Wikipedia, and people believe that it's true and for a time, it was worth believing. Now, it is run by people whose political agenda supersedes any obligation they might feel to honesty or fact.\par \par \uc2 So Wikipedia, case in point is has deleted the entry on \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's investment firm, Rosemont Seneca Partners. That's the firm that funded research on deadly pathogens in Ukraine through a DoD contractor which happened despite the fact they tell you it didn't happen, it did happen. Period.\par \par \uc2 Biolabs in Ukraine, that's true, and the fact that they flip out and call you names for saying it tells you just how true it is.\par \par \uc2 By the way, he raised a bunch of money in China. Chinese officials in turn funded the company, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  knew all about this. This show obtained a photo of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  golfing with his son and members of Rosemont Seneca's because Board and we aired it, they hated that.\par \par \uc2 But now, President Biden insists there's nothing to see here. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: Mr. Vice President, how many times have you ever spoken to your son about his overseas busines