 Disney\uc2  is sticking with its plans, it looks like, to ramp up political involvement in the culture wars. Now, if you wondered how and why \uc2 Disney\uc2  went from being a family entertainment company to an activist front group, well.\par \par \uc2 Well, we have more insight for you tonight. These new clips emerge from the Reimagine Tomorrow initiative that they started in September. Now, \uc2 Disney\uc2  claims its newfound woke identity is just good business. It's all about targeting their Gen Z customers.\par \par \uc2 But in this leaked online forum with \uc2 Disney\uc2  employees obtained by journalist Chris Rufo, we learned \uc2 Disney\uc2 's real motivation and it goes even further. Here's Karey Burke, president of Disney's General Entertainment Content.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAREY BURKE, PRESIDENT OF \uc2 DISNEY\uc2  GENERAL ENTERTAINMENT CONTENT: They're targeting a younger, I think more open minded. And now we know, as my son texted me this morning, Gen Z is 30 to 40 percent queer than the other generations, mom. So \uc2 Disney\uc2  better get with it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. Is this true? I mean, I don't think so. According to the latest Gallup poll, the numbers have definitely gone up. I'm not sure that math is right. But they're just going with it, and against their own history of staying out of specific contentious political battles.\par \par \uc2 CEO \uc2 Bob Chapek\uc2  seems to be stirring in his own humiliation play. Or maybe it looks kind of like a hostage tape, begging for the radical fringe, begging for mercy.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BOB CHAPEK, CEO, THE \uc2 WALT DISNEY COMPANY\uc2 : I know that we've got work to do and that work starts with listening. I understand that we've made mistakes and the pain that those mistakes have caused. And I know that our silence wasn't just about the bill in Florida, but about every time an individual or institution that should have stood up for this community did not.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, remember, it was just a few weeks ago when a small but vocal percentage of activist employees bolstered by a lot of outside groups lashed out when the company took no position on Florida's parental rights bill.\par \par \uc2 Now, remember, the bill prohibits teachers of very young children from speaking on sexual and gender identity topics in the classroom. That's a big deal now.\par \par \uc2 Now these activist stage walkouts and pummeled \uc2 Disney\uc2  CEO with complaints. And naturally, this sad vision of a man wilted. It's really painful to watch. And it may be painful for \uc2 Disney\uc2  shareholders too. As maybe they should remind their executives who pays the bills for things like this. It's streaming service, and of course, the very expensive theme park admission fees.\par \par \uc2 And listening to Chapek, it sounds like this is just the first political battle that \uc2 Disney\uc2  is going to be entering as part of its new identity.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHAPEK: I pledge to be a better ally for the LGBTQ plus community. Apologize for not being the ally that you needed me to be, and committed to ensuring that our company lives up to its values.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But he's in luck. He has the support now of \uc2 Walt Disney\uc2 's grand niece, Abigail Disney, formerly a thorn in \uc2 Disney\uc2 's side who once railed against CEO \uc2 Bob Iger\uc2 's fat compensation package. And also, against the mistreatment of workers, she now seems to be totally on board with the magic wokedom.\par \par \uc2 In a \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  op ed that ran this morning, she claimed that those outraged over what \uc2 Disney\uc2  is doing want to 'erase' an entire class of human beings. What?\par \par \uc2 She took special umbrage against yours truly. Can you imagine that? From my warning to corporate America about the dangers of mucking around in these very controversial political issues.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Disney\uc2  heiress might want to show some real courage, though, why not? And take up a pen against China. They're real human rights abuses, or is keeping the cash flow coming from Disney Shanghai, well, maybe more important to this new moral crusader.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is the journalist who obtained all of those \uc2 Disney\uc2  videos, Chris Rufo, Manhattan Institute Senior Fellow; also joining me is Amala Ekpunobi, PragerU personality, former left-wing activist.\par \par \uc2 All right, Chris. You are - speaking of thorns in the side of these woke corporations, \uc2 Disney\uc2  went on to write that, "The only option for corporate leaders is to stand tall for authenticity, generosity, joy and decency. These things are kryptonite for the right-wing agenda. Fortunately, they are also the heart and soul of the \uc2 Disney\uc2  brand."\par \par \uc2 Well, everyone counts except all of these moderate Americans who just want to go and have fun and not be proselytized to, or not have their kids turned into sexual points of perversion for teacher. Your reaction to this?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUFO, MANHATTAN INSTITUTE SENIOR FELLOW: Yes, I mean, it really is the case that \uc2 Disney\uc2  claims to be standing tall. But you saw the video. CEO \uc2 Bob Chapek\uc2 , someone who earns $32.5 million a year as his base salary is just absolutely degrading himself every day, day in and day out.\par \par \uc2 And the reality is, is that the conservatives in this country have dealt a major blow to \uc2 Walt Disney\uc2 . In Florida, legislators are looking at taking away their special tax breaks. In Congress and DC, conservatives had said, we're not going to extend the \uc2 Disney\uc2  copyrights for Mickey Mouse and other characters that are set to expire next year. That's a multibillion dollar hit against the company.\par \par \uc2 And conservative parents and families all over this country are in revolt against the mouse, because they don't want their kids to be an experimental ground for the kind of sexual engineering of children that is clearly \uc2 Disney\uc2 's gambit.\par \par \uc2 We've seen it in the clips. We've seen the kind of bizarre personalities that are at the helm, whether it's a biromantic, asexual, a bunch of they, thems, whatever the neo-sexual identities might be, those are the people who are calling the shots. They're projecting their own bizarre psychology onto the CEO who just backs down every day.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Amala, as I said, they're targeting your generation. You're Gen Z, right?\par \par \uc2 AMALA EKPUNOBI, PRAGERU PERSONALITY: Right, I am. Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I hate all the name - I hate the names of the generations. It's all stupid, but it's so dumb. But there - they admit, that's the group they are after. My point is, most of the Gen Zers aren't going to pay 300 bucks for whatever it costs for a Park Hopper pass. (inaudible) pay that. Their parents or their grandparents pay it. And they're not going to want to foot these bills. Your reaction to all of this?\par \par \uc2 EKPUNOBI: Oh, exactly. Yes, I completely agree with you. I think what their motive here is, is to get children while they're young and infiltrate their minds with this sort of ideology, because they know that if they get these children at a young age, it will stick as it did with me. When I was a young leftist, that stuck with me into young adulthood. So that is really the goal here.\par \par \uc2 I think what they fail to recognize is the power of parents, and that parents are really awake to the indoctrination that they're trying to push on their children. We're seeing them protest at \uc2 Disney\uc2 . We're seeing them cancel their \uc2 Disney\uc2  Plus subscriptions. And they're sending letters to these executives saying, I will not tolerate you thinking that you are the parent of my child and that