n family helped Chinese businessman \uc2 Ye Jianming\uc2 , who has suspected links to the CCP and his family obtains visas to the United States.\par \par \uc2 "At the time, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , his Uncle Jim Biden, and his aunt Sarah Biden, were in business with Ye's energy conglomerate, \uc2 CEFC China Energy\uc2 . At the same day, the Bidens embarked on the visa quest, a CEFC executive authorized a $99,000 line of credit for Jim and Sarah Biden."\par \par \uc2 That's just a coincidence. Joining me now is Jason Chaffetz, Fox News contributor and former House Oversight Committee chair.\par \par \uc2 Jason, good to see you tonight. Now, you recently, I know, spoke to some members about this issue. If you can share it with us, what was your advice for how they should handle this?\par \par \uc2 JASON CHAFFETZ, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Even though they're in the minority, they need to immediately issue preservation letters. That's how they expand the net, not just to the government records, but to any contemporaneous notes, any other emails outside of this system, telephone, text messages, all of that.\par \par \uc2 The ask for the preservation should start immediately, because it's the bigger broader family that is involved and engaged in this. Then they - once they get in the majority, they can get after the financial records and all the other supporting documents.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. I want to play what the White House Chief of Staff had to say about this issue. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RON KLAIN, WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF: One reason why \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in the White House, is he promised that, unlike \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his White House wouldn't interfere with Justice Department investigations. And that's what's going on here. It's an independent investigation. I'm not going to comment on it, other than to say that we aren't in any way, shape or form, interfering with or influencing the Justice Department's conduct of 