\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Yes, when I was the chairman of the Oversight Committee, I worked actually very closely with \uc2 Elijah Cummings\uc2 . We did a deep dive. And we had to go through a couple of different secret service directors. They lack oversight, the professionalism and has been questionary.\par \par \uc2 Remember, it's a secret service that was out there advertising on pizza boxes. Hey, come on, join the Secret Service, and taxi cabs and whatnot. But the level of professionalism and training and oversight, this is what happens when you kind of get the lack of oversight that they've had in the past.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Jason, they used to be under Treasury, correct? Weren't they used to - used to be oversight under Treasury. Then they were moved to DHS post 9/11. And everything at DHS is a complete mess. So this - none of this surprised me at all. Look at the border. So - I mean - so this doesn't really shock me. All of it needs to be broken up and to be made more accountable, as you said.\par \par \uc2 Final thought, real quick.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Alejandro Mayorkas is in charge of the border. And he's also in charge of the Secret Service. Hmm. I wonder what's going on there? Maybe it there might be a little management issue. Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Jason, if to rate one to 10, 10 being the best cabinet ever, one being the worst cabinet ever. How do they rank?\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Like, zero - negative two, negative 10. How low can you go? It's about as bad as it could possibly be.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, these are political payoff appointments. Jason, great to see you. Have a great weekend.\par \par \uc2 And speaking of illegal immigration, suddenly there are Democrats pretending to care about the border. Now, eight of them have been warning Biden about repealing Title 42. Remember, that's the Trump era policy that allowed for immediate turn backs of illegals at the border because of COVID.\par \par \uc2 Now, this list of Se