ich \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 . And maybe he can't quite remember what was happening when he was vice president. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I was in the foot -- excuse, the foothills of the Himalayas with \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 , traveling with him. I traveled 17,000 miles when I was vice president, I don't know that for a fact.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: What does that have to do with the Supreme Court justice being confirmed? Absolutely nothing.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He might have that on the brain, the whole Hunter Biden connection with China. What is he supposed to say and what is he not supposed to say? It's like a ball bearing in a box. It just goes, tip it over and it goes one way. And it just makes no sense.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, it is baseball season, and just in time for the start of the season, Cracker Jack has a new sister, you know those little caramel coated popcorn. The parent company \uc2 Frito-Lay\uc2  has unveiled a new phase of the brand, Cracker Jill, to celebrate women and girls in sports.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (SINGING)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Well, Cracker Jill will be available to every sports fan, Laura, who donates five bucks to the \uc2 Women's Sports Foundation\uc2 . I kind of like the idea of Cracker Jack extending its brand to support female athletes and our girls who compete in sports. The question is, are they really? The Women's Sports Foundation that this effort supports, actually advocates biological men competing in women's sports, which as you know, is being hotly contested by female athletes. So the question is, does this advance girls in sports. Go ahead, I'll get your crack at this.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Maybe they should have called it Cracker George, because George will be competing against you know Georgina in an actual female, biological female competition, or a pe