c2 EMANUEL: Illegal immigration, inflation, Afghanistan, and more, all part of the first year of this Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 With that, let's bring in our panel, Bill McGurn, columnist for "The Wall Street Journal," Mollie Hemingway, senior editor at "The Federalist," \uc2 Charles Lane\uc2 , opinion writer for "The Washington Post." Welcome to all of you.\par \par \uc2 MOLLIE HEMINGWAY, SENIOR EDITOR, "THE FEDERALIST": Welcome.\par \par \uc2 BILL MCGURN, COLUMNIST, "THE WALL STREET JOURNAL": Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CHARLES LANE\uc2 , OPINION WRITER, "WASHINGTON POST": Thank you, Mike.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Mollie, what stands out for you first year of the Biden administration?\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: The year began with so much promise for President Biden. He had the full support of the media, which helped bring him across the finish line to achieving the victory he promised to unify the country. He pledged to defeat the coronavirus. He said that he would help the middle class out. And this year has had some success for Biden. He passed his infrastructure bill and a few other things. But it's really been marked by just massive amounts of failure, whether it's the border, Afghanistan, inflation. And it really points to not any of those specific problems but a failure of leadership and competence.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Chuck, your thoughts on the first year of President Biden and his administration?\par \par \uc2 LANE: My impression is they came into office believing that they could make a plan and carry it out. And the plan had, I think, approximately four phases. One was the big $1.9 trillion bill, the American Rescue Plan. Then that was going to be followed by an infrastructure bill, and then Build Back Better. And in between, because of the vaccines, the coronavirus by middle of July, Independence Day, would be behind us.\par \par \uc2 And the plan didn't pan out, in part, because of some of the mistakes they made, but, in part, because the Delta variant came along and threw everything off course. And what has struck me is that they continue to stick to the plan even after some other administrations might have tried to call an audible, and they have not been able to finish the plan in the form of Build Back Better.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: There were also some growing pains for Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  when it came to answering some pretty straightforward questions. Let's play it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: What's your response to reports of Americans --\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , (D) VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Hold on, hold on. Slow down, everybody.\par \par \uc2 We have been to the border. We have been to the border.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You haven't been to the border.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: And I haven't been to Europe.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: I don't understand the point that you are making.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Bill, the vice president was charged with addressing the crisis at the border. Your thoughts on the first year of the Biden White House and her performance?\par \par \uc2 MCGURN: Well, in her performance, she is the border czar who tries to stay as far away from the border as she can. And in some sense, I don't blame her. The vice president is supposed to be the chief salesman for the president's agenda. And the problem is that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has not a good agenda. When he came in, people were talking as though he would be the next FDR or LBJ, but he didn't have FDR or LBJ majorities. So now what's the most common metaphor used? It's \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 . \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2  is synonym for haplessness, with inflation. And I think Afghanistan was particularly brutal because it's not a right or left thing. I think a lot of people just have the impression that the job is too big for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . He is not up to it.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Obviously, the year ended on Capitol Hill not able to get the Build Back Better act across the finish line. House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  says they are still going to try to get it done in 2022. Let's play it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 NANCY PELOSI\uc2 , (D-CA) HOUSE SPEAKER: First and foremost, we will -- we will continue to fight to pass the legislation. This will happen, it must happen. We cannot walk away from this commitment. The Build Back Better is about transforming our society.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Mollie, do you sense they will get something done, it will just be drastically scaled back?\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: There is always that risk that they will pass something, that they will be able to get Joe Manchin to sign on to something. But their best bet for their future political prospects is actually not to pass something, given that we already have such high inflation, which is caused by flooding the zone with trillions of dollars. Doing more of what has caused some of the problems is not going to help out the Biden administration. But it's also a good reminder that \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has been doing no favors for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . And the extreme way in which she is managing her caucus is not helping him at all.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Chuck, your thoughts as we look ahead to the agenda in 2022?\par \par \uc2 LANE: I'm waiting to see how they manage to pivot the two issues that I think people feel they have neglected, inflation and crime, and get control over those as 2022 rolls on, because those, much more than the failure to pass Build Back Better, those are the ones that, first of all, are on the minds of voters, but also threaten the Democrats' prospects in the fall.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Bill, let's get a quick comment from you before we move on.\par \par \uc2 MCGURN: Yes, I agree with Charles. I would add, though, inflation, I think, is the big one, because people don't get their news about inflation from the president or the Fed chairman. They get it when they go fill up their cars and it's an extra 20 bucks. I would add foreign affairs. We have \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  really menacing, and we have Iran out there. And I don't think if these men looked at Afghanistan, they are going to take lessons, gee, better not mess with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . He is going to be really tough.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Let's do winners and losers at the end of 2021. Mollie, lead us off.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: So my winner for the year is \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . He alone among most GOP leaders has seen that people don't want you to just fight Democratic policies but implement conservative policies, and he's done that brilliantly by keeping schools open, fighting vaccine mandates, fighting their hatred of Critical Race Theory and having Florida be a thriving economy.\par \par \uc2 My loser is, really, the American people, but the prime cause of the wretched year that we have had has to lie \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , so he is my loser for the year.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: OK. Chuck, you're up next.\par \par \uc2 LANE: Well, my winner is Glenn Youngkin, who was elected governor of Virginia as a Republican, started out the year as a real long shot, and pulled off a narrow victory in what had been a blue-ening state. My loser of the year is a collective one, the women of Afghanistan. Again, whether you are on the left or the right, the withdrawal of U.S. and other western forces from Afghanistan has left half that country, in the sense, at the mercy of the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Chuck, a quick follow-up. Do you think there will be a push for Youngkin in 2024, or do you think the Republicans will more try to take his playbook for 2022 and beyond?\par \par \uc2 LANE: Well, I think he did provide a formula of how Republicans can win. But there is this guy called Trump I've heard might be interested in running himself.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: OK, fair enough. Bill, your winners and losers for 2021?\par \par \uc2 MCGURN: Mike, my winner, it's very personal to me because this man is also my godson. His name is Jimmy Lai. He was a newspaper founder in Hong Kong. He has just marked a year in jail because he has been advocating for democracy. And what makes his story so incredible is that he was a multimillionaire who could have fled and kept his comfortable life, but he chose the jail cell of a Chinese dissident.\par \par \uc2 My loser is a double hitter here, the Cuomo brothers. Just two years ago \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  and Chris Cuomo were at the top of the game. Everyone was lauding them and so forth. And both have now lost their jobs. Both face accusations of sexual impropriety, and so forth. It's been a sharp fall.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: All right, let's go around the horn and get a look at your predictions for next year. Mollie?\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: I'm going to take the really easy bet that Republicans are going to do extremely well in November of next year. They are poised to take the House and take it strongly. They might even take the Senate. And they are on good footing for retaking the presidency in a few years.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: All right, Chuck, your turn.\par \par \uc2 LANE: There's tremendous concern in a number of big cities over crime. There's a growing political ferment around that issue. And on June 7th, Chesa Boudin, the ultra-progressive D.A. for San Francisco, is going to face a recall election based on people who feel he is too soft, and I think he is going to lose.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: We're up against the clock. Bill, bring us home.\par \par \uc2 MCGURN: Very quickly, I think the Supreme Court is going to grant cert to the case of Asian-American citizens suing Harvard for discrimination and finally rule that this kind of racial preferences is unwelcome and unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Panelists, thanks so much. Happy New Year.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, "Notable Quotables."\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Finally tonight, it's Friday. That means "Notable Quotables."\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I can't even go my neighborhood drugstore. And then coming here, we just got shot down, saying that they are not going to take any more people.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: There is no federal solution. This gets solved at the state level.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: This was a mad dash to get a new flight. There were no flights.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It really had a lot to do with what we thought people would be able to tolerate.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: There are not enough adults in there. You need to go remote. It is not safe in those buildings.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: There's embers throwing and coming over your car, and I would imagine this is what a nuclear attack would look like.\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , (D) VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: We are prepared to issue sanctions like you have not seen before.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You have more words from the Biden administration, but no actions, no demonstrated result.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Ghislaine Maxwell facing 65 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Today, justice has been done.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: John was a legend in his time, but whenever he showed up on the field, it was obvious he presence was there.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Tonight, we remember former Nevada senator and former Senate Majority Leader Harry Reid.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: He has not quite left us, and yet he has left us.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I really don't know anyone who didn't admire and love Betty White.\par \par \uc2 DR. ANTHONY FAUCI\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE CHIEF MEDICAL ADVISER: When you are talking about a New Year's Eve party, we have 30, 40, 50 people celebrating. I would recommend strongly stay away from that this year.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: That's when the whole world comes together and we count down those 60 seconds to the New Year filled with joy, filled with hope.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Quite a week to end 2021.\par \par \uc2 Monday on SPECIAL REPORT, the first day back to school for millions of children amid the Omicron surge. Please join Trace Gallagher Sunday for FOX NEWS SUNDAY. His guests will be Education Secretary \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2  and Arkansas Republican Governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Have a happy New Year. Thank you for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for this SPECIAL REPORT, fair, balanced, and unafraid. We'll leave you with a live look from London as they get ready to ring in the New Year at the top of the hour.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2021 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2021 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FNSPBB0020220101ehcv00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Special Edition of "Hannity": Exposing the Biden-Harris Agenda\b0\par\par\uc2 Jason Chaffetz, Charlie Hurt, Joey Jones, Nicole Saphier, Gregg  Jarrett, Leo Terrell \par \uc2 7,845 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 December 2021\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2021 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2021 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Have a happy and contented and anxiety-free weekend with the ones you love the most. That's our hope for you. And we'll see you Monday. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 JASON CHAFFETZ, FOX NEWS HOST: Welcome to this special edition of HANNITY: Exposing the Biden-Harris agenda. I'm Jason Chaffetz, in for Sean.\par \par \uc2 And tonight, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's Build Back Better socialist spending spree -- well, it appears to be on the verge of collapse in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 . Democrat divisions are as stark as ever. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  are reportedly still way apart on key provisions and the Senate parliamentarian yesterday issued Democrats a brutal reality check, rejecting their latest scheme to sneak amnesty into the Build Back Better bill, ruling that the immigration plan would outweigh the budgetary impact and therefore be outside the scope of the reconciliation process.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: All kidding aside, of course, President Harris is a proud Howard alum. I'm here to congratulate you --\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: But infighting capping off yet another rough week for President Biden, because earlier today, Biden had yet another stream of baffling moments. During his remarks to south -- students in \uc2 South Carolina State University\uc2 , have a look at this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: All kidding aside, of course, President Harris is a proud Howard alum. I'm here to congratulate you but also to let you know that your country -- this is not hyperbole -- is counting on you. They're counting on you, to change, to turn the dial at a moment we have a chance to do it.\par \par \uc2 On police reform, I share the frustration and I know the family well of George -- Family Justice Act and Policing Act. I know the family well. I got started in politics because of the civil rights movement. I noticed some of you were looking, I thought you were wondering, how does he know the black national anthem? Well, because I sat in a black church after going to seven o'clock mass. I'm a -- having a practicing Catholic, at 10:00 on the east side, getting ready to go out to desegregate restaurant, some movie theaters in my state.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, to be clear there's no record of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ever desegregating restaurants during the civil rights movement. So whether it's on messaging or on policy or everything in between, the Biden presidency is imploding. His approval is slumping. His agenda is in peril and Americans are losing confidence in his leadership ability by the second.\par \par \uc2 It's a massive failure on every front and at a time when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is desperate for a political win, things are only getting worse all while Democrats in the media are pointing fingers and attacking Senator Manchin for being a voice of fiscal sanity.\par \par \uc2 For example, take a look at this piece from "The Associated Press," quote, in an extraordinary display of political power in the evenly spit 50/50 Senate, a single senator is about to seriously set back an entire presidential agenda. No, there's actually at least 51 senators, a majority of senators, probably even more that are opposed to this reckless spending bonanza.\par \par \uc2 And Congresswoman \uc2 Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  -- well, she tweeted: The fact is when Dem leadership is really truly set on something, they use a huge amount of procedural political media and resource tools to force votes in very powerful ways. They do it all the time. Now they need to do it with Build Back Better.\par \par \uc2 But worst of all, the media