ake advantage of people and we've treated people wrongly.\par \par \uc2 And when you're looking at the one class of Americans who had so much belief in this country that they were willing to lay their life down for it, they're not going to buy that. And so, even if they're socially liberal or even if they're fiscally Democratic and they believe in a more progressive idea, they're not -- they're going to draw a line and stop it when you start telling them that our country is rotten to the core from its inception.\par \par \uc2 And those are essentially the words we hear out of people like \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  and the Squad who have also driven the policy bust for this president in a lot of ways. And so, I think a lot of people that are just patriotic - - not just served in the military -- we're talking first responders, even teachers, people that really sacrifice thousands of dollars a year to work in a job that serves their communities and their country, they're going to take a second look at a party and people who basically tell them that this country isn't worth that anymore. And it needs revolutionary change to even be worth their effort.\par \par \uc2 And I think that's a big part of what we don't talk about enough. I mean, there's reason why parents are so passionate at school boards and it's not just because of the CRT. It's also because of a complete lack of understanding of how important patriotism and loving this country is.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Yeah, I know, I agree. Again, thank you for your service.\par \par \uc2 All right. Before we go, we should mention that Dana is the co-author of the children's book "Paws Off My \uc2 Canon\uc2 ". So, congratulations to you on that, and thank you all --\par \par \uc2 LOESCH: Thank you. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: All right. Charlie Hurt, Joey Jones and \uc2 Dana Loesch\uc2 , thank you so much for joining us.\par \par \uc2 All right. Now, even as foreign threats in Russia, Iran, North Korea and China are 