at's spreading throughout this country .\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: We've only got about 30 seconds, Mr. Attorney General. But what's the core difference between the way Arizona's is handling this and California is handling it?\par \par \uc2 BRNOVICH: You've got to hold people accountable. We know the number one deterrent of crime is police presence. So, I would ask everyone out there, who is trying to defund the police department, who is trying to demonize the police department? That is the far left, Biden administration and Democrats in Congress.\par \par \uc2 So, that's why we need to make sure that we enforce the laws they had hold people accountable that break the law, because property rights are fundamental not only to political protect, but to economic prosperity. That's what me this country great, Jason.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Yeah, they not only need to catch the criminals, but they need to prosecute them. So, you get a George Gascon there in Los Angeles who works hard to get criminals out of jail harder than taking care of the victims, in my opinion. That's just a cause of her increased violence. It doesn't need to happen.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Attorney General, thank you so much for joining us tonight.\par \par \uc2 BRNOVICH: Thank you, Jason.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: All right. Coming up, the left's radical policies and their failed results are once again on full display. We'll explain as Erin Perrine and Leo Terrell join us with reaction. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: All right. Back in June, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  made a very strange comment about black entrepreneurs and lawyers. And today, he repeated it again. Have a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: The data shows, young black entrepreneurs are just as capable of succeeding given the chance as white entrepreneurs are. But they don't have lawyers, they don't have -- they don't have accountants. But they have great ideas.\par \par \uc2 Because, 