merica an apology. And if he doesn't give that apology, he should be incarcerated for lying on the witness stand. This whole country knows that he lied.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes. Do you think he will do time?\par \par \uc2 TERRELL: I'm begging. I got my fingers crossed that the judge will give him time if he doesn't acknowledge that he lied to the witness stand. But if the judge didn't do that, I think it's a disservice. He deserves at least six months in jail for lying on the witness stand. He knows he lied and his attorneys should be held responsible --\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: And they said they're going to appeal. What do you what do you think of, I got like 10 seconds, about the fact that he walked out of there yesterday after being found guilty on five charges?\par \par \uc2 TERRELL: Shame, total shame. He's a convicted felon, but people understand he's a convicted felon. Kamala Harris, Joe Biden, Nancy Pelosi, you are supporting a convicted felon and you did not know the facts before you start justifying and calling that this was a race, modern day lynching. It's shameful.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: I mean, you know, the crazy thing is you know how it works now in the world we live. It's something like this happens and you don't immediately say that you support him, then you're saying, Oh, why didn't they say anything? They should have said something, and that indicates something on its own. And it's just -- it's a crazy cycle.\par \par \uc2 Leo, thank you very much. Good to have you here.\par \par \uc2 TERRELL: Thank you, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Always a dose of common sense, which we appreciate around here.\par \par \uc2 TERRELL: So thank you for being here today, Leo. So that is THE STORY of Friday, it's Friday, happy Friday, everybody, December the 10, 2021. Have a wonderful weekend and we will see you back here on THE STORY on Monday at 3:00. But stick around because "YOUR WORLD" is just getting started with Neil after this.\par \par \uc2 END\