\uc2 And remember, we are very happy and grateful that you would spend time with us every night, and we always believe without you none of this is possible. Freedom Matters, yes it does. And it's America now and forever.\par \par \uc2 Greg Gutfeld takes it all from here.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2021 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2021 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020211204ehc300001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 First Case Of Omicron Variant Confirmed In U.S.; Update On Michigan School Shooting That Killed Four Teens; Sheriff: Charging Suspect As Adult Is Appropriate; Sheriff: Quick Actions Of School Saved Lives; Sheriff: We Had No Notice Of Threat In Advance; Arraignment Of Michigan School Shooting Suspect\b0\par\par\uc2 Martha MacCallum, Peter Doocy, Marty Makary \par \uc2 9,519 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 December 2021\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: The Story with Martha MacCallum\par \uc2 HUNDD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2021 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2021 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SANDRA SMITH, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: He will be charged as an adult in that case, 15 years old. That was the breaking news from Oxford a short time ago. Lots of news, jam packed two hours, John, great to be with you. I'm Sandra Smith.\par \par \uc2 JOHN ROBERTS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: And I'm John Roberts. By the way, they may also charge the parents they haven't made that decision yet. THE STORY with Martha starts right now. We'll see you tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA MACCALLUM, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Thanks, guys. Good afternoon, everybody. I'm Martha McCallum in New York. We have two very big stories and brand-new developments in both of them right now. Any minute, we expect a live update from Oxford, Michigan, where this story just gets worse by the day, horrific, terrible, terrible high school shooting has now led to the death of a fourth high school student, a 17-year-old. The shooter is now going to be charged as an adult and will face murder and terrorism charges. We're going to take you there live as soon as they step to the podium. They are getting that set up.\par \par \uc2 Also, this afternoon, the Omicron variant has been found in the United States. The infected individual was fully vaccinated as the administration considers big pullback changes for travelers. In moments, Dr. Marty Makary joins us but first, White House Correspondent Peter Doocy joins us, he was in that briefing, very wide-ranging briefing. Dr. Fauci in there answering questions. Peter, over to you.\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: And Martha, it was a very dramatic moment at the start of that briefing when Dr. Fauci came in and confirmed reports that were starting to trickle in that someone in California is now the first case of Omicron in the United States. We understand the President has been briefed about this. He's got a new statement.\par \par \uc2 It says in part, "The President's mental medical team continues to believe that existing vaccines will provide some level of protection against severe illness from Omicron and individuals who have gotten boosters have even stronger protection. As such, we urge all adults to get their booster shots and to get themselves and their kids vaccinated if they haven't already."\par \par \uc2 We understand that tomorrow, the President is set to announce new testing requirements at a minimum for international travelers arriving in the US, which sounds like it is an incomplete policy, at least right now. So, I asked Dr. Fauci about that.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Dr. Fauci as you advise the President about the possibility of new testing requirements for people coming into this country, does that include everybody?\par \par \uc2 DR. ANTHONY FAUCI, WHITE HOUSE CHIEF MEDICAL ADVISER: The answer is yes. Because you know that the new the new regulation, if you want to call it that, is that anybody and everybody who's coming into the country needs to get a test within 24 hours of getting on the plane to come here.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: But what about people who don't take a plane and just these border crossers coming in huge numbers?\par \par \uc2 FAUCI: You know, that's a different issue. For example, when you took a -- we still have Title 42 with regard to protection at the border. So, there are protections at the border that you don't have the capability, as you know, of somebody getting on a plane, getting checked, looking at a passport, we don't have that there but we can get some degree of mitigation.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Is there something to do to test these people somewhere else?\par \par \uc2 FAUCI: No, there is, there is testing at the border under certain circumstances.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: So, they're trying to figure out what exactly to do right now, even though they do admit, and they want to caution people, it's going to take about two weeks from now to figure out exactly how bad this new variant is, and how strong vaccines are in fighting it, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes, that was very interesting. The answer to your question, Peter, he said that people who crossed the border are tested in certain circumstances, and yet, they're cracking down to make sure that anyone who flies into the country, there are no certain circumstances, you absolutely have to be tested now, within 24 hours of coming into the country. So, it just sort of, you know, boggles the mind that you wouldn't have the same policy for people crossing the southern border, right?\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Well, that's because COVID is COVID, and what they're basically saying is that these people who want to document their arrival in the United States at an airport, are going to have to subject themselves to strict government testing before they get here and possibly after they get here, according to these reports, that we're getting the early reports, whereas these people who are coming undocumented when they talk about certain circumstances that they're tested, as we've come to understand that over the last couple months, that just means that someone is showing severe symptoms.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Right. No, it's a complete double standard, that makes absolutely no sense. Peter, thank you for pressing on that question. Always good, always good to see Peter. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Thanks, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, joining me now, Dr. Marty Makary, Johns Hopkins University Professor, Editor in Chief of Med Page Today and a Fox News Medical Contributor. Doctor, great to have you with us. Talk to me a little bit about this new development. I think all of us expected that this would be the case having seen how these, how quickly these variants and viruses travel around the world but you know, documented case in California, of Omicron here in the U.S., what do you think?\par \par \uc2 DR. MARTY MAKARY, FOX NEWS MEDICAL CONTRIBUTOR: Well, good afternoon, Martha. There's nothing really new here. We've known for a while that it's been in the United States and this is just confirmatory, what we're learning about today with the first new case documented. 23 countries this morning have identified the new variant, and those were just the countries looking for it.\par \par \uc2 So, we believe it's at large but I'm not that concerned when many virology and vaccinology experts are saying that this should be encompassed by immunity, both vaccinated and natural immunity. We have major developments with therapeutics. And remember, there's no evidence that this is a more virulent or dangerous virus, it may be a downward mutation, which would be very favorable. We hear about all the mutations on the spike protein, but 95 percent of the spike protein of Omicron are identical to previous variants.\par \par \uc2 So, it's likely that it's encompassed. And final point, we're making inferences about Omicron. That cannot be derived from the data. For example, South Africa doubled its testing, yet there was a 60 percent increase in the positivity rate, at the same time, they're having a delta wave. So, you cannot make any conclusion about it being more contagious.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: I always wonder how long these variants have been around because we've been watching the spike in New England. And it seemed like it was spreading very quickly in certain areas, and it just raised a lot of questions given the vaccination rates in those places. Do you think that we are going to learn that Omicron -- because we probably didn't know how to test for it a month ago, has been here longer than today?\par \par \uc2 MAKARY: Yes, I think it's been here for a couple of weeks, although the person who tested positive was recently traveling from South Africa. So, that makes sense. But remember, the doctors taking care of these patients in South Africa are describing a less virulent, more mild infection. Right now, we're getting very distracted by Omicron, because there's no evidence that it's a real threat.\par \par \uc2 And we are still having a problem in the United States, not with Omicron -- we're having a problem with adults who have a risk factor like obesity who are not vaccinated and don't have natural immunity from prior infection. They are coming to hospital. That's where we should be focusing our efforts, not on the quick reflex that we heard from Dr. Fauci to give a booster to young people, even young people who have natural immunity. That's not our problem right now.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: He's never discussed that option that people who've had COVID, and we've seen the Israel studies that show that COVID is in even better protection than then vaccines in boosters, correct -- is that correct?\par \par \uc2 MAKARY: That's right. Look, real medical leadership would be talking about Molnupiravir, which just got an upvote from the FDA yesterday, amazing drug that cut COVID deaths to almost zero. Fluvoxamine, which he's never talked about cut COVID desk by 91 percent. It's already available. If there was real medical leadership, you'd see assurance, like the head of the \uc2 South African Medical Association\uc2 , who said, there is absolutely -- this is a direct quote, "There's absolutely no need to panic."\par \par \uc2 That's what we should be hearing from our public health leaders. And final point, we have four BSL four virology labs. Take this sample and quickly run it against the current antibodies that the vaccine produces. And in 12 hours give us the result as to whether or not this Omicron variant is encompassed by the vaccines in the immune system, instead of putting the entire world economy on hold until we get that answer.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes, there are some indications that in Israel, they've done that and have found that the current vaccines seem to be having some effectiveness early to say, but that there's some early indications that that is the case, and we certainly hope it is. Look at this quote from the Moderna's CEO Stephane Bancel, she says, "There is no world I think, where the effectiveness is the same level. All the scientists I've talked to are like, this is not going to be good." What do you make of that doctor?\par \par \uc2 MAKARY: Well, that may be good for his shareholders. But it's not consistent with what we're hearing from \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 , or \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 , or the vast majority of vaccinologist who are very confident that vaccinated immunity will encompass Omicron. So, he did really alert a lot of people and send market spiraling yesterday when he said that, but it's not consistent with everything else out there.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Thank you very much, Dr. Marty Makary. Always good to see you, Sir.\par \par \uc2 MAKARY: Thanks.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: And there's always a new development in this story. We hope that these cases will remain mild and that we have the treatments and the vaccines to cover it. Thank you so much, Doctor.\par \par \uc2 MAKARY: Thanks.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Great to see you as always. So, as we mentioned, we are waiting for an update from the Oakland County Sheriff on the investigation into yesterday's school shooting that happened about this time. The suspect now charged with terrorism and multiple counts of murder. He is in custody. We're going to bring you that news conference as soon as it gets underway.\par \par \uc2 Also, breaking this afternoon, the future of abortion rights in America now in the hands of the Supreme Court in a huge case that came before them today. Fascinating arguments. We're going to replace some of that for you coming up next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Sheriff Bouchard is now in front of the microphones. Let's listen into what he's saying about the shooting yesterday in Oxford, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MIKE BOUCHARD, OAKLAND COUNTY SHERIFF: -- deplorable tragic event that occurred by choice. And so, we appreciate her stepping up quickly. And charging this individual as an adult, which like I've said from the beginning of this, I believe is most appropriate.\par \par \uc2 You also know we put out a release sadly the 17-year-old fourth victim passed today at McLaren Hospital shortly after 10:00, as our fourth decedent today from gunshot wounds and (INAUDIBLE) senseless shooting. They already know the other three tragic victims, and thankfully we're learning more about them and then hopefully we'll honor their memory. Not just with the charges, but to talk about their life. And what amazing young people they were.\par \par \uc2 You also know seven other people were injured. I'm going to update you on their status. Six students, one teacher, four remain hospitalized. Three have not been treated and released. A 14-year-old male remains in serious condition with GSW gunshot wounds to the jaw and hand.\par \par \uc2 A 17-year-old female with neck wounds. She is at the local area of McLaren Hospital. A 14-year-old female has improved, thankfully. I would say no small part to great medical care, emergency responders, fire service, and prayers. Quite frankly, the public, she's been removed from critical to stable, with gunshot wounds to the left chest and neck. She's at Hurley Medical in Flint.\par \par \uc2 And we have a 17-year-old female that still remains in critical condition with a gunshot wound to the chest. So, still looking for prayers and support for her and her family.\par \par \uc2 The following discharge was a 15-year-old male who had a wound to the left leg, a 17-year-old male who had a hip gunshot wound, he was discharged. And a 47-year-old female teacher that had suffered a gunshot wound to her left shoulder was discharged, as you already know.\par \par \uc2 Again, the charges levied by the prosecutor were supportive of including one kind of terrorism causing death. Because very clearly, there were a lot of victims in that school other than the ones that were actually struck.\par \par \uc2 And then in addition to that, she charged four counts of first-degree murder, seven counts of assault with intent to do murder, and 12 counts of felony firearm.\par \par \uc2 Our detectives right now are in the car, on the way to District Court 52-3 for a swear to, to the facts and allegations contained in these warrants. And after those are sworn to, we anticipate that a video arraignment from Children's Village direct to the court will occur. And we are asking and joining the prosecutor to ask the judge that this individual be transferred to the Oakland County Jail from Children's Village. So, we hope that the judge rules on that as well.\par \par \uc2 I'd like to update you on some of the information. This is still evolving, right? That's a crime scene, we've still got a ton of interviews to do, video to review, documents review, search warrants that have been completed that have to be examined in terms of content, and items that were seized. So, sometimes things evolve.\par \par \uc2 When I said last night that he had seven rounds left, he actually had a pain. Seven were in his pocket that were loose. So, he added additional rounds in an actual magazine. Excuse me, so he had a total of 18 live rounds left.\par \par \uc2 We have recovered 30 spent shell casings at this point by processing the scene, meaning he fired more than 30 shots. More to the point again, I think it highlights the fact that with this much ammunition still with him, 18 live rounds, the quick actions of the school and the lockdown, as well as the deputies getting in, and going to the sound -- going to the danger, save lives.\par \par \uc2 That doesn't minimize the loss or the tragedy, but it's important that we continue to look for ways to prevent these. And if they ever tragically happen, how we can mitigate and reduce that tragedy.\par \par \uc2 The suspect we believe at this point now had three 15-round magazines. Two were initially recovered by investigators. And after a thorough forensic examination of the crime scene, which went until 5:30 this morning, another magazine was recovered.\par \par \uc2 As I mentioned, the crime scene was searched and processed until 5:30 this morning and has now been turned back to open the proceeding Oxford Schools. We're coordinating counseling and therapist efforts with care house to assist all Oxford community schools. And we also have an offer for our crisis team from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and we're grateful for that assistance.\par \par \uc2 I would remind and encourage anyone whether they were there or feel traumatized by the event. It is strength to seek help, not weakness. That trauma affects people in dramatic and sad ways. And asking people for help, seeking a therapist or a counselor or a chaplain is an important step to process such a tragedy.\par \par \uc2 Also, I want to clear up some of the incorrect information that keeps circulating. Social media keeps ginning up a great deal of false information. A video was disseminated rather while widely that showed the students\par \par \uc2 A great deal of false information. A video was disseminated rather while widely that showed the students in a classroom, and depicted someone knocking on the door. And pretty much the allegation was that, that was the suspect. We've now been able to determine that was not the suspect.\par \par \uc2 Excuse me, more than likely, it was one of our plainclothes detectives. And he may have been talking, bro, in a conversational manner to try to bring them down from the crisis to say, Come on, bro, let's get out of the classroom, let's get you outside, let's get you -- that kind of comment.\par \par \uc2 The suspect we have now confirmed by analyzing all of the video from the time it began to the time we took him into custody, never knocked on the door.\par \par \uc2 So, the other thing that we are seeing that we have heard on social media was that, again, we were notified about this threat in advance. False, the threat that we were notified in advance was one from November 11 that actually we did investigate, and it was determined to be from Georgia, not Oakland County, and had no relationship to Oxford Schools, and was cleared as such.\par \par \uc2 That is continuing to be cross populated to this event. It has nothing to do with this event. So, people are posting, I call the sheriff's office about a threat. It was a different set of circumstances that had nothing to do with this individual or the facts at hand.\par \par \uc2 There were two events that happen, fairly close proximity and timelines and locations to Oxford. Both of them had nothing to do with this. We received no information about this individual prior to the shooting.\par \par \uc2 We also were told that the school had some information or some contact with the individual. We had no information from the schools. But we have since learned that the schools did have contact with the student the day before and the day of the shooting for behavior in the classroom that they felt was concerning.\par \par \uc2 In fact, the parents were brought in the morning of the shooting and had a face-to-face meeting with the school. The content of that meeting, obviously as part of the investigation, but we did not learn of that meeting, nor of the content of that meeting until after the shooting and during this investigation.\par \par \uc2 So, please, I remind everyone, be wary of social media, and what spread because it's hurtful to the community. It's hurtful to the victims, and it spreads false sad misinformation.\par \par \uc2 If anyone has information or believes they know something about this case, or frankly, any case, for any potential threat anywhere in Oakland County, please call our phone line that we've given out before at 248-858-4911. Or you can e-mail us at OCSO, Oakland County Sheriff's Office. OCSO @oakgov.com. And of course, we always accept anonymous tips.\par \par \uc2 So, I'll try to answer questions if it doesn't get too deeply into the evidence because we're right now at the baton point where we're passing the baton from investigation, the prosecution, and we don't want to say anything that may jeopardize that further ends of the case.\par \par \uc2 Secondly, one of the victim's families has been getting a great deal of contact from the media. They don't want to talk to the media. And they're feeling bombarded in this unbelievable moment of pain. So, we would ask you to leave the family members that lost loved ones alone.\par \par \uc2 And that the father described it as wolves at the door. And they're dealing with the loss of a child. Let's not victimize them again, please.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Sheriff, on the victim who've passed today, multiple ages have been given, 17 --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: 17.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Prosecutor just said 15 and --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: 17.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: 100 percent?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: We verified that he had driver's license.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Sheriff, would you clarify that the suspect -- that the suspect was at school, and then, left, and then came back. Is that true?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: The suspect was at school and did not leave. Was brought into a meeting and then went back in, into the school area.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Sheriff, (INAUDIBLE) about the nature of the concerning behavior (INAUDIBLE) in the classroom, was it a threat? Was it violent behavior?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: I can't -- I can't get into that. Again, we're at the evidentiary handoff point. But --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: is that information that should have been relayed to this police officer or you guys?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: We always prefer to err on the side of too much rather than too little. I can't really go much beyond that. But we would rather, as I said, yesterday, check out 1,000 nothing's in this one real deal.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Is that could be investigated. Is the school going to have to potentially answer a question?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: Well, it's certainly part of our investigation. And that's where we learned about it.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Sheriff, he was in school, the face to face with his parents, and seeing the meeting with them, that opportunity?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And the parents left with the status quo.\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You know, what time in the morning that might have occurred their face to face?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: Shortly after 10:00, I believe.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: So, it was almost 10:00 and almost 1:00, right? Does the shooting was close to 1:00, right?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: Correct. 12:52 thereabouts was first call came in or was just (INAUDIBLE).\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: (INAUDIBLE) Sheriff, we're also hearing that he went into the bathroom, he loaded the gun in the bathroom before walking out to shoot. Can you confirm that?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: I can tell you, he came out of the bathroom with the firearm and began shooting. I can't tell you if he loaded it in there.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Any updates on a motive (INAUDIBLE), Sheriff.\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: No, we are obviously are not communicating with the suspect. So, we can't get that from him. We're working, you know, items that we have seized, as I talked about documents, papers, phones, evidentiary value, items to look to see if there's something that would lead to us understanding what motivate him. But I will say again, there is nothing that he could have faced that would warrant senseless, absolutely brutal violence on other kids.\par \par \uc2 And I have also asked the school if they had any records of him being bullied, and the coordinator of anti-bullying programs had no information that he had been bullied by anyone.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutor, talked about premeditation, in your estimation, but was not able to clarify whether it was pre-meditation of certain victims. Can you go there with the intent to just kill? And these people were randomly targeted? Or is there any indication they were specifically targeted?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: We have no indication that these students were specifically targeted. And based on what I seen, I don't think that's the case.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: (INAUDIBLE) the student certain discipline that was discussed (INAUDIBLE) that was decided in that meeting?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: I really don't want to get into the specifics of that meeting, because now it's part of the investigation. But I wanted to be transparent that we learned that a meeting had occurred. And we did not know about that until after the shooting.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Sir, was he ever expelled from school?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: No, he -- prior to those two meetings, there was no contact and nothing in his file by either concerning behavior or discipline.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: How much --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: From your investigation, how is the interactions with the parents?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: With the parents of the child.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Of the suspect.\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: Yes, well, they apparently hired an attorney. So, we're not talking to the child or the parents.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I understand you're saying (INAUDIBLE) we're not reporting to your office, but as we go through these -- digital evidence and the findings, how clear or specific address (INAUDIBLE) just generally (INAUDIBLE).\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: And I really don't want to get into, ultimately, what will be disclosed at a trial.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Sheriff --\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: And what we come for recover in terms of documented evidence.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And debunking social media (INAUDIBLE), can you address some of the rumors about a countdown being displayed on one of the social media accounts of the (INAUDIBLE) taken out of the day?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: That's the first I've heard of it right now. So, and again, there's so much out on social media that we've spent a lot of time investigating and finding, there was nothing to it than debunking and it's causing us a great deal of resources, and it's causing the victims more harm and more hurt.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Is there any indication that suspect had been treated for a mental health condition, or (INAUDIBLE)?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: We have no information about.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Sheriff, what was his proximity to that? Was he within if you kids walking down the hall?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: Very close.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Would very close as opposed to --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: Very close -- very close.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Sheriff, I know all of this happen between like a five minutes, is there like a timeline that you can give us as far as where the students started and the direction or aggravates?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: Again, I don't want to get too awfully specific into the actual elements. He came out of the bathroom, began shooting, move through hall hallways, and back through hallways, and was apprehended in the hallway. Never went into a room. He was in the hallway the whole time.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And I had one more question, sheriff. Did he ever spend any time in a multi-facility at all? Do you know that?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: Not that I'm aware of.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Are you aware of a shooter going to gun range in the days before the event, to train with a weapon?\par \par \uc2 BOUCHARD: We're told by different people that he had. There are some social media posts that alleged that. We have not had the ability to verify at this point, if there was a range or if that happened. And that's again, I mean, understand the scope of this. The school