cumbing to critical injuries that had occurred yesterday.\par \par \uc2 The assaults are many and the counts are many, four counts of first-degree murder, seven counts of assault with intent to murder, 12 counts of possession of a firearm. Crumbley, you might recall, was arrested in the immediate aftermath of the shooting, taken into custody.\par \par \uc2 We also had a chance to see -- his parents were part of this arraignment process. We learned through the police and then the chief police in the area that they had been with their son that morning on a school discipline issue that had come up over two days, first on Monday, and then separately meeting with some other teachers, we're told -- we assume teachers -- the very next day.\par \par \uc2 Whether they were with him on both days, it appears that they were. They were with him at this arraignment. Again, just keeping you posted on this. But all of this comes at a time we're learning that there is now apparently a massive amount of digital evidence, videotape, social media, that absolutely confirms that we can show this was a premeditated act.\par \par \uc2 This is coming from the Oakland county prosecutor, Karen McDonald, who said that this was not just an impulsive act, it was planned, it was very well- planned.\par \par \uc2 Let's go to Steve Harrigan right now following all these developments in Oxford, Michigan -- Steve.\par \par \uc2 STEVE HARRIGAN, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Neil, a lot of news coming out about this case and some remarkable images there from the courtroom, where you saw the 15-year-old sophomore in a bulletproof vest slumped over, looking very small and not powerful at all, his parents in baseball caps on a different screen at the same time.\par \par \uc2 We have learned that the 15-year-old will be charged as an adult, that he will face four charges of first-degree murder that show premeditation. Also, he will face the charge of terrorism that causes death, an unusual charge. The prosecutor