joking interviews with the governor last year when both brothers were riding high.\par \par \uc2 The question now is whether Chris Cuomo can return to CNN after such a high-profile suspension. One CNN host told viewers it's possible Cuomo be on the air next month. But a spokesperson told FOX News there is no end date, at least while the network weighs his future. Bret?\par \par \uc2 BAIER: OK, Howie, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Up next, the panel on the Omicron variant arriving in America and President Biden's reaction to all that.\par \par \uc2 First, here is what some of our FOX affiliates around the country are covering tonight. FOX 5 in New York where at least six people are injured and dozens displaced after a house explodes in Brooklyn. A massive fireball erupted from the building into the street. Two people in the home were able to escape. Investigators are still looking into the cause of that incident.\par \par \uc2 FOX 44 in Waco, Texas, as the clock is ticking for Major League Baseball and the player's union to strike a deal. The sports collective bargaining agreement expires at 11:59 p.m. eastern time tonight. The two groups appear headed to a lockout after little progress in negotiations. Major League Baseball has not had a work stoppage since 1994.\par \par \uc2 And this is a live look at Chicago from FOX 32. You may have heard the judge talk about this. One of the big stories there tonight, at least a story, the original "Home Alone" house is now available to book on \uc2 Airbnb\uc2 . The McCallister home is opening its doors to fans for one night only, December 12th, and \uc2 Buzz\uc2  McCallister, the elder brother from the 1990 film, will be hosting the stay for $25.\par \par \uc2 That's tonight's live look outside the beltway from SPECIAL REPORT. we'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: We're learning more every single day. And we will fight